window.DVA_QUIZ_BANK = [
{"id":"q1","q":"A company is implementing an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The application needs to process incoming transactions. When the application detects a transaction that is not valid, the application must send a chat message to the company's support team. To send the message, the application needs to retrieve the access token to authenticate by using the chat API. A developer needs to implement a solution to store the access token. The access token must be encrypted at rest and in transit. The access token must also be accessible from other AWS accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST management overhead?","options":["Use an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store SecureString parameter that uses an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) AWS managed key to store the access token. Add a resource-based policy to the parameter to allow access from other accounts. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances with permissions to access Parameter Store. Retrieve the token from Parameter Store with the decrypt flag enabled. Use the decrypted access token to send the message to the chat.","Encrypt the access token by using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. Store the access token in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances with permissions to access DynamoDB and AWS KMS. Retrieve the token from DynamoDB. Decrypt the token by using AWS KMS on the EC2 instances. Use the decrypted access token to send the message to the chat.","Use AWS Secrets Manager with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key to store the access token. Add a resource-based policy to the secret to allow access from other accounts. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances with permissions to access Secrets Manager. Retrieve the token from Secrets Manager. Use the decrypted access token to send the message to the chat.","Encrypt the access token by using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) AWS managed key. Store the access token in an Amazon S3 bucket. Add a bucket policy to the S3 bucket to allow access from other accounts. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances with permissions to access Amazon S3 and AWS KMS. Retrieve the token from the S3 bucket. Decrypt the token by using AWS KMS on the EC2 instances. Use the decrypted access token to send the message to the chat."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **AWS Secrets Manager - Purpose-built for secrets management**:\n - Được thiết kế riêng để lưu trữ và quản lý các secret (access tokens, API keys, credentials)\n - Tích hợp native với AWS KMS để mã hóa at rest\n - Automatic encryption in transit khi sử dụng AWS SDK\n\n2. **Cross-account access capabilities**:\n - Hỗ trợ resource-based policies cho phép access từ các AWS accounts khác\n - Dễ dàng cấu hình mà không cần complex IAM role setup\n\n3. **Least management overhead**:\n - Automatic rotation giảm operational overhead\n - Native integration với EC2 instances thông qua IAM roles\n - AWS SDK hỗ trợ sẵn việc retrieve và decrypt secrets\n\n4. **Security benefits**:\n - Centralized secrets management\n - Audit trail thông qua AWS CloudTrail\n - Fine-grained access control thông qua IAM policies\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Parameter Store tuy có SecureString nhưng không có automatic rotation và ít feature-rich hơn Secrets Manager\n- **B, D:** DynamoDB và S3 không phải dịch vụ chuyên dụng cho secret management, yêu cầu manual encryption/decryption và không có automatic rotation\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần lưu trữ secrets với yêu cầu cross-account access và minimal management → AWS Secrets Manager là lựa chọn tối ưu."},
{"id":"q2","q":"A company is running Amazon EC2 instances in multiple AWS accounts. A developer needs to implement an application that collects all the lifecycle events of the EC2 instances. The application needs to store the lifecycle events in a single Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue in the company's main AWS account for further processing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure Amazon EC2 to deliver the EC2 instance lifecycle events from all accounts to the Amazon EventBridge event bus of the main account. Add an EventBridge rule to the event bus of the main account that matches all EC2 instance lifecycle events. Add the SQS queue as a target of the rule.","Use the resource policies of the SQS queue in the main account to give each account permissions to write to that SQS queue. Add to the Amazon EventBridge event bus of each account an EventBridge rule that matches all EC2 instance lifecycle events. Add the SQS queue in the main account as a target of the rule.","Write an AWS Lambda function that scans through all EC2 instances in the company accounts to detect EC2 instance lifecycle changes. Configure the Lambda function to write a notification message to the SQS queue in the main account if the function detects an EC2 instance lifecycle change. Add an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function every minute.","Configure the permissions on the main account event bus to receive events from all accounts. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in each account to send all the EC2 instance lifecycle events to the main account event bus. Add an EventBridge rule to the main account event bus that matches all EC2 instance lifecycle events. Set the SQS queue as a target for the rule."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Centralized Event Collection**:\n - Cấu hình quyền trên event bus của tài khoản chính để nhận sự kiện từ tất cả các tài khoản\n - Cho phép tập trung sự kiện vào một nơi duy nhất\n\n2. **Distributed Rule Configuration**:\n - Tạo EventBridge rule trong mỗi tài khoản để gửi sự kiện vòng đời EC2 đến event bus chính\n - Đảm bảo tất cả sự kiện được chuyển tiếp từ mọi account\n\n3. **Centralized Processing**:\n - Thêm EventBridge rule trên event bus chính để lọc sự kiện vòng đời EC2\n - Đặt SQS queue làm target cho rule để xử lý tập trung\n\n4. **Best Practice Architecture**:\n - Tuân thủ mô hình cross-account event collection của AWS\n - Dễ dàng mở rộng khi có thêm tài khoản mới\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Không thể cấu hình EC2 trực tiếp gửi sự kiện đến event bus của tài khoản khác\n- **B:** Quản lý resource policies của SQS phức tạp và không scalable khi số lượng account tăng\n- **C:** Giải pháp polling không hiệu quả, có thể bỏ lỡ sự kiện và tạo ra overhead không cần thiết\n\n**Tips:** Để thu thập sự kiện từ multiple accounts → sử dụng EventBridge cross-account event bus kết hợp với rules ở mỗi account."},
{"id":"q3","q":"An application is using Amazon Cognito user pools and identity pools for secure access. A developer wants to integrate the user-specific file upload and download features in the application with Amazon S3. The developer must ensure that the files are saved and retrieved in a secure manner and that users can access only their own files. The file sizes range from 3 KB to 300 MB. Which option will meet these requirements with the HIGHEST level of security?","options":["Use S3 Event Notifications to validate the file upload and download requests and update the user interface (UI).","Save the details of the uploaded files in a separate Amazon DynamoDB table. Filter the list of files in the user interface (UI) by comparing the current user ID with the user ID associated with the file in the table.","Use Amazon API Gateway and an AWS Lambda function to upload and download files. Validate each request in the Lambda function before performing the requested operation.","Use an IAM policy within the Amazon Cognito identity prefix to restrict users to use their own folders in Amazon S3."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Fine-Grained IAM Security**:\n - Sử dụng Cognito Identity Pools để cấp temporary AWS credentials cho users\n - IAM policy hạn chế users chỉ được truy cập vào folder S3 của chính họ\n - Security được enforce ở infrastructure level\n\n2. **Direct S3 Access**:\n - Users upload/download trực tiếp đến S3 mà không qua intermediary service\n - Hiệu quả với file lớn (lên đến 300 MB) - tránh Lambda timeout và API Gateway payload limits\n - Không có performance bottleneck\n\n3. **Cognito Integration**:\n - Tận dụng built-in authentication của Cognito User Pools\n - Identity Pools map users đến IAM roles với permissions phù hợp\n - Automatic credential rotation và security token management\n\n4. **Zero-Trust Security Model**:\n - Mỗi user chỉ có quyền truy cập vào prefix S3 của riêng họ\n - Không thể truy cập hoặc thấy files của users khác\n - Encryption at rest và in transit được đảm bảo bởi S3 và IAM\n\nSai:\n- **A:** S3 Event Notifications không dùng để validate requests, chỉ để trigger downstream processing\n- **B:** Security through UI filtering không an toàn - users có thể bypass UI và access trực tiếp\n- **C:** Mặc dù an toàn nhưng không hiệu quả với file lớn và tạo ra unnecessary complexity\n\n**Tips:** Để user-specific file access với S3 → sử dụng Cognito Identity Pools với IAM policies restricting access to user-specific prefixes."},
{"id":"q4","q":"A company is building a scalable data management solution by using AWS services to improve the speed and agility of development. The solution will ingest large volumes of data from various sources and will process this data through multiple business rules and transformations. The solution requires business rules to run in sequence and to handle reprocessing of data if errors occur when the business rules run. The company needs the solution to be scalable and to require the least possible maintenance. Which AWS service should the company use to manage and automate the orchestration of the data flows to meet these requirements?","options":["AWS Batch","AWS Step Functions","AWS Glue","AWS Lambda"],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Workflow Orchestration**:\n - Step Functions được thiết kế đặc biệt để orchestrate complex workflows\n - Cho phép định nghĩa business rules chạy tuần tự theo state machine\n - Visual workflow giúp dễ dàng design và monitor\n\n2. **Error Handling and Retry Logic**:\n - Built-in error handling với retry policies (exponential backoff, max attempts)\n - Catch branches để xử lý reprocessing khi business rules fail\n - Custom error handling cho different exception types\n\n3. **Scalability and Serverless**:\n - Automatic scaling để handle large volumes of data\n - Serverless - no infrastructure management, least maintenance\n - Pay-per-use pricing model\n\n4. **Service Integration**:\n - Native integration với multiple AWS services (Lambda, Batch, Glue, etc.)\n - Có thể kết hợp các services khác trong workflow\n - Support both synchronous và asynchronous execution\n\n5. **State Management**:\n - Duy trì state giữa các execution steps\n - Input/output transformation giữa các business rules\n - Context object truyền data qua lại giữa các states\n\nSai:\n- **A:** AWS Batch tốt cho batch computing nhưng không phải workflow orchestration\n- **C:** AWS Glue tập trung vào ETL, không phải general workflow orchestration\n- **D:** AWS Lambda tốt cho compute nhưng không có built-in state management và complex error handling\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần orchestrate workflows với sequential steps và error handling → AWS Step Functions là lựa chọn tối ưu."},
{"id":"q5","q":"A developer has created an AWS Lambda function that is written in Python. The Lambda function reads data from objects in Amazon S3 and writes data to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The function is successfully invoked from an S3 event notification when an object is created. However, the function fails when it attempts to write to the DynamoDB table. What is the MOST likely cause of this issue?","options":["The Lambda function's concurrency limit has been exceeded.","DynamoDB table requires a global secondary index (GSI) to support writes.","The Lambda function does not have IAM permissions to write to DynamoDB.","The DynamoDB table is not running in the same Availability Zone as the Lambda function."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **IAM Permissions Analysis**:\n - Lambda function được invoke thành công bởi S3 event → có quyền đọc từ S3\n - Lỗi xảy ra cụ thể khi write to DynamoDB → thiếu quyền ghi\n - Nguyên tắc least privilege: Lambda role cần explicit permissions cho mỗi service\n\n2. **Required DynamoDB Permissions**:\n - Để write to DynamoDB, Lambda cần permissions như: `dynamodb:PutItem`, `dynamodb:UpdateItem`, etc.\n - Thiếu các permissions này sẽ gây ra `AccessDeniedException`\n\n3. **Common Configuration Issue**:\n - Đây là lỗi phổ biến khi setup Lambda functions\n - Dễ bỏ sót khi chỉ tập trung vào trigger permissions mà quên execution permissions\n - CloudWatch Logs sẽ hiển thị access denied errors\n\n4. **Troubleshooting Steps**:\n - Kiểm tra IAM role attached to Lambda function\n - Verify DynamoDB permissions trong IAM policy\n - Check CloudWatch Logs cho specific error messages\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Concurrency limit exceeded sẽ gây lỗi invocation, không phải lỗi during execution\n- **B:** GSI không required cho basic write operations, chỉ cho querying\n- **D:** DynamoDB là regional service, không phụ thuộc vào Availability Zone\n\n**Tips:** Khi Lambda thực thi thành công nhưng fail khi access AWS service → kiểm tra IAM permissions đầu tiên."},
{"id":"q6","q":"A developer is creating an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy Amazon EC2 instances across multiple AWS accounts. The developer must choose the EC2 instances from a list of approved instance types. How can the developer incorporate the list of approved instance types in the CloudFormation template?","options":["Create a separate CloudFormation template for each EC2 instance type in the list.","In the Resources section of the CloudFormation template, create resources for each EC2 instance type in the list.","In the CloudFormation template, create a separate parameter for each EC2 instance type in the list.","In the CloudFormation template, create a parameter with the list of EC2 instance types as AllowedValues."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Parameter with AllowedValues**:\n - Tạo single parameter với danh sách approved instance types làm AllowedValues\n - CloudFormation tự động validate input against allowed values\n - Ngăn chặn deployment với instance types không được approve\n\n2. **Template Reusability**:\n - Một template có thể dùng cho multiple accounts và use cases\n - Users chọn instance type phù hợp từ dropdown list\n - Dễ dàng maintain và update approved list\n\n3. **Best Practice Implementation**:\n - Tuân thủ CloudFormation best practices cho parameter design\n - Cung cấp documentation thông qua Parameter descriptions\n - Có thể set default value từ approved list\n\n4. **Example Configuration**:\n```yaml\nParameters:\n InstanceType:\n Type: String\n AllowedValues:\n - t3.micro\n - t3.small\n - t3.medium\n - m5.large\n Description: Select from approved EC2 instance types\n Default: t3.micro\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Tạo multiple templates không scalable và khó maintain\n- **B:** Tạo resources cho mỗi type sẽ deploy nhiều instances không cần thiết\n- **C:** Multiple parameters làm phức tạp hóa template và user experience\n\n**Tips:** Để enforce approved values trong CloudFormation → sử dụng Parameters với AllowedValues."},
{"id":"q7","q":"A developer has an application that makes batch requests directly to Amazon DynamoDB by using the BatchGetItem low-level API operation. The responses frequently return values in the UnprocessedKeys element. Which actions should the developer take to increase the resiliency of the application when the batch response includes values in UnprocessedKeys? (Choose two.)","options":["Retry the batch operation immediately.","Retry the batch operation with exponential backoff and randomized delay.","Update the application to use an AWS software development kit (AWS SDK) to make the requests.","Increase the provisioned read capacity of the DynamoDB tables that the operation accesses.","Increase the provisioned write capacity of the DynamoDB tables that the operation accesses."],"correct":[1,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án B và D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Exponential Backoff Retry Strategy (B)**:\n - UnprocessedKeys thường do temporary capacity issues\n - Exponential backoff giảm tải cho DynamoDB bằng cách tăng dần thời gian chờ giữa các lần retry\n - Randomized delay tránh thundering herd problem\n - AWS best practice cho resilient distributed systems\n\n2. **Increase Read Capacity (D)**:\n - BatchGetItem là read operation → cần read capacity units (RCUs)\n - UnprocessedKeys thường xảy ra khi vượt quá provisioned read capacity\n - Tăng read capacity giải quyết root cause của vấn đề\n - Có thể sử dụng auto-scaling để tự động điều chỉnh capacity\n\n3. **Understanding UnprocessedKeys**:\n - Xuất hiện khi: vượt quá throughput, item size quá lớn, internal errors\n - Application nên implement retry logic cho UnprocessedKeys\n - SDKs thường có built-in retries nhưng custom implementation cho phép fine-tuning\n\n4. **Complete Resiliency Pattern**:\n - Retry với exponential backoff xử lý temporary issues\n - Tăng capacity xử lý sustained throughput requirements\n - Kết hợp cả hai giải pháp cho comprehensive resiliency\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Retry immediately có thể làm trầm trọng thêm vấn đề throughput\n- **C:** AWS SDKs đã có retry logic, nhưng custom implementation cho phép optimization tốt hơn\n- **E:** BatchGetItem là read operation, không liên quan đến write capacity\n\n**Tips:** Xử lý DynamoDB UnprocessedKeys → kết hợp retry với exponential backoff và điều chỉnh provisioned capacity."},
{"id":"q8","q":"A company is running a custom application on a set of on-premises Linux servers that are accessed using Amazon API Gateway. AWS X-Ray tracing has been enabled on the API test stage. How can a developer enable X-Ray tracing on the on-premises servers with the LEAST amount of configuration?","options":["Install and run the X-Ray SDK on the on-premises servers to capture and relay the data to the X-Ray service.","Install and run the X-Ray daemon on the on-premises servers to capture and relay the data to the X-Ray service.","Capture incoming requests on-premises and configure an AWS Lambda function to pull, process, and relay relevant data to X-Ray using the PutTraceSegments API call.","Capture incoming requests on-premises and configure an AWS Lambda function to pull, process, and relay relevant data to X-Ray using the PutTelemetryRecords API call."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **X-Ray Daemon Simplicity**:\n - X-Ray daemon là lightweight application dễ cài đặt và cấu hình\n - Tự động thu thập và gửi trace data đến X-Ray service\n - Không yêu cầu thay đổi application code\n\n2. **Least Configuration Required**:\n - Download daemon binary và run với minimal configuration\n - Cấu hình IAM credentials để daemon có quyền gửi data đến X-Ray\n - Daemon tự động xử lý buffering, batching, và retries\n\n3. **On-Premises Integration**:\n - Daemon chạy như background process trên Linux servers\n - Có thể giao tiếp qua HTTP/HTTPS từ on-premises đến AWS\n - Hỗ trợ multiple programming languages và frameworks\n\n4. **End-to-End Tracing**:\n - Kết hợp với API Gateway X-Ray tracing để có full distributed trace\n - Theo dõi request từ API Gateway qua on-premises application\n - Identifies performance bottlenecks across hybrid architecture\n\n5. **Installation Steps**:\n```bash\n# Download and install X-Ray daemon\nwget https://s3.aws.amazon.com/xray-daemon/aws-xray-daemon-linux-3.x.zip\nunzip aws-xray-daemon-linux-3.x.zip\n# Run daemon với appropriate IAM credentials\n./xray -o -n us-east-1\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** X-Ray SDK yêu cầu code changes và instrumentation\n- **C, D:** Lambda solutions phức tạp, yêu cầu additional components và configuration\n\n**Tips:** Để enable X-Ray tracing trên on-premises servers với ít config nhất → sử dụng X-Ray daemon."},
{"id":"q9","q":"A company wants to share information with a third party. The third party has an HTTP API endpoint that the company can use to share the information. The company has the required API key to access the HTTP API. The company needs a way to manage the API key by using code. The integration of the API key with the application code cannot affect application performance. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST securely?","options":["Store the API credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. Retrieve the API credentials at runtime by using the AWS SDK. Use the credentials to make the API call.","Store the API credentials in a local code variable. Push the code to a secure Git repository. Use the local code variable at runtime to make the API call.","Store the API credentials as an object in a private Amazon S3 bucket. Restrict access to the S3 object by using IAM policies. Retrieve the API credentials at runtime by using the AWS SDK. Use the credentials to make the API call.","Store the API credentials in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Restrict access to the table by using resource-based policies. Retrieve the API credentials at runtime by using the AWS SDK. Use the credentials to make the API call."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Purpose-Built Secret Management**:\n - AWS Secrets Manager được thiết kế specifically cho secret storage\n - Automatic encryption at rest using AWS KMS\n - Built-in rotation capabilities giảm operational overhead\n\n2. **Security Best Practices**:\n - Fine-grained access control through IAM policies\n - Audit trail through AWS CloudTrail integration\n - No secret exposure in code, environment variables, or repositories\n\n3. **Performance Optimization**:\n - SDK caching giảm số lần call đến Secrets Manager\n - Client-side caching của retrieved secrets\n - Không ảnh hưởng đến application performance\n\n4. **Runtime Retrieval Pattern**:\n```python\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef get_secret():\n secret_name = \"third-party-api-key\"\n region_name = \"us-east-1\"\n \n session = boto3.session.Session()\n client = session.client(service_name='secretsmanager', region_name=region_name)\n \n try:\n get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=secret_name)\n except ClientError as e:\n # Handle error\n raise e\n else:\n secret = get_secret_value_response['SecretString']\n return secret\n```\n\n5. **Enterprise Features**:\n - Cross-account access capabilities\n - Version tracking của secrets\n - Integration với AWS security services\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Lưu secret trong code là extremely insecure practice\n- **C:** S3 không được thiết kế cho secret management, thiếu rotation và auditing\n- **D:** DynamoDB không phải secret management service, requires manual encryption\n\n**Tips:** Để quản lý API keys và credentials một cách secure → sử dụng AWS Secrets Manager với runtime retrieval."},
{"id":"q10","q":"A developer is deploying a new application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The developer needs to securely store and retrieve different types of variables. These variables include authentication information for a remote API, the URL for the API, and credentials. The authentication information and API URL must be available to all current and future deployed versions of the application across development, testing, and production environments. How should the developer retrieve the variables with the FEWEST application changes?","options":["Update the application to retrieve the variables from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Use unique paths in Parameter Store for each variable in each environment. Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager in each environment.","Update the application to retrieve the variables from AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Store the API URL and credentials as unique keys for each environment.","Update the application to retrieve the variables from an encrypted file that is stored with the application. Store the API URL and credentials in unique files for each environment.","Update the application to retrieve the variables from each of the deployed environments. Define the authentication information and API URL in the ECS task definition as unique names during the deployment process."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Centralized Configuration Management**:\n - Systems Manager Parameter Store cung cấp centralized storage cho configuration data\n - Hỗ trợ cả plaintext và SecureString parameters\n - Dễ dàng quản lý values cho multiple environments\n\n2. **Secure Credential Storage**:\n - AWS Secrets Manager được thiết kế riêng cho sensitive data như credentials\n - Automatic rotation và encryption tại rest\n - Integration với ECS qua environment variables\n\n3. **Environment-Specific Configuration**:\n - Sử dụng paths như `/dev/api/url`, `/prod/api/url` cho từng environment\n - Application chỉ cần thay đổi path prefix cho mỗi environment\n - Không cần thay đổi code khi thêm environment mới\n\n4. **Least Application Changes**:\n - Application chỉ cần implement logic retrieve từ Parameter Store/Secrets Manager một lần\n - Không cần rebuild/redeploy khi thay đổi configuration values\n - Hỗ trợ dynamic configuration updates\n\nSai:\n- **B:** AWS KMS không phải service để lưu trữ configuration data\n- **C:** Encrypted files khó quản lý version và không centralized\n- **D:** Hardcoding trong task definition không scalable và khó maintain\n\n**Tips:** Để quản lý configuration across multiple environments → sử dụng Systems Manager Parameter Store kết hợp với Secrets Manager."},
{"id":"q11","q":"A company is migrating legacy internal applications to AWS. Leadership wants to rewrite the internal employee directory to use native AWS services. A developer needs to create a solution for storing employee contact details and high-resolution photos for use with the new application. Which solution will enable the search and retrieval of each employee's individual details and high-resolution photos using AWS APIs?","options":["Encode each employee's contact information and photos using Base64. Store the information in an Amazon DynamoDB table using a sort key.","Store each employee's contact information in an Amazon DynamoDB table along with the object keys for the photos stored in Amazon S3.","Use Amazon Cognito user pools to implement the employee directory in a fully managed software-as-a-service (SaaS) method.","Store employee contact information in an Amazon RDS DB instance with the photos stored in Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Optimal Data Storage Strategy**:\n - DynamoDB: Lý tưởng cho structured data (contact details) với fast query capabilities\n - Amazon S3: Tối ưu cho unstructured data (high-resolution photos) với cost-effective storage\n\n2. **Efficient Data Retrieval**:\n - Store S3 object keys trong DynamoDB để tạo liên kết hiệu quả\n - Fast lookup của contact information qua DynamoDB queries\n - Direct access đến photos qua S3 URLs\n\n3. **AWS API Integration**:\n - DynamoDB cung cấp SDKs cho search và retrieval operations\n - S3 cung cấp APIs cho image serving và management\n - Cả hai services đều hỗ trợ fine-grained access control\n\n4. **Scalability and Performance**:\n - DynamoDB auto-scaling cho growing employee data\n - S3 hỗ trợ high-throughput cho image access\n - Low-latency retrieval cho cả text và binary data\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Base64 encoding images trong DynamoDB không hiệu quả và tốn kém\n- **C:** Cognito User Pools không designed cho employee directory data storage\n- **D:** RDS + EFS phức tạp hơn cần thiết và không tối ưu cho use case này\n\n**Tips:** Để lưu trữ metadata + files/images → sử dụng DynamoDB cho metadata và S3 cho files, với object references trong DynamoDB."},
{"id":"q12","q":"A company receives food orders from multiple partners. The company has a microservices application that uses Amazon API Gateway APIs with AWS Lambda integration. Each partner sends orders by calling a customized API that is exposed through API Gateway. The API call invokes a shared Lambda function to process the orders. Partners need to be notified after the Lambda function processes the orders. Each partner must receive updates for only the partner's own orders. The company wants to add new partners in the future with the fewest code changes possible. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST scalable way?","options":["Create a different Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic for each partner. Configure the Lambda function to publish messages for each partner to the partner's SNS topic.","Create a different Lambda function for each partner. Configure the Lambda function to notify each partner's service endpoint directly.","Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure the Lambda function to publish messages with specific attributes to the SNS topic. Subscribe each partner to the SNS topic. Apply the appropriate filter policy to the topic subscriptions.","Create one Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe all partners to the SNS topic."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Single Topic Architecture**:\n - Một SNS topic duy nhất cho tất cả partners\n - Lambda function publishes messages với message attributes (ví dụ: partnerId)\n - Simplified management và reduced operational overhead\n\n2. **Message Filtering**:\n - Mỗi partner subscription có filter policy dựa trên message attributes\n - Partners chỉ nhận messages có attribute values phù hợp với họ\n - Fine-grained control over message delivery\n\n3. **Scalability and Flexibility**:\n - Dễ dàng thêm partners mới bằng cách tạo subscription với filter policy\n - Không cần thay đổi Lambda function code khi thêm partners\n - SNS tự động handle message routing và delivery\n\n4. **Cost Efficiency**:\n - Single topic reduces management complexity\n - Pay-per-use pricing model của SNS\n - No unused resources cho inactive partners\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Multiple SNS topics khó quản lý và không scalable\n- **B:** Multiple Lambda functions tạo ra code duplication và maintenance overhead\n- **D:** Single topic without filtering sẽ gửi all messages đến all partners\n\n**Tips:** Để publish-notify pattern với selective messaging → sử dụng SNS topic với message attributes và subscription filter policies."},
{"id":"q13","q":"A financial company must store original customer records for 10 years for legal reasons. A complete record contains personally identifiable information (PII). According to local regulations, PII is available to only certain people in the company and must not be shared with third parties. The company needs to make the records available to third-party organizations for statistical analysis without sharing the PII. A developer wants to store the original immutable record in Amazon S3. Depending on who accesses the S3 document, the document should be returned as is or with all the PII removed. The developer has written an AWS Lambda function to remove the PII from the document. The function is named removePii. What should the developer do so that the company can meet the PII requirements while maintaining only one copy of the document?","options":["Set up an S3 event notification that invokes the removePii function when an S3 GET request is made. Call Amazon S3 by using a GET request to access the object without PII.","Set up an S3 event notification that invokes the removePii function when an S3 PUT request is made. Call Amazon S3 by using a PUT request to access the object without PII.","Create an S3 Object Lambda access point from the S3 console. Select the removePii function. Use S3 Access Points to access the object without PII.","Create an S3 access point from the S3 console. Use the access point name to call the GetObjectLegalHold S3 API function. Pass in the removePii function name to access the object without PII."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **S3 Object Lambda Architecture**:\n - S3 Object Lambda cho phép modify data returned bởi S3 GET requests\n - Sử dụng Lambda function để dynamically process data during retrieval\n - Maintain single copy của original document trong S3\n\n2. **Dynamic PII Removal**:\n - removePii function được invoke khi third parties access documents\n - Internal users với appropriate permissions có thể access original documents\n - PII removal happens on-the-fly based trên requester identity\n\n3. **Immutable Storage Compliance**:\n - Original records được giữ nguyên trong S3\n - No modification đến stored objects - compliance với legal requirements\n - Object versioning có thể được enable cho additional protection\n\n4. **Access Control Integration**:\n - S3 Object Lambda Access Points tích hợp với IAM policies\n - Different access points cho internal vs external access\n - Fine-grained control over who sees PII vs anonymized data\n\nSai:\n- **A:** S3 event notifications không trigger trên GET requests\n- **B:** S3 event notifications trên PUT sẽ modify stored object, vi phạm immutability requirement\n- **D:** GetObjectLegalHold không liên quan đến PII removal\n\n**Tips:** Để dynamic content modification based trên requester → sử dụng S3 Object Lambda với Lambda functions."},
{"id":"q14","q":"A developer is deploying an AWS Lambda function The developer wants the ability to return to older versions of the function quickly and seamlessly. How can the developer achieve this goal with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Use AWS OpsWorks to perform blue/green deployments.","Use a function alias with different versions.","Maintain deployment packages for older versions in Amazon S3.","Use AWS CodePipeline for deployments and rollbacks."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Versioning and Aliases**:\n - Lambda tự động maintains all published versions của function\n - Aliases là pointers đến specific function versions\n - Quick rollback bằng cách update alias pointer đến previous version\n\n2. **Seamless Version Switching**:\n - Alias update là instantaneous operation\n - No downtime hoặc service disruption\n - Clients continue to use same alias ARN\n\n3. **Least Operational Overhead**:\n - Built-in Lambda feature - no additional services required\n - Simple API calls để publish versions và update aliases\n - No infrastructure management hoặc complex deployment pipelines\n\n4. **Traffic Routing**:\n - Aliases có thể được used trong API Gateway integrations\n - Easy A/B testing và canary deployments\n - Version history được maintained automatically\n\nSai:\n- **A:** OpsWorks introduces unnecessary complexity cho Lambda deployments\n- **C:** Manual S3 package management tăng operational overhead\n- **D:** CodePipeline là overkill cho simple version rollbacks\n\n**Tips:** Để quick rollbacks và version management cho Lambda → sử dụng Lambda Versions và Aliases."},
{"id":"q15","q":"A developer has written an AWS Lambda function. The function is CPU-bound. The developer wants to ensure that the function returns responses quickly. How can the developer improve the function's performance?","options":["Increase the function's CPU core count.","Increase the function's memory.","Increase the function's reserved concurrency.","Increase the function's timeout."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda CPU-Memory Relationship**:\n - AWS Lambda allocates CPU power proportional to memory configured\n - Tăng memory đồng thời tăng CPU capacity available cho function\n - Direct performance improvement cho CPU-bound workloads\n\n2. **CPU-Bound Workload Optimization**:\n - CPU-bound functions benefit trực tiếp từ increased computational power\n - Faster execution times lead to quicker response times\n - Cost-per-request có thể giảm do reduced execution duration\n\n3. **Practical Performance Tuning**:\n - Experiment với different memory settings để find optimal configuration\n - Monitor CloudWatch metrics để measure performance improvements\n - Balance giữa performance và cost efficiency\n\n4. **Easy Configuration**:\n - Memory configuration là simple parameter update\n - No code changes required\n - Có thể được adjusted through console, CLI, hoặc infrastructure-as-code\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Lambda không cho phép direct CPU core configuration\n- **C:** Reserved concurrency affects parallel execution, không phải individual execution performance\n- **D:** Timeout increase allows longer execution, nhưng không improve performance\n\n**Tips:** Để improve Lambda performance cho CPU-intensive tasks → tăng memory allocation để tăng proportional CPU power."},
{"id":"q16","q":"For a deployment using AWS Code Deploy, what is the run order of the hooks for in-place deployments?","options":["BeforeInstall -> ApplicationStop -> ApplicationStart -> AfterInstall","ApplicationStop -> BeforeInstall -> AfterInstall -> ApplicationStart","BeforeInstall -> ApplicationStop -> ValidateService -> ApplicationStart","ApplicationStop -> BeforeInstall -> ValidateService -> ApplicationStart"],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CodeDeploy Hook Execution Order**:\n - ApplicationStop: Dừng application hiện tại\n - BeforeInstall: Tasks trước khi install new version\n - AfterInstall: Tasks sau khi install new version\n - ApplicationStart: Khởi động application mới\n\n2. **In-Place Deployment Logic**:\n - Stop current application trước\n - Prepare environment và install new version\n - Execute post-installation tasks\n - Start application với new version\n\n3. **Official Documentation Reference**:\n - AWS CodeDeploy documentation specifies this exact order\n - Ensures proper sequencing cho successful deployments\n - Validated through AWS testing và customer use cases\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Sai thứ tự - ApplicationStop phải đến trước BeforeInstall\n- **C:** ValidateService không phải standard hook và sai thứ tự\n- **D:** ValidateService không phải standard hook\n\n**Tips:** Nhớ CodeDeploy hook order: Stop → Before → After → Start cho in-place deployments."},
{"id":"q17","q":"A company is building a serverless application on AWS. The application uses an AWS Lambda function to process customer orders 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. The Lambda function calls an external vendor's HTTP API to process payments. During load tests, a developer discovers that the external vendor payment processing API occasionally times out and returns errors. The company expects that some payment processing API calls will return errors. The company wants the support team to receive notifications in near real time only when the payment processing external API error rate exceed 5% of the total number of transactions in an hour. Developers need to use an existing Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that is configured to notify the support team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Write the results of payment processing API calls to Amazon CloudWatch. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the CloudWatch logs. Schedule the Lambda function to check the CloudWatch logs and notify the existing SNS topic.","Publish custom metrics to CloudWatch that record the failures of the external payment processing API calls. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to notify the existing SNS topic when error rate exceeds the specified rate.","Publish the results of the external payment processing API calls to a new Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the support team members to the new SNS topic.","Write the results of the external payment processing API calls to Amazon S3. Schedule an Amazon Athena query to run at regular intervals. Configure Athena to send notifications to the existing SNS topic when the error rate exceeds the specified rate."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudWatch Custom Metrics**:\n - Lambda function publishes success/failure metrics cho mỗi API call\n - Custom metrics capture error rate accurately\n - Real-time metric collection và aggregation\n\n2. **CloudWatch Alarms**:\n - Configurable thresholds (5% error rate)\n - Statistical period (1 hour)\n - Direct integration với existing SNS topic\n - Near real-time notifications\n\n3. **Serverless Monitoring Pattern**:\n - No additional infrastructure required\n - Automatic scaling với transaction volume\n - Cost-effective monitoring solution\n\n4. **Precise Error Rate Calculation**:\n - CloudWatch tự động calculates percentages dựa trên metric data\n - Alarm triggers only when threshold breached\n - Supports complex expressions và multi-metric alarms\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Log analysis introduces delay và không near real-time\n- **C:** New SNS topic không tính error rate và sends all notifications\n- **D:** S3 + Athena solution có high latency và complexity\n\n**Tips:** Để real-time error rate monitoring → sử dụng CloudWatch Custom Metrics và Alarms với SNS integration."},
{"id":"q18","q":"A company is offering APIs as a service over the internet to provide unauthenticated read access to statistical information that is updated daily. The company uses Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda to develop the APIs. The service has become popular, and the company wants to enhance the responsiveness of the APIs. Which action can help the company achieve this goal?","options":["Enable API caching in API Gateway.","Configure API Gateway to use an interface VPC endpoint.","Enable cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) for the APIs.","Configure usage plans and API keys in API Gateway."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **API Gateway Caching Benefits**:\n - Lưu trữ responses từ backend services (Lambda)\n - Giảm latency bằng cách serve cached responses\n - Giảm load trên Lambda functions và downstream services\n\n2. **Ideal Use Case Fit**:\n - Statistical information updated daily - perfect cho caching\n - Unauthenticated read access - no user-specific data\n - Public APIs - high cache hit ratio expected\n\n3. **Performance Optimization**:\n - Response times improved từ milliseconds đến microseconds\n - Có thể configure cache TTL based trên data update frequency\n - Support cho different cache sizes based trên traffic patterns\n\n4. **Cost Reduction**:\n - Fewer Lambda invocations reduce compute costs\n - Efficient resource utilization\n - Better user experience với faster responses\n\nSai:\n- **B:** VPC endpoints cho private access, không improve public API performance\n- **C:** CORS cho browser security, không improve API responsiveness\n- **D:** Usage plans cho rate limiting, không improve performance\n\n**Tips:** Để improve performance của read-heavy, infrequently-changing data → enable API Gateway caching."},
{"id":"q19","q":"A developer wants to store information about movies. Each movie has a title, release year, and genre. The movie information also can include additional properties about the cast and production crew. This additional information is inconsistent across movies. For example, one movie might have an assistant director, and another movie might have an animal trainer. The developer needs to implement a solution to support the following use cases: For a given title and release year, get all details about the movie that has that title and release year. For a given title, get all details about all movies that have that title. For a given genre, get all details about all movies in that genre. Which data store configuration will meet these requirements?","options":["Create an Amazon DynamoDB table. Configure the table with a primary key that consists of the title as the partition key and the release year as the sort key. Create a global secondary index that uses the genre as the partition key and the title as the sort key.","Create an Amazon DynamoDB table. Configure the table with a primary key that consists of the genre as the partition key and the release year as the sort key. Create a global secondary index that uses the title as the partition key.","On an Amazon RDS DB instance, create a table that contains columns for title, release year, and genre. Configure the title as the primary key.","On an Amazon RDS DB instance, create a table where the primary key is the title and all other data is encoded into JSON format as one additional column."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **DynamoDB Schema Design**:\n - Primary Key: title (partition) + release year (sort) - supports query by title and year\n - Allows efficient retrieval của specific movie\n - Supports query by title alone (using begins_with trên sort key)\n\n2. **Global Secondary Index for Genre Queries**:\n - GSI: genre (partition) + title (sort)\n - Enables efficient queries by genre\n - Supports sorting movies by title within each genre\n\n3. **Flexible Data Model**:\n - DynamoDB supports flexible, schemaless data\n - Additional properties (cast, crew) stored như attributes không cần predefined schema\n - No migration needed khi adding new attribute types\n\n4. **Query Pattern Support**:\n - Use case 1: Query trên primary key với title và release year\n - Use case 2: Query trên primary key với title và filter/sort key\n - Use case 3: Query trên GSI với genre\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Schema không hỗ trợ efficient query bằng title và release year\n- **C:** RDS fixed schema không phù hợp cho inconsistent additional properties\n- **D:** RDS với JSON column không tối ưu cho complex query patterns\n\n**Tips:** Để flexible schema với multiple query patterns → DynamoDB với appropriate primary key và GSIs."},
{"id":"q20","q":"A developer maintains an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Customers use the API through a frontend UI and Amazon Cognito authentication. The developer has a new version of the API that contains new endpoints and backward-incompatible interface changes. The developer needs to provide beta access to other developers on the team without affecting customers. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Define a development stage on the API Gateway API. Instruct the other developers to point the endpoints to the development stage.","Define a new API Gateway API that points to the new API application code. Instruct the other developers to point the endpoints to the new API.","Implement a query parameter in the API application code that determines which code version to call.","Specify new API Gateway endpoints for the API endpoints that the developer wants to add."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **API Gateway Stages**:\n - Stages provide isolated deployments của cùng API\n - Development stage có thể host beta version\n - Production stage continues to serve customers uninterrupted\n\n2. **Least Operational Overhead**:\n - No new APIs cần được created\n - Simple stage configuration through console hoặc infrastructure-as-code\n - Developers use same API với different stage name trong URL\n\n3. **Isolation and Security**:\n - Stages có thể có separate throttling limits và caching settings\n - Cognito authentication works across all stages\n - Easy to manage permissions và monitoring per stage\n\n4. **URL Structure**:\n - Production: `https://api-id.execute-api.region.amazonaws.com/prod/resource`\n - Development: `https://api-id.execute-api.region.amazonaws.com/dev/resource`\n - Developers chỉ cần change stage name trong requests\n\nSai:\n- **B:** New API creation introduces additional management overhead\n- **C:** Query parameter approach requires code changes và complicates logic\n- **D:** Adding new endpoints không giải quyết backward-incompatible changes\n\n**Tips:** Để beta testing và version isolation → sử dụng API Gateway Stages cho separate deployment environments."},
{"id":"q21","q":"A developer is creating an application that will store personal health information (PHI). The PHI needs to be encrypted at all times. An encrypted Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance is storing the data. The developer wants to increase the performance of the application by caching frequently accessed data while adding the ability to sort or rank the cached datasets. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis instance. Enable encryption of data in transit and at rest. Store frequently accessed data in the cache.","Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached instance. Enable encryption of data in transit and at rest. Store frequently accessed data in the cache.","Create an Amazon RDS for MySQL read replica. Connect to the read replica by using SSL. Configure the read replica to store frequently accessed data.","Create an Amazon DynamoDB table and a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster for the table. Store frequently accessed data in the DynamoDB table."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **ElastiCache for Redis với Encryption**:\n - Hỗ trợ encryption in-transit (TLS) và at-rest\n - Đáp ứng yêu cầu bảo mật cho PHI data\n - Redis clusters có thể được configured với encryption enabled\n\n2. **Sorting và Ranking Capabilities**:\n - Redis cung cấp native sorted sets cho ranking operations\n - Hỗ trợ các operations như ZADD, ZRANGE, ZREVRANK\n - Efficient sorting của cached datasets\n\n3. **High Performance Caching**:\n - Sub-millisecond latency cho cached data access\n - Reduce load trên RDS database\n - Improve application responsiveness\n\n4. **PHI Compliance**:\n - Encryption features đáp ứng healthcare compliance requirements\n - Secure data handling throughout caching lifecycle\n - Integration với AWS KMS cho key management\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Memcached không hỗ trợ encryption at-rest và thiếu advanced data structures cho sorting\n- **C:** Read replicas không phải caching solution và không improve performance significantly\n- **D:** DynamoDB + DAX không cung cấp native sorting capabilities như Redis sorted sets\n\n**Tips:** Để caching với sorting/ranking capabilities và encryption → ElastiCache for Redis."},
{"id":"q22","q":"A company has a multi-node Windows legacy application that runs on premises. The application uses a network shared folder as a centralized configuration repository to store configuration files in .xml format. The company is migrating the application to Amazon EC2 instances. As part of the migration to AWS, a developer must identify a solution that provides high availability for the repository. Which solution will meet this requirement MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Mount an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume onto one of the EC2 instances. Deploy a file system on the EBS volume. Use the host operating system to share a folder. Update the application code to read and write configuration files from the shared folder.","Deploy a micro EC2 instance with an instance store volume. Use the host operating system to share a folder. Update the application code to read and write configuration files from the shared folder.","Create an Amazon S3 bucket to host the repository. Migrate the existing .xml files to the S3 bucket. Update the application code to use the AWS SDK to read and write configuration files from Amazon S3.","Create an Amazon S3 bucket to host the repository. Migrate the existing .xml files to the S3 bucket. Mount the S3 bucket to the EC2 instances as a local volume. Update the application code to read and write configuration files from the disk."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Amazon S3 High Availability**:\n - S3 cung cấp 99.999999999% (11 9's) durability\n - 99.99% availability across multiple AZs\n - No single point of failure\n\n2. **Cost-Effectiveness**:\n - Pay-per-use pricing với no upfront costs\n - No compute resources required for file serving\n - Cheaper than maintaining dedicated file servers\n\n3. **Simplified Management**:\n - Fully managed service - no OS patching or maintenance\n - Automatic scaling với traffic patterns\n - Built-in versioning và lifecycle policies\n\n4. **Application Integration**:\n - AWS SDKs cung cấp simple APIs cho file operations\n - Support cho XML file format\n - Consistent performance across all EC2 instances\n\nSai:\n- **A:** EBS volumes are AZ-bound và attached to single instance - no high availability\n- **B:** Instance store volumes are ephemeral và not persistent\n- **D:** Mounting S3 as local volume không phải best practice và có performance issues\n\n**Tips:** Để highly available file storage → sử dụng Amazon S3 với AWS SDK integration."},
{"id":"q23","q":"A company wants to deploy and maintain static websites on AWS. Each website's source code is hosted in one of several version control systems, including AWS CodeCommit, Bitbucket, and GitHub. The company wants to implement phased releases by using development, staging, user acceptance testing, and production environments in the AWS Cloud. Deployments to each environment must be started by code merges on the relevant Git branch. The company wants to use HTTPS for all data exchange. The company needs a solution that does not require servers to run continuously. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Host each website by using AWS Amplify with a serverless backend. Connect the repository branches that correspond to each of the desired environments. Start deployments by merging code changes to a desired branch.","Host each website in AWS Elastic Beanstalk with multiple environments. Use the EB CLI to link each repository branch. Integrate AWS CodePipeline to automate deployments from version control code merges.","Host each website in different Amazon S3 buckets for each environment. Configure AWS CodePipeline to pull source code from version control. Add an AWS CodeBuild stage to copy source code to Amazon S3.","Host each website on its own Amazon EC2 instance. Write a custom deployment script to bundle each website's static assets. Copy the assets to Amazon EC2. Set up a workflow to run the script when code is merged."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **AWS Amplify - Fully Managed Service**:\n - Serverless architecture - no servers to manage\n - Automatic deployments triggered by Git branch merges\n - Built-in support for multiple environments (dev, staging, prod)\n\n2. **Multi-Repository Support**:\n - Native integration với AWS CodeCommit, Bitbucket, và GitHub\n - Automatic build và deploy on code changes\n - Branch-based environment mapping\n\n3. **HTTPS and Security**:\n - Automatic SSL certificate provisioning\n - Global CDN distribution với CloudFront\n - DDoS protection và security headers\n\n4. **Least Operational Overhead**:\n - No infrastructure management\n - Automatic scaling với traffic\n - Built-in monitoring và analytics\n\n5. **Phased Release Support**:\n - Branch-based environment segregation\n - Easy promotion between environments\n - Support for preview deployments\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Elastic Beanstalk requires EC2 instances - không serverless\n- **C:** Multiple services (S3, CodePipeline, CodeBuild) increase operational complexity\n- **D:** EC2 instances require ongoing management và không cost-effective\n\n**Tips:** Để static websites với automated deployments từ Git → AWS Amplify."},
{"id":"q24","q":"A company is migrating an on-premises database to Amazon RDS for MySQL. The company has read-heavy workloads. The company wants to refactor the code to achieve optimum read performance for queries. Which solution will meet this requirement with LEAST current and future effort?","options":["Use a multi-AZ Amazon RDS deployment. Increase the number of connections that the code makes to the database or increase the connection pool size if a connection pool is in use.","Use a multi-AZ Amazon RDS deployment. Modify the code so that queries access the secondary RDS instance.","Deploy Amazon RDS with one or more read replicas. Modify the application code so that queries use the URL for the read replicas.","Use open source replication software to create a copy of the MySQL database on an Amazon EC2 instance. Modify the application code so that queries use the IP address of the EC2 instance."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **RDS Read Replicas Purpose-Built for Read Scaling**:\n - Được thiết kế specifically cho read-heavy workloads\n - Asynchronous replication từ primary instance\n - Multiple read replicas có thể được added để scale read capacity\n\n2. **Least Effort Implementation**:\n - Read replicas được managed hoàn toàn bởi AWS\n - Application chỉ cần modified để use read replica endpoint\n - No complex replication setup hoặc maintenance\n\n3. **Optimal Read Performance**:\n - Offload read queries từ primary instance\n - Reduce contention trên primary database\n - Improve overall application performance\n\n4. **Future Scalability**:\n - Dễ dàng add more read replicas khi read load increases\n - Automatic backup và patching\n - Cross-region read replicas cho geographic distribution\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Multi-AZ cho high availability, không improve read performance\n- **B:** Secondary instance trong Multi-AZ không available cho read traffic\n- **D:** Self-managed replication trên EC2 requires significant effort và expertise\n\n**Tips:** Để scale read performance → sử dụng RDS Read Replicas."},
{"id":"q25","q":"A developer is creating an application that will be deployed on IoT devices. The application will send data to a RESTful API that is deployed as an AWS Lambda function. The application will assign each API request a unique identifier. The volume of API requests from the application can randomly increase at any given time of day. During periods of request throttling, the application might need to retry requests. The API must be able to handle duplicate requests without inconsistencies or data loss. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. Store the unique identifier for each request in a database table. Modify the Lambda function to check the table for the identifier before processing the request.","Create an Amazon DynamoDB table. Store the unique identifier for each request in the table. Modify the Lambda function to check the table for the identifier before processing the request.","Create an Amazon DynamoDB table. Store the unique identifier for each request in the table. Modify the Lambda function to return a client error response when the function receives a duplicate request.","Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached instance. Store the unique identifier for each request in the cache. Modify the Lambda function to check the cache for the identifier before processing the request."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **DynamoDB for IoT Scale and Performance**:\n - Automatic scaling để handle random traffic spikes\n - Single-digit millisecond latency cho IoT workloads\n - Pay-per-request pricing cho cost efficiency\n\n2. **Idempotency Pattern Implementation**:\n - Store request IDs trong DynamoDB để track processed requests\n - Lambda function checks for existing request ID before processing\n - Prevent duplicate processing mà không gây data inconsistencies\n\n3. **Serverless Architecture**:\n - DynamoDB integrates seamlessly với Lambda functions\n - No provisioning hoặc capacity planning required\n - Automatic handling của traffic patterns\n\n4. **Durability and Reliability**:\n - DynamoDB cung cấp high durability\n - Persistent storage cho request history\n - Conditional writes để prevent race conditions\n\nSai:\n- **A:** RDS không scale automatically và có higher latency\n- **C:** Returning errors cho duplicates không đáp ứng requirement \"handle without data loss\"\n- **D:** Memcached không persistent và có thể mất data\n\n**Tips:** Để idempotent API với high scalability → sử dụng DynamoDB để track request IDs."},
{"id":"q26","q":"A developer wants to expand an application to run in multiple AWS Regions. The developer wants to copy Amazon Machine Images (AMIs) with the latest changes and create a new application stack in the destination Region. According to company requirements, all AMIs must be encrypted in all Regions. However, not all the AMIs that the company uses are encrypted. How can the developer expand the application to run in the destination Region while meeting the encryption requirement?","options":["Create new AMIs, and specify encryption parameters. Copy the encrypted AMIs to the destination Region. Delete the unencrypted AMIs.","Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to enable encryption on the unencrypted AMIs. Copy the encrypted AMIs to the destination Region.","Use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to enable encryption on the unencrypted AMIs. Copy the encrypted AMIs to the destination Region.","Copy the unencrypted AMIs to the destination Region. Enable encryption by default in the destination Region."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **AMI Encryption Process**:\n - Create new AMIs từ existing instances với encryption enabled\n - Specify encryption parameters during AMI creation\n - Use AWS KMS keys để encrypt AMI data\n\n2. **Cross-Region AMI Copy**:\n - Copy encrypted AMIs đến destination regions\n - Shared KMS keys hoặc create new keys trong destination regions\n - Maintain encryption throughout the process\n\n3. **Compliance Enforcement**:\n - Ensure all AMIs meet encryption requirements\n - Phase out unencrypted AMIs\n - Establish encryption-as-default policy\n\n4. **Step-by-Step Approach**:\n - Launch instance từ unencrypted AMI\n - Create new encrypted AMI từ running instance\n - Copy encrypted AMI đến target regions\n - Update automation scripts để use encrypted AMIs\n\nSai:\n- **B:** KMS cannot directly encrypt existing unencrypted AMIs\n- **C:** ACM is for SSL/TLS certificates, not AMI encryption\n- **D:** Encryption by default doesn't apply to existing unencrypted AMIs\n\n**Tips:** Để migrate AMIs across regions với encryption → create new encrypted AMIs và copy them."},
{"id":"q27","q":"A company hosts a client-side web application for one of its subsidiaries on Amazon S3. The web application can be accessed through Amazon CloudFront from https://www.example.com. After a successful rollout, the company wants to host three more client-side web applications for its remaining subsidiaries on three separate S3 buckets. To achieve this goal, a developer moves all the common JavaScript files and web fonts to a central S3 bucket that serves the web applications. However, during testing, the developer notices that the browser blocks the JavaScript files and web fonts. What should the developer do to prevent the browser from blocking the JavaScript files and web fonts?","options":["Create four access points that allow access to the central S3 bucket. Assign an access point to each web application bucket.","Create a bucket policy that allows access to the central S3 bucket. Attach the bucket policy to the central S3 bucket","Create a cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) configuration that allows access to the central S3 bucket. Add the CORS configuration to the central S3 bucket.","Create a Content-MD5 header that provides a message integrity check for the central S3 bucket. Insert the Content-MD5 header for each web application request."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CORS Configuration for Cross-Origin Requests**:\n - Browser blocks resources từ different origins due to same-origin policy\n - CORS configuration cho phép cross-origin resource sharing\n - S3 bucket cần configured để allow requests từ web application domains\n\n2. **S3 CORS Configuration**:\n - Configure CORS trên central S3 bucket\n - Specify allowed origins (web application domains)\n - Define allowed methods (GET, HEAD) và headers\n\n3. **Example CORS Configuration**:\n```xml\n<CORSConfiguration>\n <CORSRule>\n <AllowedOrigin>https://www.example.com</AllowedOrigin>\n <AllowedOrigin>https://app2.example.com</AllowedOrigin>\n <AllowedMethod>GET</AllowedMethod>\n <AllowedMethod>HEAD</AllowedMethod>\n <MaxAgeSeconds>3000</MaxAgeSeconds>\n <AllowedHeader>*</AllowedHeader>\n </CORSRule>\n</CORSConfiguration>\n```\n\n4. **Browser Security Compliance**:\n - CORS headers được included trong responses\n - Browser allows resource loading từ cross-origin\n - Maintains security while enabling resource sharing\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Access points solve access control, not CORS issues\n- **B:** Bucket policies control access, not CORS headers\n- **D:** Content-MD5 is for data integrity, not CORS\n\n**Tips:** Để resources từ different domains → configure CORS trên S3 bucket."},
{"id":"q28","q":"An application is processing clickstream data using Amazon Kinesis. The clickstream data feed into Kinesis experiences periodic spikes. The PutRecords API call occasionally fails and the logs show that the failed call returns the response with ProvisionedThroughputExceededException. Which techniques will help mitigate this exception? (Choose two.)","options":["Implement retries with exponential backoff.","Use a PutRecord API instead of PutRecords.","Reduce the frequency and/or size of the requests.","Use Amazon SNS instead of Kinesis.","Reduce the number of KCL consumers."],"correct":[0,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **A. Implement retries with exponential backoff**:\n - ProvisionedThroughputExceededException thường là temporary\n - Exponential backoff giúp giảm tải cho Kinesis trong spikes\n - Cho phép hệ thống tự phục hồi mà không mất data\n\n2. **C. Reduce the frequency and/or size of the requests**:\n - Giảm trực tiếp throughput pressure lên Kinesis stream\n - Smaller batches hoặc less frequent requests giúp stay within provisioned limits\n - Đặc biệt hiệu quả trong periods of high traffic\n\nSai:\n- **B:** PutRecord (single record) thay vì PutRecords (batch) có thể làm tăng số lượng requests và làm vấn đề tồi tệ hơn\n- **D:** Thay đổi sang SNS là architectural change lớn, không giải quyết vấn đề Kinesis throughput\n- **E:** KCL consumers liên quan đến reading data, không liên quan đến PutRecords (writing data)\n\n**Tips:** Khi gặp ProvisionedThroughputExceededException trong Kinesis → retry với exponential backoff và điều chỉnh request pattern là giải pháp hiệu quả nhất."},
{"id":"q29","q":"A developer has an application that stores data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application uses an HTTP API to store and retrieve objects. When the PutObject API operation adds objects to the S3 bucket the developer must encrypt these objects at rest by using server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). Which solution will meet this requirement?","options":["Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. Assign the KMS key to the S3 bucket.","Set the x-amz-server-side-encryption header when invoking the PutObject API operation.","Provide the encryption key in the HTTP header of every request.","Apply TLS to encrypt the traffic to the S3 bucket."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **SSE-S3 Implementation**:\n - x-amz-server-side-encryption header specifies encryption type\n - Value \"AES256\" enables SSE-S3 encryption\n - S3 automatically encrypts object với S3-managed keys\n\n2. **API-Level Encryption Control**:\n - Header must be included trong mỗi PutObject request\n - Ensures individual objects are encrypted at rest\n - No bucket-level configuration required\n\n3. **SSE-S3 vs Other Options**:\n - SSE-S3: S3-managed keys, no additional charge\n - SSE-KMS: KMS-managed keys, additional charges\n - SSE-C: Customer-provided keys\n\n4. **Request Example**:\n```http\nPUT /object-key HTTP/1.1\nHost: bucket-name.s3.amazonaws.com\nx-amz-server-side-encryption: AES256\nContent-Length: content-length\n\n[object content]\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** KMS key configuration enables SSE-KMS, not SSE-S3\n- **C:** SSE-C requires customer-provided keys, not S3-managed\n- **D:** TLS encrypts data in transit, not at rest\n\n**Tips:** Để SSE-S3 encryption → set x-amz-server-side-encryption: AES256 header trong PutObject requests."},
{"id":"q30","q":"A developer needs to perform geographic load testing of an API. The developer must deploy resources to multiple AWS Regions to support the load testing of the API. How can the developer meet these requirements without additional application code?","options":["Create and deploy an AWS Lambda function in each desired Region. Configure the Lambda function to create a stack from an AWS CloudFormation template in that Region when the function is invoked.","Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the load test resources. Use the AWS CLI create-stack-set command to create a stack set in the desired Regions.","Create an AWS Systems Manager document that defines the resources. Use the document to create the resources in the desired Regions.","Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the load test resources. Use the AWS CLI deploy command to create a stack from the template in each Region."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudFormation Stack Sets**:\n - Stack sets enable deployment đến multiple accounts và regions\n - Single template deployed across multiple regions\n - Centralized management và updates\n\n2. **No Additional Application Code**:\n - Infrastructure defined declaratively trong template\n - AWS handles cross-region deployment logic\n - No custom code required cho deployment orchestration\n\n3. **Geographic Load Testing Support**:\n - Deploy identical resources across multiple regions\n - Consistent configuration cho accurate testing\n - Easy cleanup after testing completion\n\n4. **Automated Deployment**:\n```bash\naws cloudformation create-stack-set \\\n --stack-set-name load-test-stackset \\\n --template-body file://template.yaml \\\n --parameters ParameterKey=Param1,ParameterValue=Value1\n\naws cloudformation create-stack-instances \\\n --stack-set-name load-test-stackset \\\n --regions us-east-1 us-west-2 eu-west-1 \\\n --accounts 123456789012\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Requires custom Lambda code cho deployment orchestration\n- **C:** Systems Manager documents not optimized cho multi-region resource deployment\n- **D:** Manual deployment đến each region increases effort và potential errors\n\n**Tips:** Để deploy identical resources across multiple regions → sử dụng CloudFormation Stack Sets."},
{"id":"q31","q":"A developer is creating an application that includes an Amazon API Gateway REST API in the us-east-2 Region. The developer wants to use Amazon CloudFront and a custom domain name for the API. The developer has acquired an SSL/TLS certificate for the domain from a third-party provider. How should the developer configure the custom domain for the application?","options":["Import the SSL/TLS certificate into AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) in the same Region as the API. Create a DNS A record for the custom domain.","Import the SSL/TLS certificate into CloudFront. Create a DNS CNAME record for the custom domain.","Import the SSL/TLS certificate into AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) in the same Region as the API. Create a DNS CNAME record for the custom domain.","Import the SSL/TLS certificate into AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) in the us-east-1 Region. Create a DNS CNAME record for the custom domain."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudFront Certificate Requirement**:\n - CloudFront yêu cầu SSL/TLS certificates phải được stored trong us-east-1 Region\n - This is a hard requirement của AWS CloudFront service\n - Certificates từ other regions không thể được used với CloudFront\n\n2. **ACM Certificate Import**:\n - Third-party certificates có thể được imported vào ACM\n - ACM provides managed certificate renewal và management\n - Integration với CloudFront là seamless\n\n3. **DNS Configuration**:\n - CNAME records are used để point custom domains đến CloudFront distributions\n - CloudFront provides distribution domain name cho CNAME configuration\n - A records are not typically used directly với CloudFront\n\n4. **Complete Architecture**:\n - Custom domain → CloudFront distribution → API Gateway (us-east-2)\n - End-to-end HTTPS encryption\n - Global content delivery với low latency\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Certificate must be in us-east-1 for CloudFront, not same region as API\n- **B:** Cannot import certificates directly into CloudFront\n- **C:** Certificate region must be us-east-1, not API region\n\n**Tips:** Để custom domain với CloudFront → import certificate vào ACM in us-east-1 và use CNAME records."},
{"id":"q32","q":"A company has deployed infrastructure on AWS. A development team wants to create an AWS Lambda function that will retrieve data from an Amazon Aurora database. The Amazon Aurora database is in a private subnet in company's VPC. The VPC is named VPC1. The data is relational in nature. The Lambda function needs to access the data securely. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create the Lambda function. Configure VPC1 access for the function. Attach a security group named SG1 to both the Lambda function and the database. Configure the security group inbound and outbound rules to allow TCP traffic on Port 3306.","Create and launch a Lambda function in a new public subnet that is in a new VPC named VPC2. Create a peering connection between VPC1 and VPC2.","Create the Lambda function. Configure VPC1 access for the function. Assign a security group named SG1 to the Lambda function. Assign a second security group named SG2 to the database. Add an inbound rule to SG1 to allow TCP traffic from Port 3306.","Export the data from the Aurora database to Amazon S3. Create and launch a Lambda function in VPC1. Configure the Lambda function query the data from Amazon S3."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **VPC Configuration for Lambda**:\n - Lambda functions cần được configured với VPC access để reach resources trong private subnets\n - Function được deployed trong same VPC (VPC1) như database\n - Lambda ENIs được created trong specified subnets\n\n2. **Security Group Best Practices**:\n - Same security group cho cả Lambda và database simplifies configuration\n - Inbound rules trên database security group allow traffic từ Lambda\n - Outbound rules trên Lambda security group allow traffic đến database\n - Port 3306 là default port cho Aurora MySQL\n\n3. **Secure Communication**:\n - All traffic stays within VPC\n - No exposure đến public internet\n - Security groups provide instance-level firewall\n\n4. **Network Architecture**:\n - Lambda trong private subnets (recommended) hoặc dedicated subnets\n - Aurora trong private subnets cho maximum security\n - Route tables configured cho proper routing\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Unnecessarily complex với VPC peering và public subnet\n- **C:** Security group rules are incorrect - should allow from Lambda SG to database\n- **D:** Exporting to S3 changes data access pattern và không necessary\n\n**Tips:** Để Lambda access RDS/Aurora trong VPC → configure Lambda VPC settings và proper security groups."},
{"id":"q33","q":"A developer is building a web application that uses Amazon API Gateway to expose an AWS Lambda function to process requests from clients. During testing, the developer notices that the API Gateway times out even though the Lambda function finishes under the set time limit. Which of the following API Gateway metrics in Amazon CloudWatch can help the developer troubleshoot the issue? (Choose two.)","options":["CacheHitCount","IntegrationLatency","CacheMissCount","Latency","Count"],"correct":[1,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án B và D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **IntegrationLatency (B)**:\n - Measures time between API Gateway forwarding request đến backend và receiving response\n - High integration latency indicates issues với Lambda function execution\n - Includes Lambda invocation time, execution time, và response time\n - Critical cho identifying backend performance issues\n\n2. **Latency (D)**:\n - Measures end-to-end latency từ khi API Gateway receives request đến khi sends response\n - Includes integration latency + API Gateway processing time\n - Helps identify if timeout is due to backend hoặc API Gateway itself\n - Compare với IntegrationLatency để isolate issue location\n\n3. **Troubleshooting Approach**:\n - Check IntegrationLatency: Nếu high, issue is với Lambda function\n - Check Latency: Nếu high but IntegrationLatency normal, issue is với API Gateway\n - Compare both metrics để identify root cause\n\n4. **Timeout Analysis**:\n - API Gateway timeout (max 29 seconds) vs Lambda timeout (max 15 minutes)\n - IntegrationLatency should be less than API Gateway timeout setting\n - Monitor for patterns trong latency spikes\n\nSai:\n- **A, C:** Cache metrics unrelated to timeout issues\n- **E:** Count metrics show request volume, not performance characteristics\n\n**Tips:** Để troubleshoot API Gateway timeout → monitor IntegrationLatency và Latency metrics."},
{"id":"q34","q":"A developer is designing a serverless application with two AWS Lambda functions to process photos. One Lambda function stores objects in an Amazon S3 bucket and stores the associated metadata in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The other Lambda function fetches the objects from the S3 bucket by using the metadata from the DynamoDB table. Both Lambda functions use the same Python library to perform complex computations and are approaching the quota for the maximum size of zipped deployment packages. What should the developer do to reduce the size of the Lambda deployment packages with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Package each Python library in its own .zip file archive. Deploy each Lambda function with its own copy of the library.","Create a Lambda layer with the required Python library. Use the Lambda layer in both Lambda functions.","Combine the two Lambda functions into one Lambda function. Deploy the Lambda function as a single .zip file archive.","Download the Python library to an S3 bucket. Program the Lambda functions to reference the object URLs."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Layers Benefits**:\n - Layers allow sharing common code và dependencies across multiple functions\n - Library được stored once trong layer, not duplicated trong each function\n - Significant reduction trong deployment package size\n - Easy updates - change layer version, all functions automatically updated\n\n2. **Operational Efficiency**:\n - Single layer management cho both functions\n - No code changes required - functions reference layer\n - Version control cho layer updates\n - Rollback capabilities với layer versions\n\n3. **Deployment Package Optimization**:\n - Each function package contains only unique business logic\n - Common dependencies moved to shared layer\n - Stay within 50MB zipped / 250MB unzipped limits\n\n4. **Implementation Steps**:\n - Create layer với Python library\n - Publish layer version\n - Attach layer to both Lambda functions\n - Update function configuration\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Duplicates library, increases package size, và maintenance overhead\n- **C:** Combines unrelated functions, violates single responsibility principle\n- **D:** Downloading from S3 during execution increases latency và complexity\n\n**Tips:** Để share dependencies across Lambda functions → sử dụng Lambda Layers."},
{"id":"q35","q":"A developer is writing an AWS Lambda function. The developer wants to log key events that occur while the Lambda function runs. The developer wants to include a unique identifier to associate the events with a specific function invocation. The developer adds the following code to the Lambda function: function handler(event, context) { } Which solution will meet this requirement?","options":["Obtain the request identifier from the AWS request ID field in the context object. Configure the application to write logs to standard output.","Obtain the request identifier from the AWS request ID field in the event object. Configure the application to write logs to a file.","Obtain the request identifier from the AWS request ID field in the event object. Configure the application to write logs to standard output.","Obtain the request identifier from the AWS request ID field in the context object. Configure the application to write logs to a file."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Context Object Contains Invocation Metadata**:\n - context.aws_request_id provides unique identifier cho each invocation\n - This ID is consistent throughout the invocation lifecycle\n - Available trong context object, not event object\n\n2. **Standard Output for Lambda Logging**:\n - Lambda automatically captures stdout và stderr\n - Logs are sent to Amazon CloudWatch Logs\n - No additional configuration required\n - Best practice cho Lambda logging\n\n3. **Logging Implementation**:\n```javascript\nfunction handler(event, context) {\n const requestId = context.aws_request_id;\n console.log(`[${requestId}] Processing started`);\n // Business logic\n console.log(`[${requestId}] Processing completed`);\n}\n```\n\n4. **CloudWatch Logs Integration**:\n - Each log stream contains logs từ specific function\n - Request ID helps correlate logs across distributed systems\n - Enables debugging và monitoring\n\nSai:\n- **B, C:** Request ID is in context object, not event object\n- **B, D:** Writing to files is not recommended - Lambda has ephemeral storage\n\n**Tips:** Để Lambda logging với request correlation → use context.aws_request_id và console.log()."},
{"id":"q36","q":"A company runs an ecommerce application on AWS. The application stores data in an Amazon Aurora database. A developer is adding a caching layer to the application. The caching strategy must ensure that the application always uses the most recent value for each data item. Which caching strategy will meet these requirements?","options":["Implement a TTL strategy for every item that is saved in the cache.","Implement a write-through strategy for every item that is created and updated.","Implement a lazy loading strategy for every item that is loaded.","Implement a read-through strategy for every item that is loaded."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Write-Through Caching Strategy**:\n - Data được written to both cache và database simultaneously\n - Cache always contains the most recent data\n - No stale data issues\n - Strong consistency guarantee\n\n2. **Data Consistency**:\n - Every write operation updates cache immediately\n - Read operations always get latest data từ cache\n - No need to invalidate cache entries\n - Perfect for financial/ecommerce data\n\n3. **Implementation Pattern**:\n - Application writes to cache first\n - Cache synchronously writes to database\n - Write operation completes only when both succeed\n - Read operations served từ cache\n\n4. **Use Case Fit**:\n - Ecommerce applications require real-time inventory, pricing\n - User sessions, shopping carts need immediate consistency\n - Order processing cannot tolerate stale data\n\nSai:\n- **A:** TTL strategy may serve stale data between expiration và refresh\n- **C:** Lazy loading only updates cache on cache misses\n- **D:** Read-through doesn't handle write consistency\n\n**Tips:** Để strong consistency trong caching → sử dụng write-through strategy."},
{"id":"q37","q":"A developer has written the following IAM policy to provide access to an Amazon S3 bucket:\n\n```json\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": [\n \"s3:GetObject\",\n \"s3:PutObject\"\n ],\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/*\"\n },\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n \"Action\": \"s3:*\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets*\"\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nWhich access does the policy allow regarding the s3:GetObject and s3:PutObject actions?","options":["Access on all buckets except the \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\" bucket","Access on all buckets that start with \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\" except the \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets\" bucket","Access on all objects in the \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\" bucket along with access to all S3 actions for objects in the \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\" bucket that start with \"secrets\"","Access on all objects in the \"DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\" bucket except on objects that start with \"secrets\""],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Policy structure analysis**:\n - Statement 1: Cho phép s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên tất cả objects trong bucket DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\n - Statement 2: Từ chối TẤT CẢ s3 actions (s3:*) trên objects có prefix 'secrets' trong bucket DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\n\n2. **IAM evaluation logic**:\n - Trong IAM, Deny statements luôn override Allow statements\n - User được phép GetObject/PutObject trên hầu hết objects trong bucket\n - Nhưng bị DENY hoàn toàn đối với objects bắt đầu bằng 'secrets'\n\n3. **Effective permissions**:\n - ✅ ĐƯỢC PHÉP: s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/normal-file.txt\n - ✅ ĐƯỢC PHÉP: s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/data/file.pdf\n - ❌ BỊ TỪ CHỐI: s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets/password.txt\n - ❌ BỊ TỪ CHỐI: s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets-config.json\n\n4. **Wildcard pattern**:\n - 'secrets*' pattern match mọi object key bắt đầu với 'secrets'\n - Bao gồm: secrets/, secrets/file.txt, secrets123, secrets-config, etc.\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Policy chỉ áp dụng cho DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET, không phải 'all buckets except'\n- **B:** Policy không đề cập đến buckets khác có prefix DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\n- **C:** Deny statement ngăn chặn HOÀN TOÀN mọi access đến objects với prefix 'secrets'\n\n**Tips:** Trong IAM policy evaluation: Explicit DENY → Explicit ALLOW → Default DENY. Policy này tạo ra pattern 'allow-all-except-specific-prefix'."},
{"id":"q38","q":"A developer is creating a mobile app that calls a backend service by using an Amazon API Gateway REST API. For integration testing during the development phase, the developer wants to simulate different backend responses without invoking the backend service. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Create an AWS Lambda function. Use API Gateway proxy integration to return constant HTTP responses.","Create an Amazon EC2 instance that serves the backend REST API by using an AWS CloudFormation template.","Customize the API Gateway stage to select a response type based on the request.","Use a request mapping template to select the mock integration response."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **API Gateway Mock Integration - Zero operational overhead**:\n - Built-in feature của API Gateway, không cần deploy thêm services\n - Không có cost phát sinh cho mock responses\n - Dễ dàng configure trong API Gateway console\n\n2. **Request mapping templates cho flexible responses**:\n - Có thể define different responses based on request parameters/headers\n - Simulate various HTTP status codes, headers, và body content\n - Không cần viết code hoặc manage infrastructure\n\n3. **Development testing friendly**:\n - Perfect cho integration testing phase\n - Không invoke real backend services\n - Có thể simulate errors, delays, different data scenarios\n\n4. **Quick setup và teardown**:\n - Có thể enable/disable mock integration dễ dàng\n - Không ảnh hưởng đến production configuration\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Lambda function tạo operational overhead (coding, deployment, monitoring, cost)\n- **B:** EC2 instance có highest operational overhead (server management, scaling, cost)\n- **C:** API Gateway stages không cung cấp direct mock response selection capability\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần simulate API responses cho testing → API Gateway Mock Integration với mapping templates là giải pháp đơn giản và hiệu quả nhất."},
{"id":"q39","q":"An Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream is receiving customer data that contains personally identifiable information. A developer needs to remove pattern-based customer identifiers from the data and store the modified data in an Amazon S3 bucket. What should the developer do to meet these requirements?","options":["Implement Kinesis Data Firehose data transformation as an AWS Lambda function. Configure the function to remove the customer identifiers. Set an Amazon S3 bucket as the destination of the delivery stream.","Launch an Amazon EC2 instance. Set the EC2 instance as the destination of the delivery stream. Run an application on the EC2 instance to remove the customer identifiers. Store the transformed data in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create an Amazon OpenSearch Service instance. Set the OpenSearch Service instance as the destination of the delivery stream. Use search and replace to remove the customer identifiers. Export the data to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to remove the customer identifiers. As the last step in the workflow, store the transformed data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Set the workflow as the destination of the delivery stream."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Kinesis Data Firehose Data Transformation**:\n - Native feature cho real-time data processing\n - Lambda function được invoked cho mỗi batch of records\n - Function can modify, filter, hoặc enrich data\n - Seamless integration với Firehose delivery stream\n\n2. **PII Removal Process**:\n - Lambda function scans records cho pattern-based identifiers\n - Removes hoặc masks sensitive information\n - Can use regular expressions cho pattern matching\n - Returns transformed records to Firehose\n\n3. **Serverless Architecture**:\n - No infrastructure management\n - Automatic scaling với data volume\n - Pay-per-use pricing model\n - High availability và durability\n\n4. **End-to-End Flow**:\n - Data source → Kinesis Data Firehose → Lambda transformation → S3\n - Buffering và batching handled automatically\n - Error handling với retry mechanisms\n\nSai:\n- **B:** EC2 instance requires management và doesn't scale automatically\n- **C:** OpenSearch Service is for search, not real-time data transformation\n- **D:** Step Functions cannot be direct destination cho Firehose\n\n**Tips:** Để real-time data transformation trong Kinesis Firehose → sử dụng Lambda data transformation."},
{"id":"q40","q":"A developer is using an AWS Lambda function to generate avatars for profile pictures that are uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. The Lambda function is automatically invoked for profile pictures that are saved under the /original/ S3 prefix. The developer notices that some pictures cause the Lambda function to time out. The developer wants to implement a fallback mechanism by using another Lambda function that resizes the profile picture. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","options":["Set the image resize Lambda function as a destination of the avatar generator Lambda function for the events that fail processing.","Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Set the SQS queue as a destination with an on failure condition for the avatar generator Lambda function. Configure the image resize Lambda function to poll from the SQS queue.","Create an AWS Step Functions state machine that invokes the avatar generator Lambda function and uses the image resize Lambda function as a fallback. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches events from the S3 bucket to invoke the state machine.","Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Set the SNS topic as a destination with an on failure condition for the avatar generator Lambda function. Subscribe the image resize Lambda function to the SNS topic."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Destinations - Least development effort**:\n - Built-in feature của Lambda, không cần viết thêm code\n - Có thể configure trực tiếp trong Lambda console hoặc qua Infrastructure-as-Code\n - Hỗ trợ asynchronous invocation và failure handling\n\n2. **Direct Lambda-to-Lambda integration**:\n - Không cần intermediate services (SQS, SNS, Step Functions)\n - Không cần configure polling, subscriptions, hoặc state machines\n - Minimal operational overhead\n\n3. **Automatic failure routing**:\n - Lambda tự động route failed events (bao gồm timeouts) đến destination\n - Destination Lambda nhận được event với failure context\n\n4. **Simple configuration**:\n - Chỉ cần set 'On Failure' destination cho avatar generator Lambda\n - Không cần thay đổi existing S3 event trigger\n\nSai:\n- **B:** SQS queue cần polling logic và queue management → more development effort\n- **C:** Step Functions + EventBridge tạo complex workflow → highest development effort\n- **D:** SNS topic cần topic creation và subscription management → more development effort\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần simple failure handling cho Lambda → sử dụng Lambda Destinations là giải pháp đơn giản và hiệu quả nhất."},
{"id":"q41","q":"An application uses Lambda functions to extract metadata from files uploaded to an S3 bucket; the metadata is stored in Amazon DynamoDB. The application starts behaving unexpectedly, and the developer wants to examine the logs of the Lambda function code for errors. Based on this system configuration, where would the developer find the logs?","options":["Amazon S3","AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch","Amazon DynamoDB"],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudWatch Logs là default logging service cho Lambda**:\n - Lambda functions tự động gửi logs đến CloudWatch Logs\n - Không cần additional configuration\n - Tất cả stdout/stderr output được capture tự động\n\n2. **Application-level logging**:\n - CloudWatch Logs chứa application logs, errors, và execution details\n - Bao gồm Lambda function code errors, exceptions, và custom log messages\n\n3. **Log groups và log streams**:\n - Mỗi Lambda function có dedicated log group trong CloudWatch\n - Mỗi invocation tạo log stream riêng\n - Dễ dàng search và filter logs\n\n4. **Integration với AWS services**:\n - CloudWatch tích hợp với nhiều AWS services khác\n - Cung cấp metrics và alarms cùng với logs\n\nSai:\n- **A:** S3 dùng để store file objects, không phải application logs\n- **B:** CloudTrail ghi API calls và management events, không phải application code logs\n- **D:** DynamoDB store application data/metadata, không phải execution logs\n\n**Tips:** Lambda function logs luôn được gửi đến CloudWatch Logs tự động. Để xem Lambda logs → vào CloudWatch Console → Log groups → tìm log group của Lambda function."},
{"id":"q42","q":"A company is using an AWS Lambda function to process records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. The company recently observed slow processing of the records. A developer notices that the iterator age metric for the function is increasing and that the Lambda run duration is constantly above normal. Which actions should the developer take to increase the processing speed? (Choose two.)","options":["Increase the number of shards of the Kinesis data stream.","Decrease the timeout of the Lambda function.","Increase the memory that is allocated to the Lambda function.","Decrease the number of shards of the Kinesis data stream.","Increase the timeout of the Lambda function."],"correct":[0,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **A. Increase the number of shards of the Kinesis data stream**:\n - Mỗi shard hỗ trợ tối đa 5 concurrent Lambda invocations\n - Tăng shards = tăng parallelism và throughput tổng thể\n - Giảm iterator age (backlog) bằng cách tăng processing capacity\n\n2. **C. Increase the memory that is allocated to the Lambda function**:\n - Tăng memory cũng tăng CPU allocation proportionally\n - Function sẽ xử lý records nhanh hơn, giảm execution duration\n - Có thể xử lý nhiều records hơn trong cùng thời gian\n\n3. **Problem analysis**:\n - Increasing iterator age = Lambda không thể process records nhanh bằng rate records đến\n - High run duration = Lambda function đang xử lý chậm\n - Cần tăng cả stream capacity (shards) và function performance (memory/CPU)\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Giảm timeout sẽ gây nhiều failures hơn, không giải quyết root cause\n- **D:** Giảm shards sẽ làm vấn đề tồi tệ hơn, giảm parallelism\n- **E:** Tăng timeout chỉ cho phép function chạy lâu hơn, không cải thiện processing speed\n\n**Tips:** Khi có Kinesis iterator age cao + Lambda duration cao → scale cả stream (shards) và function (memory) để tăng processing speed."},
{"id":"q43","q":"A company needs to harden its container images before the images are in a running state. The company's application uses Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) as an image registry. Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) for compute, and an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that orchestrates a continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) workflow. Dynamic application security testing occurs in the final stage of the pipeline after a new image is deployed to a development namespace in the EKS cluster. A developer needs to place an analysis stage before this deployment to analyze the container image earlier in the CI/CD pipeline. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","options":["Build the container image and run the docker scan command locally. Mitigate any findings before pushing changes to the source code repository. Write a pre-commit hook that enforces the use of this workflow before commit.","Create a new CodePipeline stage that occurs after the container image is built. Configure ECR basic image scanning to scan on image push. Use an AWS Lambda function as the action provider. Configure the Lambda function to check the scan results and to fail the pipeline if there are findings.","Create a new CodePipeline stage that occurs after source code has been retrieved from its repository. Run a security scanner on the latest revision of the source code. Fail the pipeline if there are findings.","Add an action to the deployment stage of the pipeline so that the action occurs before the deployment to the EKS cluster. Configure ECR basic image scanning to scan on image push. Use an AWS Lambda function as the action provider. Configure the Lambda function to check the scan results and to fail the pipeline if there are findings."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **ECR Basic Scanning - Built-in và efficient**:\n - ECR Basic scanning tự động scan images for vulnerabilities\n - Scan được trigger trên image push, không cần manual intervention\n - Không có additional cost cho Basic scanning\n\n2. **Pipeline integration tại optimal stage**:\n - Stage mới sau image build nhưng trước deployment\n - Scan xảy ra sớm trong pipeline, ngăn insecure images được deploy\n - Lambda function tự động check scan results và fail pipeline nếu có findings\n\n3. **Most operational efficiency**:\n - Tận dụng AWS managed services (ECR scanning, Lambda, CodePipeline)\n - Không cần maintain scanning infrastructure\n - Automated workflow với minimal operational overhead\n\n4. **Container image focus**:\n - Scan actual container image (bao gồm OS packages, dependencies)\n - Khác với source code scanning chỉ scan application code\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Local scanning manual và không scalable, không integrate với CI/CD pipeline\n- **C:** Source code scanning không detect container-level vulnerabilities\n- **D:** Adding action to deployment stage là quá muộn - image đã được build và push\n\n**Tips:** Để container image scanning trong CI/CD → sử dụng ECR scanning sau image build + Lambda để automate pipeline control."},
{"id":"q44","q":"A developer is using AWS Amplify Hosting to build and deploy an application. The developer is receiving an increased number of bug reports from users. The developer wants to add end-to-end testing to the application to eliminate as many bugs as possible before the bugs reach production. Which solution should the developer implement to meet these requirements?","options":["Run the amplify add test command in the Amplify CLI.","Create unit tests in the application. Deploy the unit tests by using the amplify push command in the Amplify CLI.","Add a test phase to the amplify.yml build settings for the application.","Add a test phase to the aws-exports.js file for the application."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **amplify.yml build configuration**:\n - File amplify.yml định nghĩa build settings cho Amplify Hosting\n - Có thể thêm test phase vào build workflow\n - Tests chạy tự động trong CI/CD pipeline\n\n2. **End-to-end testing integration**:\n - Test phase trong amplify.yml có thể run end-to-end tests\n - Có thể sử dụng testing frameworks như Cypress, Selenium, etc.\n - Tests chạy sau build nhưng trước deployment\n\n3. **Pre-production bug prevention**:\n - Pipeline sẽ fail nếu tests không pass\n - Ngăn chặn buggy code được deploy đến production\n - End-to-end tests catch integration issues mà unit tests bỏ sót\n\n4. **Amplify Hosting native integration**:\n - Không cần external tools hoặc complex setup\n - Tích hợp trực tiếp vào existing Amplify workflow\n - Managed service với minimal operational overhead\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Không có 'amplify add test' command trong Amplify CLI\n- **B:** Unit tests không phải end-to-end tests, và amplify push không chạy tests\n- **D:** aws-exports.js là file config cho client-side, không phải build configuration\n\n**Tips:** Để thêm testing vào Amplify Hosting → sử dụng test phase trong amplify.yml build specification."},
{"id":"q45","q":"An ecommerce company is using an AWS Lambda function behind Amazon API Gateway as its application tier. To process orders during checkout, the application calls a POST API from the frontend. The POST API invokes the Lambda function asynchronously. In rare situations, the application has not processed orders. The Lambda application logs show no errors or failures. What should a developer do to solve this problem?","options":["Inspect the frontend logs for API failures. Call the POST API manually by using the requests from the log file.","Create and inspect the Lambda dead-letter queue. Troubleshoot the failed functions. Reprocess the events.","Inspect the Lambda logs in Amazon CloudWatch for possible errors. Fix the errors.","Make sure that caching is disabled for the POST API in API Gateway."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Asynchronous Lambda invocation behavior**:\n - Khi Lambda được invoke async, AWS tự động retry failed invocations (2 retries)\n - Chỉ sau khi cả 3 attempts đều fail, event mới được gửi đến DLQ\n - Lambda logs có thể không show errors vì retries xảy ra transparently\n\n2. **Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) for async processing**:\n - DLQ lưu trữ events mà Lambda không thể process sau maximum retries\n - Cho phép inspect failed events và troubleshoot root cause\n - Có thể reprocess events từ DLQ sau khi fix issues\n\n3. **No errors in Lambda logs**:\n - Events có thể bị drop trong async processing mà không có error logs\n - DLQ là nơi duy nhất để track những events này\n - Phù hợp với 'rare situations' described\n\n4. **Order processing reliability**:\n - DLQ đảm bảo không mất order data\n - Có thể reprocess orders sau khi resolve underlying issues\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Frontend logs chỉ show API call success, không capture async Lambda processing failures\n- **C:** Lambda logs đã được check và không có errors - vấn đề nằm ở async processing\n- **D:** API Gateway caching không liên quan đến async Lambda invocation failures\n\n**Tips:** Khi Lambda async invocation có missing events mà không có errors → check DLQ là bước đầu tiên."},
{"id":"q46","q":"A company is building a web application on AWS. When a customer sends a request, the application will generate reports and then make the reports available to the customer within one hour. Reports should be accessible to the customer for 8 hours. Some reports are larger than 1 MB. Each report is unique to the customer. The application should delete all reports that are older than 2 days. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Generate the reports and then store the reports as Amazon DynamoDB items that have a specified TTL. Generate a URL that retrieves the reports from DynamoDB. Provide the URL to customers through the web application.","Generate the reports and then store the reports in an Amazon S3 bucket that uses server-side encryption. Attach the reports to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) message. Subscribe the customer to email notifications from Amazon SNS.","Generate the reports and then store the reports in an Amazon S3 bucket that uses server-side encryption. Generate a presigned URL that contains an expiration date. Provide the URL to customers through the web application. Add S3 Lifecycle configuration rules to the S3 bucket to delete old reports.","Generate the reports and then store the reports in an Amazon RDS database with a date stamp. Generate an URL that retrieves the reports from the RDS database. Provide the URL to customers through the web application. Schedule an hourly AWS Lambda function to delete database records that have expired date stamps."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **S3 phù hợp cho large files**:\n - Reports >1 MB - S3 handle được files lớn không giới hạn\n - DynamoDB có item size limit 400KB, không phù hợp\n\n2. **Presigned URLs cho temporary access**:\n - Có thể set expiration time (8 hours) cho URL\n - Customer chỉ có thể access report trong thời gian quy định\n - Không cần authentication phức tạp\n\n3. **S3 Lifecycle cho automatic cleanup**:\n - Tự động delete reports sau 2 days\n - Không cần scheduled Lambda functions hoặc manual cleanup\n - Zero operational overhead\n\n4. **Server-side encryption**:\n - Đảm bảo data security at rest\n - SSE-S3 hoặc SSE-KMS đều được hỗ trợ\n\n5. **Least operational overhead**:\n - S3 là fully managed service\n - Không cần quản lý servers, databases, hoặc scheduling\n\nSai:\n- **A:** DynamoDB không phù hợp cho files >1 MB (400KB limit)\n- **B:** Email attachments không phù hợp cho large files, và không control được access duration\n- **D:** RDS + Lambda scheduling có higher operational overhead\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần temporary file access với automatic expiration → S3 + Presigned URLs + Lifecycle policies là giải pháp tối ưu."},
{"id":"q47","q":"A developer is migrating some features from a legacy monolithic application to use AWS Lambda functions instead. The application currently stores data in an Amazon Aurora DB cluster that runs in private subnets in a VPC. The AWS account has one VPC deployed. The Lambda functions and the DB cluster are deployed in the same AWS Region in the same AWS account. The developer needs to ensure that the Lambda functions can securely access the DB cluster without crossing the public internet. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure the DB cluster's public access setting to Yes.","Configure an Amazon RDS database proxy for the Lambda functions.","Configure a NAT gateway and a security group for the Lambda functions.","Configure the VPC, subnets, and a security group for the Lambda functions."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda VPC configuration**:\n - Configure Lambda để chạy trong cùng VPC với Aurora DB cluster\n - Lambda sẽ có ENI (Elastic Network Interface) trong VPC subnets\n - Có thể access DB cluster trực tiếp qua private network\n\n2. **Private subnets cho secure access**:\n - Đặt Lambda trong private subnets (cùng với DB cluster)\n - Traffic giữa Lambda và DB cluster không đi qua internet\n - Đảm bảo network isolation và security\n\n3. **Security groups cho network control**:\n - Security group cho Lambda cho phép outbound traffic đến DB port\n - Security group cho DB cho phép inbound traffic từ Lambda security group\n - Fine-grained network access control\n\n4. **No internet exposure**:\n - Toàn bộ communication xảy ra trong VPC private network\n - Không cần NAT gateway hoặc public internet access\n - Đáp ứng yêu cầu 'without crossing the public internet'\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Public access trên DB cluster sẽ expose database ra internet → không secure\n- **B:** RDS Proxy giúp connection management nhưng không giải quyết network connectivity\n- **C:** NAT gateway chỉ cần cho outbound internet access từ private subnets, không cần cho VPC-internal communication\n\n**Tips:** Để Lambda access RDS/Aurora trong VPC → configure Lambda VPC settings với proper subnets và security groups."},
{"id":"q48","q":"A company is building a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions. The company needs to create a set of test events to test Lambda functions in a development environment. The test events will be created once and then will be used by all the developers in an IAM developer group. The test events must be editable by any of the IAM users in the IAM developer group. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create and store the test events in Amazon S3 as JSON objects. Allow S3 bucket access to all IAM users.","Create the test events. Configure the event sharing settings to make the test events shareable.","Create and store the test events in Amazon DynamoDB. Allow access to DynamoDB by using IAM roles.","Create the test events. Configure the event sharing settings to make the test events private."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda built-in test events feature**:\n - Lambda console có tính năng tạo và quản lý test events\n - Events được lưu trữ và quản lý trực tiếp trong Lambda service\n\n2. **Shareable events configuration**:\n - Có thể configure test events thành 'shareable'\n - Cho phép tất cả IAM users trong account access và edit events\n - Không cần external storage hoặc complex IAM configurations\n\n3. **Collaborative development**:\n - Tất cả developers trong IAM group có thể sử dụng cùng test events\n - Có thể edit và update test events khi cần\n - Đảm bảo consistency trong testing\n\n4. **Simple management**:\n - Không cần quản lý S3 buckets hoặc DynamoDB tables\n - Không cần cấu hình IAM policies phức tạp\n - Integrated trực tiếp với Lambda testing workflow\n\nSai:\n- **A:** S3 storage cần bucket management, IAM policies, và không integrate trực tiếp với Lambda testing\n- **C:** DynamoDB phức tạp không cần thiết, không có direct integration với Lambda test events\n- **D:** Private events không cho phép sharing giữa multiple developers\n\n**Tips:** Để shared test events cho Lambda development → sử dụng Lambda's built-in shareable test events feature."},
{"id":"q49","q":"A developer is configuring an application's deployment environment in AWS CodePipeline. The application code is stored in a GitHub repository. The developer wants to ensure that the repository package's unit tests run in the new deployment environment. The developer has already set the pipeline's source provider to GitHub and has specified the repository and branch to use in the deployment. Which combination of steps should the developer take next to meet these requirements with the LEAST overhead? (Choose two.)","options":["Create an AWS CodeCommit project. Add the repository package's build and test commands to the project's buildspec.","Create an AWS CodeBuild project. Add the repository package's build and test commands to the project's buildspec.","Create an AWS CodeDeploy project. Add the repository package's build and test commands to the project's buildspec.","Add an action to the source stage. Specify the newly created project as the action provider. Specify the build artifact as the action's input artifact.","Add a new stage to the pipeline after the source stage. Add an action to the new stage. Specify the newly created project as the action provider. Specify the source artifact as the action's input artifact."],"correct":[1,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án B và E là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **B. Create AWS CodeBuild project với buildspec**:\n - CodeBuild là managed build service, không cần quản lý servers\n - Buildspec file định nghĩa build và test commands (install dependencies, run unit tests)\n - Có thể specify runtime environment phù hợp với application\n\n2. **E. Add new stage sau source stage**:\n - Tạo Build stage riêng biệt sau Source stage\n - CodeBuild project là action provider cho stage này\n - Source artifact từ GitHub là input, đảm bảo tests chạy trên latest code\n\n3. **Least overhead architecture**:\n - Fully managed services (CodePipeline + CodeBuild)\n - Không cần quản lý build servers hoặc infrastructure\n - Automated workflow từ source đến testing\n\n4. **Pipeline flow**:\n - Source Stage (GitHub) → Build Stage (CodeBuild với unit tests)\n - Nếu tests pass, pipeline tiếp tục; nếu fail, pipeline dừng\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CodeCommit không cần thiết khi đã dùng GitHub\n- **C:** CodeDeploy dùng cho deployment, không phải build và test\n- **D:** Không nên add action vào source stage - cần separate build stage\n\n**Tips:** Để thêm testing vào CodePipeline → tạo CodeBuild project với buildspec và add build stage sau source stage."},
{"id":"q50","q":"A company launched an online portal to announce a new product that the company will release in 6 months. The portal requests that users enter an email address to receive communications about the product. The company needs to create a REST API that will store the email addresses in Amazon DynamoDB. A developer has created an AWS Lambda function that can store the email addresses. The developer will deploy the Lambda function by using the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM). The developer must provide access to the Lambda function over HTTP. Which solutions will meet these requirements with the LEAST additional configuration? (Choose two.)","options":["Expose the Lambda function by using function URLs.","Expose the Lambda function by using a Gateway Load Balancer.","Expose the Lambda function by using a Network Load Balancer.","Expose the Lambda function by using AWS Global Accelerator.","Expose the Lambda function by using Amazon API Gateway."],"correct":[0,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và E là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **A. Lambda Function URLs - Least configuration**:\n - Built-in feature của Lambda, không cần additional services\n - Có thể enable với vài dòng code trong SAM template\n - Cung cấp HTTPS endpoint trực tiếp cho Lambda function\n - Perfect cho simple use cases như email collection\n\n2. **E. API Gateway - Standard for REST APIs**:\n - Được thiết kế specifically cho REST APIs\n - Tích hợp native với Lambda và AWS SAM\n - Có thể configure dễ dàng trong SAM template\n - Cung cấp features như rate limiting, caching, authentication\n\n3. **AWS SAM integration**:\n - Cả hai options đều có thể configure trực tiếp trong SAM template\n - Minimal additional configuration required\n - Deploy as part of serverless application\n\n4. **Simple use case fit**:\n - Email collection là simple POST operation\n - Không cần complex routing hoặc advanced features\n - Cả hai solutions đều đủ cho requirements\n\nSai:\n- **B, C:** Load Balancers (Gateway/Network) phức tạp hơn, cần VPC configuration, không tích hợp trực tiếp với Lambda\n- **D:** Global Accelerator dùng cho performance optimization, không phải để expose Lambda functions\n\n**Tips:** Để expose Lambda over HTTP với least configuration → Lambda Function URLs (đơn giản nhất) hoặc API Gateway (REST API standard)."},
{"id":"q51","q":"A developer creates a VPC named VPC-A that has public and private subnets. The developer also creates an Amazon RDS database inside the private subnet of VPC-A. To perform some queries, the developer creates an AWS Lambda function in the default VPC. The Lambda function has code to access the RDS database. When the Lambda function runs, an error message indicates that the function cannot connect to the RDS database. How can the developer solve this problem?","options":["Modify the RDS security group. Add a rule to allow traffic from all the ports from the VPC CIDR block.","Redeploy the Lambda function in the same subnet as the RDS instance. Ensure that the RDS security group allows traffic from the Lambda function.","Create a security group for the Lambda function. Add a new rule in the RDS security group to allow traffic from the new Lambda security group.","Create an IAM role. Attach a policy that allows access to the RDS database. Attach the role to the Lambda function."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **VPC isolation issue**:\n - Lambda trong default VPC và RDS trong VPC-A là separate network environments\n - Không có network connectivity giữa các VPCs mặc định\n - Lambda không thể reach RDS qua private network\n\n2. **Solution: Same VPC deployment**:\n - Redeploy Lambda trong VPC-A (cùng VPC với RDS)\n - Lambda sẽ có ENI trong VPC và có thể access RDS qua private network\n - Có thể đặt Lambda trong private subnet cùng với RDS hoặc trong public subnet\n\n3. **Security group configuration**:\n - RDS security group cần allow inbound traffic từ Lambda security group\n - Thường trên database port (3306 cho MySQL, 5432 cho PostgreSQL)\n - Reference Lambda's security group trong RDS security group rules\n\n4. **Network architecture fix**:\n - Đảm bảo cả Lambda và RDS trong cùng VPC\n - Proper subnet routing và security groups\n - Không cần internet gateway hoặc NAT cho internal communication\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Mở all ports từ VPC CIDR không secure và không giải quyết cross-VPC connectivity\n- **C:** Security group rules không giải quyết được vấn đề Lambda và RDS ở different VPCs\n- **D:** IAM roles giải quyết authentication, không giải quyết network connectivity\n\n**Tips:** Khi Lambda không thể connect đến RDS → đầu tiên check VPC configuration. Lambda và RDS phải trong cùng VPC hoặc có VPC peering/VPN connection."},
{"id":"q52","q":"A company runs an application on AWS. The company deployed the application on Amazon EC2 instances. The application stores data on Amazon Aurora. The application recently logged multiple application-specific custom DECRYP_ERROR errors to Amazon CloudWatch logs. The company did not detect the issue until the automated tests that run every 30 minutes failed. A developer must implement a solution that will monitor for the custom errors and alert a development team in real time when these errors occur in the production environment. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Configure the application to create a custom metric and to push the metric to CloudWatch. Create an AWS CloudTrail alarm. Configure the CloudTrail alarm to use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send notifications.","Create an AWS Lambda function to run every 5 minutes to scan the CloudWatch logs for the keyword DECRYP_ERROR. Configure the Lambda function to use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send a notification.","Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to create a metric filter that has a filter pattern for DECRYP_ERROR. Create a CloudWatch alarm on this metric for a threshold >=1. Configure the alarm to send Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notifications.","Install the CloudWatch unified agent on the EC2 instance. Configure the application to generate a metric for the keyword DECRYP_ERROR errors. Configure the agent to send Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notifications."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudWatch Logs Metric Filters - Real-time monitoring**:\n - Metric filters scan log data in real-time as it arrives\n - Có thể define filter pattern 'DECRYP_ERROR' để capture specific errors\n - Tự động tạo metric khi pattern được match\n\n2. **CloudWatch Alarms for immediate alerting**:\n - Alarm có thể trigger ngay lập tức khi metric >=1\n - Real-time notifications thông qua SNS\n - Không có delay như scheduled Lambda functions\n\n3. **Least operational overhead**:\n - Fully managed service - không cần quản lý servers hoặc code\n - Cấu hình đơn giản trong CloudWatch console\n - Không cần application code changes\n\n4. **Cost-effective và efficient**:\n - Không có cost cho metric filters (chỉ cho custom metrics được tạo)\n - Không cần Lambda execution costs\n - Minimal configuration và maintenance\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CloudTrail dùng cho API activity monitoring, không phải application logs\n- **B:** Lambda scheduled mỗi 5 phút không real-time, có operational overhead (code, deployment, monitoring)\n- **D:** CloudWatch agent cần installation và management, không real-time, higher operational overhead\n\n**Tips:** Để real-time log monitoring với least overhead → CloudWatch Logs Metric Filters + Alarms + SNS."},
{"id":"q53","q":"A developer created an AWS Lambda function that accesses resources in a VPC. The Lambda function polls an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for new messages through a VPC endpoint. Then the function calculates a rolling average of the numeric values that are contained in the messages. After initial tests of the Lambda function, the developer found that the value of the rolling average that the function returned was not accurate. How can the developer ensure that the function calculates an accurate rolling average?","options":["Set the function's reserved concurrency to 1. Calculate the rolling average in the function. Store the calculated rolling average in Amazon ElastiCache.","Modify the function to store the values in Amazon ElastiCache. When the function initializes, use the previous values from the cache to calculate the rolling average.","Set the function's provisioned concurrency to 1. Calculate the rolling average in the function. Store the calculated rolling average in Amazon ElastiCache.","Modify the function to store the values in the function's layers. When the function initializes, use the previously stored values to calculate the rolling average."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Reserved Concurrency = 1 giải quyết vấn đề concurrent execution**:\n - Đảm bảo chỉ có 1 Lambda instance chạy tại một thời điểm\n - Ngăn chặn race conditions khi multiple instances cùng update rolling average\n - Đảm bảo sequential processing của SQS messages\n\n2. **External storage với ElastiCache**:\n - Rolling average cần được lưu trữ persistently giữa các invocations\n - ElastiCache cung cấp fast, in-memory storage cho state management\n - Có thể store cả historical values và current average\n\n3. **Accurate state management**:\n - Mỗi invocation đọc current state từ cache, update với new values, và write back\n - Với reserved concurrency=1, không có concurrent access issues\n - Đảm bảo tính toán chính xác qua thời gian\n\n4. **SQS integration**:\n - Lambda poll SQS messages sequentially với single consumer\n - Không có message duplication hoặc out-of-order processing\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Không có reserved concurrency, multiple Lambda instances có thể cùng access và update cache → race conditions\n- **C:** Provisioned concurrency chỉ pre-initialize environments, không giới hạn concurrent executions\n- **D:** Lambda layers là read-only, không thể dùng để store dynamic state data\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần stateful processing với Lambda → sử dụng reserved concurrency=1 để đảm bảo sequential execution + external storage cho state management."},
{"id":"q54","q":"A company has a website that displays a daily newsletter. When a user visits the website, an AWS Lambda function processes the browser's request and queries the company's on-premises database to obtain the current newsletter. The newsletters are stored in English. The Lambda function uses the Amazon Translate TranslateText API operation to translate the newsletters, and the translation is displayed to the user. Due to an increase in popularity, the website's response time has slowed. The database is overloaded. The company cannot change the database and needs a solution that improves the response time of the Lambda function. Which solution meets these requirements?","options":["Change to asynchronous Lambda function invocation.","Cache the translated newsletters in the Lambda /tmp directory.","Enable TranslateText API caching.","Change the Lambda function to use parallel processing."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Caching trong /tmp directory giải quyết root cause**:\n - Newsletter là 'daily' - content chỉ thay đổi mỗi ngày một lần\n - Có thể cache translated newsletters trong Lambda's ephemeral storage (/tmp)\n - Giảm đáng kể database queries và Translate API calls\n\n2. **Giảm tải cho overloaded database**:\n - Thay vì query database cho mỗi request, chỉ cần query một lần mỗi ngày\n - Các requests sau đó serve từ cache\n - Database load giảm đáng kể\n\n3. **Improve response time**:\n - Không cần database query và translation cho cached requests\n - Response time nhanh hơn nhiều khi serve từ local cache\n - Giảm latency từ cả database và Translate API\n\n4. **Không cần thay đổi database**:\n - Giải pháp hoàn toàn ở application level\n - Không cần modify database infrastructure\n - Phù hợp với constraint 'cannot change the database'\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Asynchronous invocation không cải thiện response time cho user - user vẫn phải chờ kết quả\n- **C:** Amazon Translate không có built-in API caching feature\n- **D:** Parallel processing sẽ làm database overload tồi tệ hơn bằng cách tăng concurrent queries\n\n**Tips:** Khi có static/daily content và performance issues → caching là giải pháp hiệu quả nhất để giảm backend load và improve response time."},
{"id":"q55","q":"A developer deployed an application to an Amazon EC2 instance. The application needs to know the public IPv4 address of the instance. How can the application find this information?","options":["Query the instance metadata from http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/.","Query the instance user data from http://169.254.169.254/latest/user-data/.","Query the Amazon Machine Image (AMI) information from http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/ami/.","Check the hosts file of the operating system."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **EC2 Instance Metadata Service (IMDS)**:\n - Endpoint: http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/\n - Cung cấp thông tin về instance đang chạy\n - Public IPv4 address có tại: /latest/meta-data/public-ipv4\n\n2. **Cách truy cập**:\n ```bash\n curl http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/public-ipv4\n ```\n - Trả về public IPv4 address của instance\n\n3. **Metadata categories available**:\n - public-ipv4: Public IPv4 address\n - local-ipv4: Private IPv4 address\n - ipv6: IPv6 addresses (nếu có)\n - instance-id, instance-type, ami-id, etc.\n\n4. **Security và accessibility**:\n - Chỉ accessible từ within the EC2 instance\n - Không cần AWS credentials\n - Luôn available tại fixed IP address 169.254.169.254\n\nSai:\n- **B:** User data chứa script/data được cung cấp khi launch instance, không chứa network information\n- **C:** AMI information chỉ chứa thông tin về Amazon Machine Image, không phải instance network details\n- **D:** Hosts file (/etc/hosts) chứa local hostname mappings, không chứa public IP address\n\n**Tips:** Để lấy instance metadata từ EC2 → sử dụng Instance Metadata Service tại http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"},
{"id":"q56","q":"A developer wants to debug an application by searching and filtering log data. The application logs are stored in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The developer creates a new metric filter to count exceptions in the application logs. However, no results are returned from the logs. What is the reason that no filtered results are being returned?","options":["A setup of the Amazon CloudWatch interface VPC endpoint is required for filtering the CloudWatch Logs in the VPC.","CloudWatch Logs only publishes metric data for events that happen after the filter is created.","The log group for CloudWatch Logs should be first streamed to Amazon OpenSearch Service before metric filtering returns the results.","Metric data points for logs groups can be filtered only after they are exported to an Amazon S3 bucket."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudWatch Logs Metric Filter behavior**:\n - Metric filters chỉ apply cho log events xảy ra SAU KHI filter được tạo\n - Không process retroactively trên existing log data\n - Đây là design của CloudWatch Logs metric filtering\n\n2. **Real-time processing only**:\n - Filters monitor incoming log data in real-time\n - Historical data trong log group không được scan bởi new filters\n - Chỉ log events mới sau filter creation được evaluate\n\n3. **Expected behavior**:\n - Developer sẽ thấy metric data sau khi filter được tạo VÀ có new log events match pattern\n - Cần đợi application generate new log entries với exceptions\n\n4. **Alternative for historical data**:\n - Để search historical logs, sử dụng CloudWatch Logs Insights\n - Logs Insights có thể query existing log data\n - Metric filters chỉ cho real-time monitoring\n\nSai:\n- **A:** VPC endpoints không ảnh hưởng đến metric filter functionality\n- **C:** Không cần OpenSearch Service cho CloudWatch Logs metric filtering\n- **D:** Metric filters work directly trên CloudWatch Logs, không cần S3 export\n\n**Tips:** CloudWatch Logs metric filters chỉ process new log events sau khi filter creation. Để search historical data → dùng CloudWatch Logs Insights."},
{"id":"q57","q":"A company hosts a batch processing application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk with instances that run the most recent version of Amazon Linux. The application sorts and processes large datasets. In recent weeks, the application's performance has decreased significantly during a peak period for traffic. A developer suspects that the application issues are related to the memory usage. The developer checks the Elastic Beanstalk console and notices that memory usage is not being tracked. How should the developer gather more information about the application performance issues?","options":["Configure the Amazon CloudWatch agent to push logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs by using port 443.","Configure the Elastic Beanstalk .ebextensions directory to track the memory usage of the instances.","Configure the Amazon CloudWatch agent to track the memory usage of the instances.","Configure an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard to track the memory usage of the instances."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CloudWatch Agent cho custom metrics**:\n - CloudWatch agent có thể collect system-level metrics bao gồm memory usage\n - Mặc định, EC2 instances chỉ gửi basic metrics (CPU, network, disk) đến CloudWatch\n - Memory metrics cần CloudWatch agent để collect và send\n\n2. **Elastic Beanstalk integration**:\n - Có thể configure CloudWatch agent thông qua .ebextensions\n - Agent sẽ collect memory usage data từ tất cả instances trong environment\n - Data available trong CloudWatch để analysis và troubleshooting\n\n3. **Performance troubleshooting**:\n - Memory usage metrics giúp identify memory leaks hoặc insufficient memory\n - Có thể correlate memory usage với performance degradation\n - Essential cho batch processing applications với large datasets\n\n4. **Real monitoring solution**:\n - Cung cấp actual memory usage data thay vì chỉ visualization\n - Cho phép create alarms khi memory usage vượt threshold\n - Historical data cho trend analysis\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Port configuration không giải quyết memory tracking, và logs không phải metrics\n- **B:** .ebextensions chỉ là configuration mechanism, không trực tiếp track memory\n- **D:** Dashboard chỉ visualize data, không collect data - cần metrics trước khi tạo dashboard\n\n**Tips:** Để monitor memory usage trên EC2/Elastic Beanstalk → cần configure CloudWatch agent để collect và send memory metrics đến CloudWatch."},
{"id":"q58","q":"A developer has created an AWS Lambda function to provide notification through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) whenever a file is uploaded to Amazon S3 that is larger than 50 MB. The developer has deployed and tested the Lambda function by using the CLI. However, when the event notification is added to the S3 bucket and a 3,000 MB file is uploaded, the Lambda function does not launch. Which of the following is a possible reason for the Lambda function's inability to launch?","options":["The S3 event notification does not activate for files that are larger than 1,000 MB.","The resource-based policy for the Lambda function does not have the required permissions to be invoked by Amazon S3.","Lambda functions cannot be invoked directly from an S3 event.","The S3 bucket needs to be made public."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Resource-based Policy requirement**:\n - Khi S3 trigger Lambda, cần có permission trong Lambda's resource policy\n - S3 phải được authorize để invoke Lambda function\n - Thiếu policy này sẽ ngăn S3 invoke Lambda\n\n2. **Testing via CLI vs S3 trigger**:\n - CLI test sử dụng IAM permissions của user/role\n - S3 trigger cần explicit grant trong Lambda policy\n - Đây là common issue khi manual testing works nhưng event trigger fails\n\n3. **Correct policy configuration**:\n - Lambda resource policy cần cho phép `s3.amazonaws.com` principal\n - Action: `lambda:InvokeFunction`\n - Source ARN: S3 bucket ARN\n\n4. **File size không phải issue**:\n - S3 event notifications work với mọi file sizes\n - 3,000 MB file vẫn trigger event normally\n\nSai:\n- **A:** S3 event notifications work với files of any size, không có 1,000 MB limit\n- **C:** Lambda functions CÓ THỂ được invoke trực tiếp từ S3 events\n- **D:** S3 bucket không cần public để trigger Lambda functions\n\n**Tips:** Khi Lambda works với manual testing nhưng không với service triggers → check resource-based policies cho cross-service permissions."},
{"id":"q59","q":"A developer is creating a Ruby application and needs to automate the deployment, scaling, and management of an environment without requiring knowledge of the underlying infrastructure. Which service would best accomplish this task?","options":["AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CloudFormation","AWS OpsWorks","AWS Elastic Beanstalk"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Elastic Beanstalk - Platform as a Service (PaaS)**:\n - Fully managed service cho application deployment và management\n - Tự động handle infrastructure provisioning, scaling, monitoring\n - Developer chỉ cần upload code, EB handle everything else\n\n2. **Ruby application support**:\n - Hỗ trợ Ruby runtime environment out-of-the-box\n - Có thể deploy Ruby on Rails applications\n - Automatic platform updates và patches\n\n3. **No infrastructure knowledge required**:\n - Không cần hiểu EC2, load balancers, auto scaling groups\n - EB tự động creates và manages underlying infrastructure\n - Developer-focused với simple deployment process\n\n4. **Automated deployment, scaling, management**:\n - Continuous deployment từ Git repository\n - Auto scaling based on application load\n - Health monitoring và recovery\n - Environment management (dev, staging, prod)\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CodeDeploy chỉ handle deployment, không manage underlying infrastructure\n- **B:** CloudFormation yêu cầu infrastructure knowledge để define templates\n- **C:** OpsWorks (dựa trên Chef/Puppet) yêu cầu configuration management knowledge\n\n**Tips:** Khi cần deploy application mà không muốn manage infrastructure → Elastic Beanstalk là lựa chọn tốt nhất."},
{"id":"q60","q":"A company has a web application that is deployed on AWS. The application uses an Amazon API Gateway API and an AWS Lambda function as its backend. The application recently demonstrated unexpected behavior. A developer examines the Lambda function code, finds an error, and modifies the code to resolve the problem. Before deploying the change to production, the developer needs to run tests to validate that the application operates properly. The application has only a production environment available. The developer must create a new development environment to test the code changes. The developer must also prevent other developers from overwriting these changes during the test cycle. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort? (Choose two.)","options":["Create a new resource in the current stage. Create a new method with Lambda proxy integration. Select the Lambda function. Add the hotfix alias. Redeploy the current stage. Test the backend.","Update the Lambda function in the API Gateway API integration request to use the hotfix alias. Deploy the API Gateway API to a new stage named hotfix. Test the backend.","Modify the Lambda function by fixing the code. Test the Lambda function. Create the alias hotfix. Point the alias to the $LATEST version.","Modify the Lambda function by fixing the code. Test the Lambda function. When the Lambda function is working as expected, publish the Lambda function as a new version. Create the alias hotfix. Point the alias to the new version.","Create a new API Gateway API for the development environment. Add a resource and method with Lambda integration. Choose the Lambda function and the hotfix alias. Deploy to a new stage. Test the backend."],"correct":[1,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án B và D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **D. Lambda versioning và aliases**:\n - Publish new version sau khi fix code để tạo immutable deployment\n - Create 'hotfix' alias trỏ đến new version\n - Ngăn chặn developers khác overwrite changes (vì versions là immutable)\n\n2. **B. API Gateway stage isolation**:\n - Tạo new stage 'hotfix' trong existing API Gateway\n - Update integration để sử dụng Lambda alias 'hotfix'\n - Cung cấp isolated environment để test mà không ảnh hưởng production\n\n3. **Least development effort**:\n - Không cần tạo new API Gateway API\n - Sử dụng existing infrastructure với proper version control\n - Aliases và stages cung cấp isolation mà không cần duplicate resources\n\n4. **Safe testing environment**:\n - Hotfix stage có thể test độc lập với production\n - Lambda alias đảm bảo code không bị thay đổi trong quá trình test\n - Có thể rollback dễ dàng bằng cách update alias\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Sửa current stage sẽ ảnh hưởng đến production traffic\n- **C:** $LATEST version có thể bị overwrite bởi developers khác\n- **E:** Tạo new API Gateway API phức tạp hơn cần thiết\n\n**Tips:** Để test changes safely → sử dụng Lambda versions + aliases kết hợp với API Gateway stages."},
{"id":"q61","q":"A developer is implementing an AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) serverless application. The developer will provision several AWS Lambda functions and Amazon API Gateway APIs during AWS CloudFormation stack creation. The developer's workstation has the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) and the AWS CDK installed locally. How can the developer test a specific Lambda function locally?","options":["Run the sam package and sam deploy commands. Create a Lambda test event from the AWS Management Console. Test the Lambda function.","Run the cdk synth and cdk deploy commands. Create a Lambda test event from the AWS Management Console. Test the Lambda function.","Run the cdk synth and sam local invoke commands with the function construct identifier and the path to the synthesized CloudFormation template.","Run the cdk synth and sam local start-lambda commands with the function construct identifier and the path to the synthesized CloudFormation template."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CDK + SAM integration for local testing**:\n - `cdk synth` generates CloudFormation template từ CDK code\n - `sam local invoke` cho phép test Lambda function locally\n - Kết hợp cả hai cho phép test CDK-defined functions locally\n\n2. **Specific function testing**:\n - `sam local invoke` có thể target specific function bằng logical ID\n - Có thể pass test event data qua command line hoặc file\n - Cho phép rapid iteration và debugging\n\n3. **No deployment required**:\n - Không cần deploy lên AWS để test\n - Fast feedback loop cho development\n - Test trong isolated local environment\n\n4. **Workflow efficiency**:\n - CDK synth → SAM local invoke\n - Không cần manual template creation\n - Leverages existing SAM CLI capabilities\n\nSai:\n- **A, B:** Cả hai đều require deployment lên AWS, không phải local testing\n- **D:** `sam local start-lambda` starts local Lambda emulator, không invoke specific function directly\n\n**Tips:** Để test CDK Lambda functions locally → sử dụng `cdk synth` để generate template + `sam local invoke` để test specific function."},
{"id":"q62","q":"A company's new mobile app uses Amazon API Gateway. As the development team completes a new release of its APIs, a developer must safely and transparently roll out the API change. What is the SIMPLEST solution for the developer to use for rolling out the new API version to a limited number of users through API Gateway?","options":["Create a new API in API Gateway. Direct a portion of the traffic to the new API using an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy.","Validate the new API version and promote it to production during the window of lowest expected utilization.","Implement an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to trigger a rollback if the observed HTTP 500 status code rate exceeds a predetermined threshold.","Use the canary release deployment option in API Gateway. Direct a percentage of the API traffic using the canarySettings setting."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **API Gateway Canary Deployment - Built-in feature**:\n - Canary releases là tính năng tích hợp sẵn trong API Gateway\n - Cho phép route một phần traffic (%) đến new API version\n - Có thể configure trực tiếp trong stage settings\n\n2. **Simple configuration**:\n - Chỉ cần set `canarySettings.percentTraffic` trong API Gateway\n - Không cần external services hoặc complex routing logic\n - Có thể adjust percentage dynamically\n\n3. **Limited user exposure**:\n - Chính xác control số lượng users được expose đến new version\n - Có thể start với 5-10% traffic và gradually increase\n - Minimal risk nếu có issues với new version\n\n4. **Monitoring và rollback**:\n - Có thể monitor metrics cho cả canary và baseline deployment\n - Dễ dàng rollback bằng cách set percentTraffic về 0%\n - Tích hợp với CloudWatch metrics\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Tạo new API + Route 53 weighted routing phức tạp hơn, cần multiple APIs và DNS management\n- **B:** Big bang deployment không safe, không cho limited user exposure\n- **C:** CloudWatch alarm chỉ là monitoring, không phải deployment strategy\n\n**Tips:** Để canary deployment với API Gateway → sử dụng built-in canary release feature với percentTraffic settings."},
{"id":"q63","q":"A company caches session information for a web application in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The company wants an automated way to delete old items from the table. What is the simplest way to do this?","options":["Write a script that deletes old records; schedule the script as a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance.","Add an attribute with the expiration time; enable the Time To Live feature based on that attribute.","Each day, create a new table to hold session data; delete the previous day's table.","Add an attribute with the expiration time; name the attribute ItemExpiration."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **DynamoDB Time to Live (TTL) - Built-in automation**:\n - TTL là tính năng tích hợp sẵn trong DynamoDB\n - Tự động delete items dựa trên timestamp attribute\n - Không cần additional code hoặc infrastructure\n\n2. **Simple configuration**:\n - Chỉ cần add attribute chứa expiration timestamp (ví dụ: 'expirationTime')\n - Enable TTL trên table và chọn attribute đó\n - DynamoDB tự động handle deletion trong background\n\n3. **No operational overhead**:\n - Không cần quản lý EC2 instances, cron jobs, hoặc Lambda functions\n - Không có additional cost cho TTL feature\n - Fully managed bởi AWS\n\n4. **Perfect for session data**:\n - Session information thường có natural expiration\n - Có thể set TTL attribute khi tạo session\n - Đảm bảo automatic cleanup sau khi session expires\n\nSai:\n- **A:** EC2 + cron job có operational overhead (server management, monitoring, scaling)\n- **C:** Tạo/xóa tables daily là inefficient và có thể gây application downtime\n- **D:** Chỉ add attribute mà không enable TTL sẽ không tự động delete items\n\n**Tips:** Để automatic item expiration trong DynamoDB → sử dụng Time to Live (TTL) feature với timestamp attribute."},
{"id":"q64","q":"A developer is monitoring an application that runs on an Amazon EC2 instance. The developer has configured a custom Amazon CloudWatch metric with data granularity of 1 second. If any issues occur, the developer wants to be notified within 30 seconds by Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). What should the developer do to meet this requirement?","options":["Configure a high-resolution CloudWatch alarm.","Set up a custom CloudWatch dashboard.","Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights.","Change to a default CloudWatch metric."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **High-Resolution Alarms cho sub-minute monitoring**:\n - High-resolution alarms có thể evaluate metrics mỗi 10 giây hoặc 30 giây\n - Phù hợp với custom metric có 1-second granularity\n - Có thể trigger notifications trong vòng 10-30 giây\n\n2. **SNS integration**:\n - CloudWatch alarms có thể direct publish đến SNS topics\n - SNS gửi notifications đến subscribers (email, SMS, etc.)\n - End-to-end notification trong vòng 30 giây\n\n3. **Custom metric compatibility**:\n - Custom metrics với 1-second granularity yêu cầu high-resolution alarms\n - Standard alarms chỉ support 1-minute evaluation periods\n - High-resolution alarms support 10-second và 30-second periods\n\n4. **Real-time alerting**:\n - Đáp ứng yêu cầu 'notified within 30 seconds'\n - Có thể detect và alert issues gần real-time\n - Phù hợp cho critical application monitoring\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Dashboards chỉ cho visualization, không tự động send notifications\n- **C:** CloudWatch Logs Insights dùng cho log analysis, không phải real-time metric alerting\n- **D:** Default metrics có 1-minute granularity, không đáp ứng 30-second notification requirement\n\n**Tips:** Để sub-minute alerting với custom metrics → sử dụng CloudWatch High-Resolution Alarms với SNS integration."},
{"id":"q65","q":"A company moved some of its secure files to a private Amazon S3 bucket that has no public access. The company wants to develop a serverless application that gives its employees the ability to log in and securely share the files with other users. Which AWS feature should the company use to share and access the files securely?","options":["Amazon Cognito user pool","S3 presigned URLs","S3 bucket policy","Amazon Cognito identity pool"],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **S3 Presigned URLs cho temporary, secure access**:\n - Tạo URLs với temporary permissions (thường 1-7 days)\n - Cho phép access đến specific S3 objects mà không cần AWS credentials\n - URLs tự động expire sau thời gian xác định\n\n2. **Serverless application integration**:\n - Backend (Lambda) có thể generate presigned URLs cho authenticated users\n - Users chỉ cần click URL để download file\n - Không cần complex authentication flow cho file access\n\n3. **Security benefits**:\n - Bucket vẫn private - chỉ accessible qua presigned URLs\n - Fine-grained control (specific files, limited time)\n - Không expose bucket contents publicly\n\n4. **Complete architecture**:\n - Amazon Cognito User Pool cho employee authentication\n - Lambda backend xử lý business logic và generate presigned URLs\n - S3 presigned URLs cho secure file sharing\n\nSai:\n- **A, D:** Cognito chỉ handle authentication, không trực tiếp giải quyết file sharing\n- **C:** Bucket policies không linh hoạt cho per-user, per-file access control\n\n**Tips:** Để secure file sharing từ private S3 bucket → sử dụng S3 presigned URLs được generate bởi authenticated backend service."},
{"id":"q66","q":"An application is processing clickstream data using Amazon Kinesis. The clickstream data feed into Kinesis experiences periodic spikes. The PutRecords API call occasionally fails and the logs show that the failed call returns ProvisionedThroughputExceededException. Which techniques will help mitigate this exception? (Choose two.)","options":["Implement retries with exponential backoff.","Use a PutRecord API instead of PutRecords.","Reduce the frequency and/or size of the requests.","Use Amazon SNS instead of Kinesis.","Reduce the number of KCL consumers."],"correct":[0,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Exponential Backoff Retries (A)**:\n - ProvisionedThroughputExceededException thường là temporary\n - Exponential backoff giảm pressure trên Kinesis stream\n - Randomized delays prevent thundering herd problem\n - AWS SDKs often include built-in retry mechanisms\n\n2. **Request Optimization (C)**:\n - Reduce request frequency để stay within provisioned capacity\n - Decrease record size hoặc batch smaller records\n - Implement client-side buffering và batching\n - Monitor và adjust provisioned capacity based trên patterns\n\n3. **Kinesis Capacity Management**:\n - ProvisionedThroughputExceededException occurs khi vượt shard limits\n - Each shard supports 1MB/s write và 2MB/s read\n - Consider increasing shard count cho predictable spikes\n\n4. **Alternative Considerations**:\n - Kinesis Data Streams vs Kinesis Data Firehose cho different use cases\n - On-demand capacity mode cho unpredictable workloads\n - Monitor CloudWatch metrics để identify capacity issues\n\nSai:\n- **B:** PutRecord (single) thay vì PutRecords (batch) increases request count\n- **D:** Switching to SNS changes architecture significantly\n- **E:** KCL consumers affect read capacity, not write capacity\n\n**Tips:** Để handle Kinesis throughput limits → implement retries với exponential backoff và optimize request patterns."},
{"id":"q67","q":"A developer has written the following IAM policy to provide access to an Amazon S3 bucket. Which access does the policy allow regarding the s3:GetObject and s3:PutObject actions?","options":["Access on all buckets except the 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET' bucket","Access on all buckets that start with 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET' except the 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets' bucket","Access on all objects in the 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET' bucket along with access to all S3 actions for objects in the 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET' bucket that start with 'secrets'","Access on all objects in the 'DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET' bucket except on objects that start with 'secrets'"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **IAM Policy Evaluation Logic**:\n - First statement: Allows s3:GetObject và s3:PutObject trên DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/*\n - Second statement: Explicitly denies access đến objects starting với 'secrets'\n - Deny statements override Allow statements\n\n2. **Policy Effect**:\n - Access granted to all objects trong DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET\n - Except objects với key prefix 'secrets'\n - Objects like 'secrets/config.txt', 'secrets/keys.pem' are denied\n\n3. **IAM Policy Best Practices**:\n - Use explicit deny cho sensitive resources\n - Principle of least privilege\n - Regular expression pattern matching\n\n4. **Example Access Patterns**:\n - ✅ Allowed: DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/images/photo.jpg\n - ✅ Allowed: DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/documents/report.pdf\n - ❌ Denied: DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets/password.txt\n - ❌ Denied: DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/secrets-backup/config.bak\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Policy specifically targets DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET, not all buckets\n- **B:** Policy doesn't mention other buckets starting với same prefix\n- **C:** Policy denies access to 'secrets' objects, không allows all actions\n\n**Tips:** Để fine-grained S3 access control → sử dụng Allow statements với explicit Deny exceptions."},
{"id":"q68","q":"When using the AWS Encryption SDK, how does the developer keep track of the data encryption keys used to encrypt data?","options":["The developer must manually keep track of the data encryption keys used for each data object.","The SDK encrypts the data encryption key and stores it (encrypted) as part of the returned ciphertext.","The SDK stores the data encryption keys automatically in Amazon S3.","The data encryption key is stored in the Userdata for the EC2 instance."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **AWS Encryption SDK Design**:\n - SDK tự động encrypts data encryption key (DEK) với key encryption key (KEK)\n - Encrypted DEK được stored cùng với encrypted data trong ciphertext\n - No manual key tracking required\n\n2. **Envelope Encryption**:\n - DEK được used để encrypt data\n - KEK được used để encrypt DEK\n - Both encrypted DEK và encrypted data được stored together\n\n3. **Automatic Key Management**:\n - SDK handles key wrapping/unwrapping\n - Developer doesn't manage keys manually\n - Secure by design\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Manual tracking không cần thiết và error-prone\n- **C:** Keys không stored trong S3\n- **D:** Userdata không liên quan đến key storage\n\n**Tips:** AWS Encryption SDK uses envelope encryption - DEK encrypted với KEK và stored với ciphertext."},
{"id":"q69","q":"An application that runs on AWS Lambda requires access to specific highly confidential objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. In accordance with the principle of least privilege, a company grants access to the S3 bucket by using only temporary credentials. How can a developer configure access to the S3 bucket in the MOST secure way?","options":["Hardcode the credentials that are required to access the S3 objects in the application code. Use the credentials to access the required S3 objects.","Create a secret access key and access key ID with permission to access the S3 bucket. Store the key and key ID in AWS Secrets Manager. Configure the application to retrieve the Secrets Manager secret and use the credentials to access the S3 objects.","Create a Lambda function execution role. Attach a policy to the role that grants access to specific objects in the S3 bucket.","Create a secret access key and access key ID with permission to access the S3 bucket. Store the key and key ID as environment variables in Lambda. Use the environment variables to access the required S3 objects."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **IAM Roles for Lambda**:\n - Lambda execution roles provide temporary credentials\n - Credentials automatically rotated by AWS\n - No long-term access keys\n\n2. **Least Privilege Principle**:\n - Policy grants access chỉ đến specific S3 objects\n - Fine-grained permissions\n - No excessive permissions\n\n3. **Security Benefits**:\n - No credentials stored trong code hoặc environment variables\n - Automatic credential management\n - AWS handles security\n\n4. **Best Practice Implementation**:\n```json\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": \"s3:GetObject\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::confidential-bucket/specific-objects/*\"\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Hardcoded credentials are insecure\n- **B:** Long-term credentials violate principle\n- **D:** Environment variables can be exposed\n\n**Tips:** Để secure Lambda access → use IAM execution roles với fine-grained policies."},
{"id":"q70","q":"A developer at a company needs to create a small application that makes the same API call once each day at a designated time. The company does not have infrastructure in the AWS Cloud yet, but the company wants to implement this functionality on AWS. Which solution meets these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","options":["Use a Kubernetes cron job that runs on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS).","Use an Amazon Linux crontab scheduled job that runs on Amazon EC2.","Use an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by an Amazon EventBridge scheduled event.","Use an AWS Batch job that is submitted to an AWS Batch job queue."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Serverless Architecture**:\n - Lambda + EventBridge = fully serverless\n - No infrastructure management\n - Pay-per-use pricing\n\n2. **Scheduled Execution**:\n - EventBridge rules support cron expressions\n - Reliable scheduling\n - Automatic retries\n\n3. **Operational Efficiency**:\n - No servers to manage\n - Automatic scaling\n - High availability\n\n4. **Cost Effectiveness**:\n - Only pay for execution time\n - No idle resource costs\n - Perfect for daily tasks\n\nSai:\n- **A:** EKS overkill for simple task\n- **B:** EC2 requires ongoing management\n- **D:** Batch designed for compute-intensive jobs\n\n**Tips:** Để scheduled tasks → Lambda + EventBridge scheduled events."},
{"id":"q71","q":"A developer is building a serverless application that is based on AWS Lambda. The developer initializes the AWS software development kit (SDK) outside of the Lambda handler function. What is the PRIMARY benefit of this action?","options":["Improves legibility and stylistic convention","Takes advantage of runtime environment reuse","Provides better error handling","Creates a new SDK instance for each invocation"],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Execution Context Reuse**:\n - Lambda reuses execution context between invocations\n - Objects outside handler persist across warm starts\n - SDK initialization happens once\n\n2. **Performance Optimization**:\n - Reduces cold start time\n - Avoids repeated SDK initialization\n - Better resource utilization\n\n3. **Code Example**:\n```javascript\nconst AWS = require('aws-sdk');\nconst s3 = new AWS.S3(); // Initialized once\n\nexports.handler = async (event) => {\n // Uses pre-initialized SDK\n return await s3.getObject(params).promise();\n};\n```\n\n4. **Best Practice**:\n - Initialize connections outside handler\n - Reuse expensive operations\n - Improve performance\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Code organization is secondary benefit\n- **C:** Error handling not directly improved\n- **D:** Opposite of what we want\n\n**Tips:** Để optimize Lambda performance → initialize SDK/clients outside handler."},
{"id":"q72","q":"A company is using Amazon RDS as the backend database for its application. After a recent marketing campaign, a surge of read requests to the database increased the latency of data retrieval from the database. The company has decided to implement a caching layer in front of the database. The cached content must be encrypted and must be highly available. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Amazon CloudFront","Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached","Amazon ElastiCache for Redis in cluster mode","Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX)"],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **ElastiCache for Redis Features**:\n - Supports encryption at rest và in-transit\n - Cluster mode provides high availability\n - Multi-AZ deployment\n - Automatic failover\n\n2. **High Availability**:\n - Redis Cluster mode\n - Read replicas\n - Automatic backup\n - Cross-AZ replication\n\n3. **Encryption Support**:\n - TLS encryption in-transit\n - KMS encryption at-rest\n - Complies với security standards\n\n4. **RDS Integration**:\n - Reduces database load\n - Improves read performance\n - Scalable caching solution\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CloudFront for CDN, not database caching\n- **B:** Memcached doesn't support encryption\n- **D:** DAX for DynamoDB, not RDS\n\n**Tips:** Để encrypted, highly available caching → ElastiCache for Redis cluster mode."},
{"id":"q73","q":"A developer creates an AWS Lambda function that is written in Java. During testing, the Lambda function does not work how the developer expected. The developer wants to use tracing capabilities to troubleshoot the problem. Which AWS service should the developer use to accomplish this goal?","options":["AWS Trusted Advisor","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS X-Ray","AWS Cloud Trail"],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **AWS X-Ray Tracing Capabilities**:\n - Provides distributed tracing across services\n - Shows request flow through Lambda function\n - Identifies performance bottlenecks\n - Visualizes service dependencies\n\n2. **Java Integration**:\n - X-Ray SDK available for Java\n - Automatic instrumentation\n - Custom segments và subsegments\n\n3. **Troubleshooting Features**:\n - Error analysis\n - Latency identification\n - Service map visualization\n - Trace details\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```java\n// Add X-Ray dependency\nAWSXRayRecorderBuilder builder = AWSXRayRecorderBuilder.standard();\nAWSXRay.setGlobalRecorder(builder.build());\n\n// Create segments trong code\nSegment segment = AWSXRay.beginSegment(\"my-segment\");\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Trusted Advisor for cost optimization và security checks\n- **B:** CloudWatch for metrics và logs, not distributed tracing\n- **D:** CloudTrail for API activity logging\n\n**Tips:** Để distributed tracing → use AWS X-Ray."},
{"id":"q74","q":"A developer has an application that is composed of many different AWS Lambda functions. The Lambda functions all use some of the same dependencies. To avoid security issues, the developer is constantly updating the dependencies of all of the Lambda functions. The result is duplicated effort for each function. How can the developer keep the dependencies of the Lambda functions up to date with the LEAST additional complexity?","options":["Define a maintenance window for the Lambda functions to ensure that the functions get updated copies of the dependencies.","Upgrade the Lambda functions to the most recent runtime version.","Define a Lambda layer that contains all of the shared dependencies.","Use an AWS CodeCommit repository to host the dependencies in a centralized location."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Layers Benefits**:\n - Centralized dependency management\n - Single update applies to all functions\n - Version control cho dependencies\n - Reduced deployment package size\n\n2. **Security Maintenance**:\n - Update layer once, all functions benefit\n - Easy security patch deployment\n - Consistent dependency versions\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\n# SAM template example\nMyLayer:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::LayerVersion\n Properties:\n LayerName: shared-dependencies\n ContentUri: layer/\n CompatibleRuntimes:\n - java11\n\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n Layers:\n - !Ref MyLayer\n```\n\n4. **Operational Efficiency**:\n - No duplicate effort\n - Simplified dependency management\n - Easy rollback với layer versions\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Maintenance windows don't solve dependency management\n- **B:** Runtime upgrade doesn't update application dependencies\n- **D:** CodeCommit doesn't provide runtime dependency management\n\n**Tips:** Để shared dependencies → use Lambda Layers."},
{"id":"q75","q":"A mobile app stores blog posts in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Millions of posts are added every day, and each post represents a single item in the table. The mobile app requires only recent posts. Any post that is older than 48 hours can be removed. What is the MOST cost-effective way to delete posts that are older than 48 hours?","options":["For each item, add a new attribute of type String that has a timestamp that is set to the blog post creation time. Create a script to find old posts with a table scan and remove posts that are older than 48 hours by using the BatchWriteItem API operation. Schedule a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance once an hour to start the script.","For each item, add a new attribute of type String that has a timestamp that is set to the blog post creation time. Create a script to find old posts with a table scan and remove posts that are older than 48 hours by using the BatchWriteItem API operation. Place the script in a container image. Schedule an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) task on AWS Fargate that invokes the container every 5 minutes.","For each item, add a new attribute of type Date that has a timestamp that is set to 48 hours after the blog post creation time. Create a global secondary index (GSI) that uses the new attribute as a sort key. Create an AWS Lambda function that references the GSI and removes expired items by using the BatchWriteItem API operation. Schedule the function with an Amazon CloudWatch event every minute.","For each item, add a new attribute of type Number that has a timestamp that is set to 48 hours after the blog post creation time. Configure the DynamoDB table with a TTL that references the new attribute."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **DynamoDB TTL Feature**:\n - Automatic item expiration\n - No additional cost\n - Built-in functionality\n - Handles millions of items efficiently\n\n2. **Cost Effectiveness**:\n - No compute resources required\n - No manual scripting\n - AWS handles deletion automatically\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```javascript\n// Item structure\n{\n \"postId\": \"123\",\n \"content\": \"Blog post content\",\n \"createdAt\": 1672531200,\n \"expireAt\": 1672704000 // 48 hours later\n}\n```\n\n4. **Operational Simplicity**:\n - Configure once\n - Automatic background cleanup\n - No ongoing maintenance\n\nSai:\n- **A, B, C:** All require compute resources và ongoing management\n- **A, B:** Table scans are expensive và inefficient\n- **C:** Lambda scheduling adds complexity\n\n**Tips:** Để automatic item expiration → use DynamoDB TTL."},
{"id":"q76","q":"A developer accesses AWS CodeCommit over SSH. The SSH keys configured to access AWS CodeCommit are tied to a user with the following permissions. The developer needs to create/delete branches. Which specific IAM permissions need to be added, based on the principle of least privilege?","options":["\"codecommit:CreateBranch\" and \"codecommit:DeleteBranch\"","\"codecommit:Put*\"","\"codecommit:Update*\"","\"codecommit:*\""],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Principle of Least Privilege**:\n - Grant only required permissions\n - Specific actions for branch management\n - No excessive permissions\n\n2. **Required Permissions**:\n - codecommit:CreateBranch - create new branches\n - codecommit:DeleteBranch - delete existing branches\n\n3. **IAM Policy Example**:\n```json\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": [\n \"codecommit:CreateBranch\",\n \"codecommit:DeleteBranch\"\n ],\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:codecommit:region:account:repository-name\"\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\n4. **Security Best Practice**:\n - Minimal permissions required\n - Reduces security risk\n - Easy to audit\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Put* grants broader permissions\n- **C:** Update* not specific to branch operations\n- **D:** Wildcard grants excessive permissions\n\n**Tips:** Để least privilege → grant specific actions needed."},
{"id":"q77","q":"An application that is deployed to Amazon EC2 is using Amazon DynamoDB. The application calls the DynamoDB REST API. Periodically, the application receives a ProvisionedThroughputExceededException error when the application writes to a DynamoDB table. Which solutions will mitigate this error MOST cost-effectively? (Choose two.)","options":["Modify the application code to perform exponential backoff when the error is received.","Modify the application to use the AWS SDKs for DynamoDB.","Increase the read and write throughput of the DynamoDB table.","Create a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster for the DynamoDB table.","Create a second DynamoDB table. Distribute the reads and writes between the two tables."],"correct":[0,1],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Exponential Backoff (A)**:\n - Cost-effective retry strategy\n - Reduces pressure on DynamoDB\n - Handles temporary throughput issues\n - No additional AWS costs\n\n2. **AWS SDK Usage (B)**:\n - SDK implements automatic retry logic\n - Built-in exponential backoff\n - Handles throttling automatically\n - Best practice implementation\n\n3. **Implementation Benefits**:\n```python\n# AWS SDK handles retries automatically\nimport boto3\n\ndynamodb = boto3.resource('dynamodb')\ntable = dynamodb.Table('my-table')\n# SDK automatically retries với exponential backoff\nresponse = table.put_item(Item=item)\n```\n\n4. **Cost Effectiveness**:\n - No additional infrastructure costs\n - Code-only solution\n - Immediate implementation\n\nSai:\n- **C:** Increases costs permanently\n- **D:** DAX for read caching, not write throughput\n- **E:** Adds complexity và costs\n\n**Tips:** Để handle DynamoDB throttling → implement exponential backoff hoặc use AWS SDK."},
{"id":"q78","q":"A company is expanding the compatibility of its photo-sharing mobile app to hundreds of additional devices with unique screen dimensions and resolutions. Photos are stored in Amazon S3 in their original format and resolution. The company uses an Amazon CloudFront distribution to serve the photos. The app includes the dimension and resolution of the display as GET parameters with every request. A developer needs to implement a solution that optimizes the photos that are served to each device to reduce load time and increase photo quality. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Use S3 Batch Operations to invoke an AWS Lambda function to create new variants of the photos with the required dimensions and resolutions. Create a dynamic CloudFront origin that automatically maps the request of each device to the corresponding photo variant.","Use S3 Batch Operations to invoke an AWS Lambda function to create new variants of the photos with the required dimensions and resolutions. Create a Lambda@Edge function to route requests to the corresponding photo variant by using request headers.","Create a Lambda@Edge function that optimizes the photos upon request and returns the photos as a response. Change the CloudFront TTL cache policy to the maximum value possible.","Create a Lambda@Edge function that optimizes the photos upon request and returns the photos as a response. In the same function, store a copy of the processed photos on Amazon S3 for subsequent requests."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **On-Demand Optimization**:\n - Lambda@Edge processes images at edge locations\n - Optimized for each device's requirements\n - No pre-processing of unused variants\n\n2. **Caching Strategy**:\n - Store processed images trong S3\n - Subsequent requests served from cache\n - Reduced Lambda@Edge costs\n\n3. **Cost Effectiveness**:\n - Process only requested variants\n - Cache eliminates reprocessing\n - Pay-per-use pricing\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```javascript\n// Lambda@Edge example\nexports.handler = async (event) => {\n const request = event.Records[0].cf.request;\n const deviceParams = parseQueryString(request.querystring);\n \n // Check if optimized version exists trong S3\n // If not, process và store\n // Return optimized image\n};\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A, B:** Pre-processing creates unused variants\n- **C:** No caching leads to repeated processing\n\n**Tips:** Để dynamic image optimization → Lambda@Edge với S3 caching."},
{"id":"q79","q":"A company is building an application for stock trading. The application needs sub-millisecond latency for processing trade requests. The company uses Amazon DynamoDB to store all the trading data that is used to process each trading request. A development team performs load testing on the application and finds that the data retrieval time is higher than expected. The development team needs a solution that reduces the data retrieval time with the least possible effort. Which solution meets these requirements?","options":["Add local secondary indexes (LSIs) for the trading data.","Store the trading data in Amazon S3, and use S3 Transfer Acceleration.","Add retries with exponential backoff for DynamoDB queries.","Use DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) to cache the trading data."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **DAX Performance Benefits**:\n - Sub-millisecond read latency\n - In-memory caching layer\n - Seamless integration với DynamoDB\n\n2. **Minimal Effort Implementation**:\n - No application code changes required\n - Point SDK to DAX cluster endpoint\n - Automatic cache management\n\n3. **Trading Application Fit**:\n - Real-time data access requirements\n - High-frequency trading needs\n - Low latency critical\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```python\nimport amazondax\n\ndax_client = amazondax.AmazonDaxClient(\n endpoint='dax-cluster.endpoint.clustercfg.dax.use1.cache.amazonaws.com:8111'\n)\n# Use same API as DynamoDB client\nresponse = dax_client.get_item(TableName='trades', Key=key)\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** LSIs improve query flexibility, not latency\n- **B:** S3 has higher latency than DynamoDB\n- **C:** Retries don't improve base latency\n\n**Tips:** Để sub-millisecond DynamoDB access → use DAX."},
{"id":"q80","q":"A developer is working on a Python application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The developer wants to enable tracing of application requests to debug performance issues in the code. Which combination of actions should the developer take to achieve this goal? (Choose two.)","options":["Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances.","Install the AWS X-Ray daemon on the EC2 instances.","Configure the application to write JSON-formatted logs to /var/log/cloudwatch.","Configure the application to write trace data to /var/log/xray.","Install and configure the AWS X-Ray SDK for Python in the application."],"correct":[1,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án B và E là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **X-Ray Daemon (B)**:\n - Collects trace data từ application\n - Batches và sends to X-Ray service\n - Runs as background process\n\n2. **X-Ray SDK (E)**:\n - Instruments Python application code\n - Creates segments và subsegments\n - Captures timing data\n\n3. **Complete Tracing Setup**:\n```python\n# Install SDK\npip install aws-xray-sdk\n\n# Configure trong application\nfrom aws_xray_sdk.core import xray_recorder\nfrom aws_xray_sdk.core import patch_all\n\npatch_all() # Auto-instrument AWS SDK calls\n\n@xray_recorder.capture('my_function')\ndef my_function():\n # Function implementation\n pass\n```\n\n4. **Debugging Benefits**:\n - Request flow visualization\n - Performance bottleneck identification\n - Service dependency mapping\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CloudWatch agent for metrics/logs, not tracing\n- **C, D:** Incorrect log paths\n\n**Tips:** Để application tracing → X-Ray SDK + X-Ray daemon."},
{"id":"q81","q":"A company has an application that runs as a series of AWS Lambda functions. Each Lambda function receives data from an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and writes the data to an Amazon Aurora DB instance. To comply with an information security policy, the company must ensure that the Lambda functions all use a single securely encrypted database connection string to access Aurora. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Use IAM database authentication for Aurora to enable secure database connections for all the Lambda functions.","Store the credentials and read the credentials from an encrypted Amazon RDS DB instance.","Store the credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a secure string parameter.","Use Lambda environment variables with a shared AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key for encryption."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Parameter Store Secure String**:\n - Encrypted using KMS\n - Single source of truth\n - Access controlled via IAM\n\n2. **Centralized Management**:\n - All Lambda functions reference same parameter\n - Easy rotation\n - Version history\n\n3. **Security Compliance**:\n - Encryption at rest\n - Audit trail\n - Fine-grained access control\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```python\nimport boto3\n\nssm = boto3.client('ssm')\n\ndef get_db_connection_string():\n response = ssm.get_parameter(\n Name='/app/database/connection-string',\n WithDecryption=True\n )\n return response['Parameter']['Value']\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** IAM auth doesn't provide encrypted connection string storage\n- **B:** Storing credentials in another DB creates circular dependency\n- **D:** Environment variables have size limits và management overhead\n\n**Tips:** Để secure credential storage → use Parameter Store Secure String."},
{"id":"q82","q":"A company developed an API application on AWS by using Amazon CloudFront, Amazon API Gateway, and AWS Lambda. The API has a minimum of four requests every second. A developer notices that many API users run the same query by using the POST method. The developer wants to cache the POST request to optimize the API resources. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure the CloudFront cache. Update the application to return cached content based upon the default request headers.","Override the cache method in the selected stage of API Gateway. Select the POST method.","Save the latest request response in Lambda /tmp directory. Update the Lambda function to check the /tmp directory.","Save the latest request in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Modify the Lambda function to take the latest request response from Parameter Store."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **API Gateway Caching**:\n - Supports POST method caching\n - Configurable tại stage level\n - Reduces Lambda invocations\n\n2. **Cache Configuration**:\n - Override cache method cho POST\n - Set appropriate TTL\n - Configure cache key parameters\n\n3. **Performance Benefits**:\n - Faster response times\n - Reduced backend load\n - Cost optimization\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\n# SAM template example\nMyApi:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Api\n Properties:\n StageName: prod\n CacheClusterEnabled: true\n CacheClusterSize: '0.5'\n MethodSettings:\n - HttpMethod: POST\n CacheTtlInSeconds: 300\n CachingEnabled: true\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CloudFront doesn't cache POST requests by default\n- **C:** /tmp directory not shared across invocations\n- **D:** Parameter Store not designed for caching\n\n**Tips:** Để cache POST requests → enable API Gateway method caching."},
{"id":"q83","q":"A company is building a microservices application that consists of many AWS Lambda functions. The development team wants to use AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) templates to automatically test the Lambda functions. The development team plans to test a small percentage of traffic that is directed to new updates before the team commits to a full deployment of the application. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way? (Choose two.)","options":["Use AWS SAM CLI commands in AWS CodeDeploy to invoke the Lambda functions to test the deployment.","Declare the EventInvokeConfig on the Lambda functions in the AWS SAM templates with OnSuccess and OnFailure configurations.","Enable gradual deployments through AWS SAM templates.","Set the deployment preference type to Canary10Percent30Minutes. Use hooks to test the deployment.","Set the deployment preference type to Linear10PercentEvery10Minutes. Use hooks to test the deployment."],"correct":[2,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án C và D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Gradual Deployments (C)**:\n - SAM supports canary deployments\n - Traffic shifting strategies\n - Automatic rollback on failures\n\n2. **Canary Deployment (D)**:\n - 10% traffic initially\n - 30-minute testing period\n - Hooks for validation tests\n\n3. **SAM Configuration**:\n```yaml\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n DeploymentPreference:\n Type: Canary10Percent30Minutes\n Hooks:\n PreTraffic: !Ref PreTrafficHook\n PostTraffic: !Ref PostTrafficHook\n```\n\n4. **Operational Efficiency**:\n - Automated testing\n - Risk mitigation\n - No manual intervention\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Manual testing không efficient\n- **B:** EventInvokeConfig for async invocation, not deployment\n- **E:** Linear deployment different from canary\n\n**Tips:** Để canary deployments → use SAM deployment preferences với hooks."},
{"id":"q84","q":"A company is using AWS CloudFormation to deploy a two-tier application. The application will use Amazon RDS as its backend database. The company wants a solution that will randomly generate the database password during deployment. The solution also must automatically rotate the database password without requiring changes to the application. What is the MOST operationally efficient solution that meets these requirements?","options":["Use an AWS Lambda function as a CloudFormation custom resource to generate and rotate the password.","Use an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store resource with the SecureString data type to generate and rotate the password.","Use a cron daemon on the application's host to generate and rotate the password.","Use an AWS Secrets Manager resource to generate and rotate the password."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Secrets Manager Features**:\n - Automatic password generation\n - Scheduled rotation\n - No application changes required\n\n2. **CloudFormation Integration**:\n - Direct resource reference\n - Automatic secret management\n - Secure by default\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\nMySecret:\n Type: AWS::SecretsManager::Secret\n Properties:\n GenerateSecretString:\n SecretStringTemplate: '{\"username\": \"admin\"}'\n GenerateStringKey: \"password\"\n PasswordLength: 16\n\nMyDB:\n Type: AWS::RDS::DBInstance\n Properties:\n MasterUsername: !Join ['', ['{{resolve:secretsmanager:', !Ref MySecret, ':SecretString:username}}']]\n MasterUserPassword: !Join ['', ['{{resolve:secretsmanager:', !Ref MySecret, ':SecretString:password}}']]\n```\n\n4. **Operational Efficiency**:\n - Fully automated\n - No custom code\n - AWS-managed rotation\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Custom Lambda requires maintenance\n- **B:** Parameter Store doesn't auto-rotate\n- **C:** Manual solution inefficient\n\n**Tips:** Để automated password management → use Secrets Manager."},
{"id":"q85","q":"A developer has been asked to create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked any time updates are made to items in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The function has been created, and appropriate permissions have been added to the Lambda execution role. Amazon DynamoDB streams have been enabled for the table, but the function is still not being invoked. Which option would enable DynamoDB table updates to invoke the Lambda function?","options":["Change the StreamViewType parameter value to NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES for the DynamoDB table.","Configure event source mapping for the Lambda function.","Map an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to the DynamoDB streams.","Increase the maximum runtime (timeout) setting of the Lambda function."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Event Source Mapping**:\n - Connects Lambda to DynamoDB Stream\n - Required for stream processing\n - Manages batch processing\n\n2. **Configuration**:\n```yaml\nMyEventSourceMapping:\n Type: AWS::Lambda::EventSourceMapping\n Properties:\n EventSourceArn: !GetAtt MyTable.StreamArn\n FunctionName: !Ref MyFunction\n StartingPosition: LATEST\n```\n\n3. **Complete Setup**:\n - DynamoDB Stream enabled\n - Lambda execution role permissions\n - Event source mapping configured\n\n4. **Troubleshooting**:\n - Verify stream ARN\n - Check IAM permissions\n - Confirm function name\n\nSai:\n- **A:** StreamViewType affects data, not invocation\n- **C:** SNS not required for direct integration\n- **D:** Timeout unrelated to invocation\n\n**Tips:** Để Lambda process DynamoDB streams → configure event source mapping."},
{"id":"q86","q":"A developer needs to deploy an application running on AWS Fargate using Amazon ECS. The application has environment variables that must be passed to a container for the application to initialize. How should the environment variables be passed to the container?","options":["Define an array that includes the environment variables under the environment parameter within the service definition.","Define an array that includes the environment variables under the environment parameter within the task definition.","Define an array that includes the environment variables under the entryPoint parameter within the task definition.","Define an array that includes the environment variables under the entryPoint parameter within the service definition."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Task Definition Configuration**:\n - Environment variables defined tại container level\n - Part of task definition\n - Applied to all tasks\n\n2. **CloudFormation Example**:\n```yaml\nMyTaskDefinition:\n Type: AWS::ECS::TaskDefinition\n Properties:\n ContainerDefinitions:\n - Name: my-container\n Image: my-image:latest\n Environment:\n - Name: DB_HOST\n Value: !Ref DatabaseHost\n - Name: API_KEY\n Value: !Ref ApiKey\n```\n\n3. **Fargate Compatibility**:\n - Works với both EC2 và Fargate\n - Container-level configuration\n - Secure value handling\n\n4. **Best Practice**:\n - Use task definition for environment\n - Service definition for scaling/network\n - Separate concerns\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Service definition không chứa environment variables\n- **C, D:** entryPoint for command, not environment\n\n**Tips:** Để container environment variables → define trong task definition."},
{"id":"q87","q":"A developer is storing sensitive data generated by an application in Amazon S3. The developer wants to encrypt the data at rest. A company policy requires an audit trail of when the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key was used and by whom. Which encryption option will meet these requirements?","options":["Server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3)","Server-side encryption with AWS KMS managed keys (SSE-KMS)","Server-side encryption with customer-provided keys (SSE-C)","Server-side encryption with self-managed keys"],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **SSE-KMS Audit Trail**:\n - KMS API calls logged trong CloudTrail\n - Shows key usage và users\n - Complete audit capability\n\n2. **Encryption Implementation**:\n```python\nimport boto3\n\ns3 = boto3.client('s3')\n\n# Upload với SSE-KMS\ns3.put_object(\n Bucket='my-bucket',\n Key='sensitive-data.txt',\n Body=data,\n ServerSideEncryption='aws:kms',\n SSEKMSKeyId='alias/my-key'\n)\n```\n\n3. **Compliance Benefits**:\n - Encryption at rest\n - Access logging\n - Key usage tracking\n\n4. **CloudTrail Integration**:\n - GenerateDataKey calls logged\n - Decrypt calls logged\n - User identity tracking\n\nSai:\n- **A:** SSE-S3 doesn't provide KMS audit trail\n- **C:** SSE-C uses customer keys, no KMS audit\n- **D:** Self-managed keys outside AWS\n\n**Tips:** Để audit trail → use SSE-KMS."},
{"id":"q88","q":"A developer is testing an application that invokes an AWS Lambda function asynchronously. During the testing phase, the Lambda function fails to process after two retries. How can the developer troubleshoot the failure?","options":["Configure AWS CloudTrail logging to investigate the invocation failures.","Configure Dead Letter Queues by sending events to Amazon SQS for investigation.","Configure Amazon Simple Workflow Service to process any direct unprocessed events.","Configure AWS Config to process any direct unprocessed events."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Dead Letter Queues (DLQ)**:\n - Captures failed async invocations\n - After retries exhausted\n - Enables post-mortem analysis\n\n2. **DLQ Configuration**:\n```yaml\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n DeadLetterQueue:\n Type: SQS\n TargetArn: !GetAtt MyDLQ.Arn\n```\n\n3. **Troubleshooting Process**:\n - Check DLQ for failed events\n - Analyze event payload\n - Identify failure patterns\n\n4. **Async Invocation Flow**:\n - Event received → Lambda invoked\n - On failure → retry (default 2 times)\n - After retries → send to DLQ\n\nSai:\n- **A:** CloudTrail logs API calls, not event payloads\n- **C:** SWF for workflow orchestration\n- **D:** Config for resource configuration\n\n**Tips:** Để troubleshoot async failures → use Dead Letter Queues."},
{"id":"q89","q":"A developer is creating a mobile application that will not require users to log in. What is the MOST efficient method to grant users access to AWS resources?","options":["Use an identity provider to securely authenticate with the application.","Create an AWS Lambda function to create an IAM user when a user accesses the application.","Create credentials using AWS KMS and apply these credentials to users when using the application.","Use Amazon Cognito to associate unauthenticated users with an IAM role that has limited access to resources."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Cognito Unauthenticated Identities**:\n - Provides temporary AWS credentials\n - No user registration required\n - IAM role with limited permissions\n\n2. **Implementation**:\n```javascript\n// Configure Cognito Identity Pool\nconst cognitoIdentity = new AWS.CognitoIdentity();\n\n// Get credentials for unauthenticated user\nconst params = {\n IdentityPoolId: 'us-east-1:12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012'\n};\n\ncognitoIdentity.getId(params, (err, data) => {\n if (!err) {\n // Get temporary credentials\n cognitoIdentity.getCredentialsForIdentity({\n IdentityId: data.IdentityId\n }, (err, credentials) => {\n // Use credentials to access AWS resources\n });\n }\n});\n```\n\n3. **Security Benefits**:\n - Temporary credentials\n - Automatic rotation\n - Limited permissions\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Requires user authentication\n- **B:** IAM users don't scale\n- **C:** KMS for encryption, not access\n\n**Tips:** Để unauthenticated access → use Cognito Identity Pool."},
{"id":"q90","q":"A developer is creating a new REST API by using Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. The development team tests the API and validates responses for the known use cases before deploying the API to the production environment. The developer wants to make the REST API available for testing by using API Gateway locally. Which AWS Serverless Application Model Command Line Interface (AWS SAM CLI) subcommand will meet these requirements?","options":["Sam local invoke","Sam local generate-event","Sam local start-lambda","Sam local start-api"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **sam local start-api**:\n - Starts local API Gateway simulator\n - Handles HTTP requests\n - Routes to local Lambda functions\n\n2. **Local Testing Workflow**:\n```bash\n# Start local API Gateway\nsam local start-api\n\n# Test API endpoints\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:3000/hello\n```\n\n3. **Development Benefits**:\n - Fast iteration\n - No cloud deployment needed\n - Realistic API simulation\n\n4. **Configuration**:\n```yaml\n# template.yaml\nResources:\n MyApi:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Api\n Properties:\n StageName: dev\n \n MyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n Events:\n Hello:\n Type: Api\n Properties:\n Path: /hello\n Method: get\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Tests individual Lambda invocations\n- **B:** Generates sample event payloads\n- **C:** Starts Lambda endpoint only\n\n**Tips:** Để local API testing → use sam local start-api."},
{"id":"q91","q":"A company is developing an application that will be accessed through the Amazon API Gateway REST API. Registered users should be the only ones who can access certain resources of this API. The token being used should expire automatically and needs to be refreshed periodically. How can a developer meet these requirements?","options":["Create an Amazon Cognito identity pool, configure the Amazon Cognito Authorizer in API Gateway, and use the temporary credentials generated by the identity pool.","Create and maintain a database record for each user with a corresponding token and use an AWS Lambda authorizer in API Gateway.","Create an Amazon Cognito user pool, configure the Cognito Authorizer in API Gateway, and use the identity or access token.","Create an IAM user for each API user, attach an invoke permissions policy to the API, and use an IAM authorizer in API Gateway."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Cognito User Pool Features**:\n - User registration và authentication\n - JWT tokens với expiration\n - Automatic token refresh\n\n2. **API Gateway Integration**:\n - Cognito authorizer validates tokens\n - Automatic token validation\n - Fine-grained access control\n\n3. **Token Management**:\n - Access tokens (short-lived)\n - Identity tokens (user info)\n - Refresh tokens (auto-renewal)\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\nMyApi:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Api\n Properties:\n Auth:\n DefaultAuthorizer: MyCognitoAuthorizer\n Authorizers:\n MyCognitoAuthorizer:\n UserPoolArn: !GetAtt MyUserPool.Arn\n\nMyUserPool:\n Type: AWS::Cognito::UserPool\n Properties:\n UserPoolName: my-user-pool\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Identity pool for AWS service access\n- **B:** Manual token management complex\n- **D:** IAM users don't scale\n\n**Tips:** Để user authentication → use Cognito User Pool authorizer."},
{"id":"q92","q":"A company has an application that stores data in Amazon RDS instances. The application periodically experiences surges of high traffic that cause performance problems. During periods of peak traffic, a developer notices a reduction in query speed in all database queries. The team's technical lead determines that a multi-threaded and scalable caching solution should be used to offload the heavy read traffic. The solution needs to improve performance. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST complexity?","options":["Use Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached to offload read requests from the main database.","Replicate the data to Amazon DynamoDB. Set up a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster.","Configure the Amazon RDS instances to use Multi-AZ deployment with one standby instance. Offload read requests from the main database to the standby instance.","Use Amazon ElastiCache for Redis to offload read requests from the main database."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Memcached Benefits**:\n - Multi-threaded architecture\n - Simple key-value store\n - Low complexity implementation\n\n2. **Performance Improvement**:\n - Reduces database load\n - Faster read responses\n - Handles traffic spikes\n\n3. **RDS Integration**:\n - Application-level caching\n - Query result caching\n - Session storage\n\n4. **Implementation Simplicity**:\n```python\nimport pymemcache\n\n# Connect to ElastiCache Memcached\nclient = pymemcache.Client(('cache-node.elasticache.aws.com', 11211))\n\n# Check cache first\nresult = client.get('query-key')\nif not result:\n # Query database\n result = db.query('SELECT * FROM table')\n # Store in cache\n client.set('query-key', result, expire=3600)\n```\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Data replication adds complexity\n- **C:** Read replicas help but not caching\n- **D:** Redis more feature-rich but higher complexity\n\n**Tips:** Để simple multi-threaded caching → use ElastiCache Memcached."},
{"id":"q93","q":"A company needs to set up secure database credentials for all its AWS Cloud resources. The company's resources include Amazon RDS DB instances, Amazon DocumentDB clusters, and Amazon Aurora DB instances. The company's security policy mandates that database credentials be encrypted at rest and rotated at a regular interval. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST securely?","options":["Set up IAM database authentication for token-based access. Generate user tokens to provide centralized access to RDS DB instances, Amazon DocumentDB clusters, and Aurora DB instances.","Create parameters for the database credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Set the Type parameter to SecureString. Set up automatic rotation on the parameters.","Store the database access credentials as an encrypted Amazon S3 object in an S3 bucket. Block all public access on the S3 bucket. Use S3 server-side encryption to set up automatic rotation on the encryption key.","Create an AWS Lambda function by using the SecretsManagerRotationTemplate template in the AWS Secrets Manager console. Create secrets for the database credentials in Secrets Manager. Set up secrets rotation on a schedule."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Secrets Manager Features**:\n - Automatic credential rotation\n - Encryption at rest với KMS\n - Support for multiple database engines\n - Built-in rotation templates\n\n2. **Multi-Database Support**:\n - RDS, Aurora, DocumentDB\n - Automatic rotation integration\n - Centralized management\n\n3. **Security Compliance**:\n - Encryption tại rest\n - Automatic rotation\n - Access auditing\n\n4. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\nMySecret:\n Type: AWS::SecretsManager::Secret\n Properties:\n Description: \"Database credentials\"\n GenerateSecretString:\n SecretStringTemplate: '{\"username\": \"admin\"}'\n GenerateStringKey: \"password\"\n PasswordLength: 16\n ExcludeCharacters: \"\\\"@/\"\n\nMyRotationSchedule:\n Type: AWS::SecretsManager::RotationSchedule\n Properties:\n SecretId: !Ref MySecret\n RotationLambdaARN: !GetAtt RotationLambda.Arn\n RotationRules:\n AutomaticallyAfterDays: 30\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** IAM auth không support credential rotation\n- **B:** Parameter Store không có automatic rotation\n- **C:** S3 không designed cho credential management\n\n**Tips:** Để secure credential rotation → use Secrets Manager."},
{"id":"q94","q":"A developer is preparing to begin development of a new version of an application. The previous version of the application is deployed in a production environment. The developer needs to deploy fixes and updates to the current version during the development of the new version of the application. The code for the new version of the application is stored in AWS CodeCommit. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["From the main branch, create a feature branch for production bug fixes. Create a second feature branch from the main branch for development of the new version.","Create a Git tag of the code that is currently deployed in production. Create a Git tag for the development of the new version. Push the two tags to the CodeCommit repository.","From the main branch, create a branch of the code that is currently deployed in production. Apply an IAM policy that ensures no other users can push or merge to the branch.","Create a new CodeCommit repository for development of the new version of the application. Create a Git tag for the development of the new version."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Git Branching Strategy**:\n - Main branch: stable production code\n - Feature branch: new version development\n - Hotfix branch: production bug fixes\n\n2. **Parallel Development**:\n - Fix production issues independently\n - Develop new features separately\n - Merge changes when ready\n\n3. **CodeCommit Workflow**:\n```bash\n# Create branches from main\ngit checkout -b hotfix/production-fix main\ngit checkout -b feature/new-version main\n\n# Work on both branches simultaneously\n# Merge hotfix to main first\n# Later merge feature to main\n```\n\n4. **Best Practices**:\n - Maintain stable main branch\n - Isolate changes\n - Controlled merges\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Tags for releases, not active development\n- **C:** Branch protection too restrictive\n- **D:** Separate repos create fragmentation\n\n**Tips:** Để parallel development → use feature branches."},
{"id":"q95","q":"A developer is creating an AWS CloudFormation stack. The stack contains IAM resources with custom names. When the developer tries to deploy the stack, they receive an InsufficientCapabilities error. What should the developer do to resolve this issue?","options":["Specify the CAPABILITY_AUTO_EXPAND capability in the CloudFormation stack.","Use an administrators role to deploy IAM resources with CloudFormation.","Specify the CAPABILITY_IAM capability in the CloudFormation stack.","Specify the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability in the CloudFormation stack."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM**:\n - Required for IAM resources với custom names\n - Acknowledges IAM resource creation\n - Required security acknowledgment\n\n2. **CloudFormation Configuration**:\n```yaml\n# template.yaml\nAWSTemplateFormatVersion: '2010-09-09'\nDescription: Stack with custom IAM resources\n\nResources:\n MyCustomRole:\n Type: AWS::IAM::Role\n Properties:\n RoleName: MyCustomRoleName # Custom name requires capability\n AssumeRolePolicyDocument:\n Version: '2012-10-17'\n Statement:\n - Effect: Allow\n Principal:\n Service: lambda.amazonaws.com\n Action: sts:AssumeRole\n\n# Deploy with capability\naws cloudformation create-stack \\\n --stack-name my-stack \\\n --template-body file://template.yaml \\\n --capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM\n```\n\n3. **Capability Types**:\n - CAPABILITY_IAM: IAM resources với generated names\n - CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM: IAM resources với custom names\n - CAPABILITY_AUTO_EXPAND: Macros transforms\n\nSai:\n- **A:** AUTO_EXPAND for macros\n- **B:** Admin role doesn't resolve capability requirement\n- **C:** CAPABILITY_IAM for generated names only\n\n**Tips:** Để custom IAM resources → use CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM."},
{"id":"q96","q":"A company uses Amazon API Gateway to expose a set of APIs to customers. The APIs have caching enabled in API Gateway. Customers need a way to invalidate the cache for each API when they test the API. What should a developer do to give customers the ability to invalidate the API cache?","options":["Ask the customers to use AWS credentials to call the InvalidateCache API operation.","Attach an InvalidateCache policy to the IAM execution role that the customers use to invoke the API. Ask the customers to send a request that contains the Cache-Control:max-age=0 HTTP header when they make an API call.","Ask the customers to use the AWS SDK API Gateway class to invoke the InvalidateCache API operation.","Attach an InvalidateCache policy to the IAM execution role that the customers use to invoke the API. Ask the customers to add the INVALIDATE_CACHE query string parameter when they make an API call."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án B là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Cache-Control Header**:\n - Cache-Control: max-age=0 forces cache bypass\n - Standard HTTP header\n - No API changes required\n\n2. **IAM Permissions**:\n - execute-api:InvalidateCache permission\n - Attached to customer's execution role\n - Fine-grained access control\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```javascript\n// Customer makes request với cache bypass\nfetch('https://api.example.com/users', {\n headers: {\n 'Cache-Control': 'max-age=0',\n 'Authorization': 'Bearer token'\n }\n});\n```\n\n4. **IAM Policy Example**:\n```json\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": \"execute-api:InvalidateCache\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:execute-api:region:account:api-id/stage/*\"\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Direct AWS API access complex for customers\n- **C:** SDK usage adds complexity\n- **D:** Custom parameter không standard\n\n**Tips:** Để cache invalidation → use Cache-Control header với IAM permissions."},
{"id":"q97","q":"A developer must provide an API key to an AWS Lambda function to authenticate with a third-party system. The Lambda function will run on a schedule. The developer needs to ensure that the API key remains encrypted at rest. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Store the API key as a Lambda environment variable by using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key.","Configure the application to prompt the user to provide the password to the Lambda function on the first run.","Store the API key as a value in the application code.","Use Lambda@Edge and only communicate over the HTTPS protocol."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda Environment Variables**:\n - Encrypted at rest với KMS\n - Automatic decryption at runtime\n - Secure storage\n\n2. **KMS Encryption**:\n - Customer managed key recommended\n - Fine-grained access control\n - Audit trail\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n Environment:\n Variables:\n API_KEY: \"{{resolve:secretsmanager:api-key-secret:SecretString:api-key}}\"\n KmsKeyArn: !Ref MyKMSKey\n```\n\n4. **Security Benefits**:\n - Encryption tại rest\n - IAM-controlled access\n - No hardcoded credentials\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Manual input không feasible for scheduled Lambda\n- **C:** Hardcoded credentials insecure\n- **D:** Lambda@Edge for edge computing, không solve storage\n\n**Tips:** Để secure credential storage → use encrypted environment variables."},
{"id":"q98","q":"An IT department uses Amazon S3 to store sensitive images. After more than 1 year, the company moves the images into archival storage. The company rarely accesses the images, but the company wants a storage solution that maximizes resiliency. The IT department needs access to the images that have been moved to archival storage within 24 hours. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Use S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) to store the images. Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive with standard retrieval to store and retrieve archived images.","Use S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) to store the images. Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive with bulk retrieval to store and retrieve archived images.","Use S3 Intelligent-Tiering to store the images. Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive with standard retrieval to store and retrieve archived images.","Use S3 One Zone-Infrequent Access (S3 One Zone-IA) to store the images. Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive with bulk retrieval to store and retrieve archived images."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Storage Tier Strategy**:\n - S3 Standard-IA: frequently accessed infrequent data\n - Glacier Deep Archive: archival với 12-hour retrieval\n - Cost-effective lifecycle\n\n2. **Lifecycle Configuration**:\n```xml\n<LifecycleConfiguration>\n <Rule>\n <ID>ArchiveRule</ID>\n <Filter>\n <Prefix>images/</Prefix>\n </Filter>\n <Status>Enabled</Status>\n <Transition>\n <Days>365</Days>\n <StorageClass>DEEP_ARCHIVE</StorageClass>\n </Transition>\n </Rule>\n</LifecycleConfiguration>\n```\n\n3. **Retrieval Requirements**:\n - Standard retrieval: 12 hours\n - Bulk retrieval: 48 hours\n - Meets 24-hour requirement\n\n4. **Resiliency Maximization**:\n - Standard-IA: 99.999999999% durability\n - Deep Archive: 99.999999999% durability\n - Multi-AZ storage\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Bulk retrieval takes 48 hours\n- **C:** Intelligent-Tiering unnecessary monitoring cost\n- **D:** One Zone-IA reduces resiliency\n\n**Tips:** Để cost-effective archival → use lifecycle policies với appropriate retrieval tiers."},
{"id":"q99","q":"A developer is building a serverless application by using the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM). The developer is currently testing the application in a development environment. When the application is nearly finished, the developer will need to set up additional testing and staging environments for a quality assurance team. The developer wants to use a feature of the AWS SAM to set up deployments to multiple environments. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","options":["Add a configuration file in TOML format to group configuration entries to every environment. Add a table for each testing and staging environment. Deploy updates to the environments by using the sam deploy command and the --config-env flag that corresponds to each environment.","Create additional AWS SAM templates for each testing and staging environment. Write a custom shell script that uses the sam deploy command and the --template-file flag to deploy updates to the environments.","Create one AWS SAM configuration file that has default parameters. Perform updates to the testing and staging environments by using the --parameter-overrides flag in the AWS SAM CLI and the parameters that the updates will override.","Use the existing AWS SAM template. Add additional parameters to configure specific attributes for the serverless function and database table resources that are in each environment. Deploy updates to the testing and staging environments by using the sam deploy command."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **SAM Configuration File**:\n - samconfig.toml file\n - Environment-specific configurations\n - Minimal code changes\n\n2. **TOML Configuration Example**:\n```toml\nversion = 0.1\n[default]\n[default.deploy]\n[default.deploy.parameters]\nstack_name = \"my-app\"\ns3_bucket = \"my-bucket\"\n\n[testing]\n[testing.deploy]\n[testing.deploy.parameters]\nstack_name = \"my-app-testing\"\nparameter_overrides = \"Environment=testing\"\n\n[staging]\n[staging.deploy]\n[staging.deploy.parameters]\nstack_name = \"my-app-staging\"\nparameter_overrides = \"Environment=staging\"\n```\n\n3. **Deployment Commands**:\n```bash\n# Deploy to testing\nsam deploy --config-env testing\n\n# Deploy to staging\nsam deploy --config-env staging\n```\n\n4. **Least Development Effort**:\n - Single template\n - Configuration-driven\n - No custom scripts\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Multiple templates increase maintenance\n- **C:** Manual parameter overrides error-prone\n- **D:** Template bloat với many parameters\n\n**Tips:** Để multi-environment deployment → use SAM configuration files."},
{"id":"q100","q":"A developer is working on an application that processes operating data from IoT devices. Each IoT device uploads a data file once every hour to an Amazon S3 bucket. The developer wants to immediately process each data file when the data file is uploaded to Amazon S3. The developer will use an AWS Lambda function to process the data files from Amazon S3. The Lambda function is configured with the S3 bucket information where the files are uploaded. The developer wants to configure the Lambda function to immediately invoke after each data file is uploaded. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Add an asynchronous invocation to the Lambda function. Select the S3 bucket as the source.","Add an Amazon EventBridge event to the Lambda function. Select the S3 bucket as the source.","Add a trigger to the Lambda function. Select the S3 bucket as the source.","Add a layer to the Lambda function. Select the S3 bucket as the source."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **S3 Event Notification**:\n - S3 can trigger Lambda directly\n - Immediate invocation on file upload\n - Configurable event types\n\n2. **Trigger Configuration**:\n```yaml\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n Events:\n FileUpload:\n Type: S3\n Properties:\n Bucket: !Ref MyBucket\n Events: s3:ObjectCreated:*\n Filter:\n S3Key:\n Rules:\n - Name: suffix\n Value: .json\n```\n\n3. **Event Types**:\n - s3:ObjectCreated:Put\n - s3:ObjectCreated:Post\n - s3:ObjectCreated:Copy\n - s3:ObjectCreated:CompleteMultipartUpload\n\n4. **Immediate Processing**:\n - Sub-second invocation\n - Automatic scaling\n - Pay-per-use\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Async invocation not for S3 events\n- **B:** EventBridge unnecessary complexity\n- **D:** Layers for dependencies, not triggers\n\n**Tips:** Để S3-triggered Lambda → add S3 trigger."},
{"id":"q101","q":"A developer is building a serverless application that connects to an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. The serverless application consists of hundreds of AWS Lambda functions. During every Lambda function scale out, a new database connection is made that increases database resource consumption. The developer needs to decrease the number of connections made to the database. The solution must not impact the scalability of the Lambda functions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure provisioned concurrency for each Lambda function by setting the ProvisionedConcurrentExecutions parameter to 10.","Enable cluster cache management for Aurora PostgreSQL. Change the connection string of each Lambda function to point to cluster cache management.","Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a connection pool to manage the database connections. Change the connection string of each Lambda function to reference the proxy.","Configure reserved concurrency for each Lambda function by setting the ReservedConcurrentExecutions parameter to 10."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **RDS Proxy Benefits**:\n - Connection pooling\n - Reduced database connections\n - Improved scalability\n\n2. **Connection Management**:\n - Proxy maintains connection pool\n - Lambda functions share connections\n - Automatic connection reuse\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```yaml\nMyRDSProxy:\n Type: AWS::RDS::DBProxy\n Properties:\n DBProxyName: my-proxy\n EngineFamily: POSTGRESQL\n RoleArn: !GetAtt ProxyRole.Arn\n VpcSubnetIds: !Ref SubnetIds\n Auth:\n - AuthScheme: SECRETS\n SecretArn: !Ref DBSecret\n\nMyFunction:\n Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n Properties:\n Environment:\n Variables:\n DB_HOST: !GetAtt MyRDSProxy.Endpoint\n```\n\n4. **Scalability Preservation**:\n - Lambda scales independently\n - Proxy handles connection scaling\n - No Lambda concurrency limits\n\nSai:\n- **A:** Provisioned concurrency doesn't reduce connections\n- **B:** Cache management không solve connection pooling\n- **D:** Reserved concurrency limits scalability\n\n**Tips:** Để connection pooling → use RDS Proxy."},
{"id":"q102","q":"A developer is creating an AWS Lambda function that will generate and export a file. The function requires 100 MB of temporary storage for temporary files while running. These files will not be needed after the function is complete. How can the developer MOST efficiently handle the temporary files?","options":["Store the files in Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) and delete the files at the end of the Lambda function.","Copy the files to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) and delete the files at the end of the Lambda function.","Store the files in the /tmp directory and delete the files at the end of the Lambda function.","Copy the files to an Amazon S3 bucket with a lifecycle policy to delete the files."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án C là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Lambda /tmp Directory**:\n - 512MB available space\n - Ephemeral storage\n - Automatic cleanup after execution\n\n2. **Efficient Usage**:\n - No additional services\n - Fast local access\n - Automatic management\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```python\nimport os\nimport tempfile\n\ndef handler(event, context):\n # Use /tmp directory\n temp_file = '/tmp/temp_data.txt'\n \n # Write temporary file\n with open(temp_file, 'w') as f:\n f.write('temporary data')\n \n # Process file\n process_file(temp_file)\n \n # File automatically cleaned up after execution\n return {'status': 'success'}\n```\n\n4. **Cost Effectiveness**:\n - No additional storage costs\n - No network transfer costs\n - Included in Lambda pricing\n\nSai:\n- **A:** EBS not available to Lambda\n- **B:** EFS adds cost và complexity\n- **D:** S3 adds latency và cost\n\n**Tips:** Để temporary files → use Lambda /tmp directory."},
{"id":"q103","q":"A developer needs to launch a new Amazon EC2 instance by using the AWS CLI. Which AWS CLI command should the developer use to meet this requirement?","options":["aws ec2 bundle-instance","aws ec2 start-instances","aws ec2 confirm-product-instance","aws ec2 run-instances"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án D là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **run-instances Command**:\n - Launches new EC2 instances\n - Required parameters: ImageId, InstanceType\n - Optional: KeyName, SecurityGroups, etc.\n\n2. **Command Syntax**:\n```bash\naws ec2 run-instances \\\n --image-id ami-0abcdef1234567890 \\\n --instance-type t3.micro \\\n --key-name MyKeyPair \\\n --security-group-ids sg-0abcdef1234567890 \\\n --subnet-id subnet-0abcdef1234567890\n```\n\n3. **Required Parameters**:\n - --image-id: AMI ID\n - --instance-type: instance size\n\n4. **Common Options**:\n - --key-name: SSH key pair\n - --security-group-ids: firewall rules\n - --subnet-id: network placement\n\nSai:\n- **A:** bundle-instance for Windows instances\n- **B:** start-instances for stopped instances\n- **C:** confirm-product-instance for marketplace\n\n**Tips:** Để launch EC2 instances → use aws ec2 run-instances."},
{"id":"q104","q":"A developer needs to troubleshoot an AWS Lambda function in a development environment. The Lambda function is configured in VPC mode and needs to connect to an existing Amazon RDS for SQL Server DB instance. The DB instance is deployed in a private subnet and accepts connections by using port 1433. When the developer tests the function, the function reports an error when it tries to connect to the database. Which combination of steps should the developer take to diagnose this issue? (Choose two.)","options":["Check that the function's security group has outbound access on port 1433 to the DB instance's security group. Check that the DB instance's security group has inbound access on port 1433 from the function's security group.","Check that the function's security group has inbound access on port 1433 from the DB instance's security group. Check that the DB instance's security group has outbound access on port 1433 to the function's security group.","Check that the VPC is set up for a NAT gateway. Check that the DB instance has the public access option turned on.","Check that the function's execution role permissions include rds:DescribeDBInstances, rds:ModifyDBInstance. and rds:DescribeDBSecurityGroups for the DB instance.","Check that the function's execution role permissions include ec2:CreateNetworkInterface, ec2:DescribeNetworkInterfaces, and ec2:DeleteNetworkInterface."],"correct":[0,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Đáp án A và E là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Security Group Rules (A)**:\n - Lambda SG needs outbound to RDS SG\n - RDS SG needs inbound from Lambda SG\n - Port 1433 for SQL Server\n\n2. **Lambda VPC Permissions (E)**:\n - ec2:CreateNetworkInterface\n - ec2:DescribeNetworkInterfaces\n - ec2:DeleteNetworkInterface\n - Required for ENI creation\n\n3. **Troubleshooting Steps**:\n - Verify security group rules\n - Check Lambda execution role\n - Confirm VPC configuration\n\n4. **Common Issues**:\n - Missing VPC permissions\n - Incorrect security group rules\n - Subnet routing issues\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Inbound on Lambda không needed\n- **C:** NAT gateway for internet access\n- **D:** RDS permissions for management, not connectivity\n\n**Tips:** Để Lambda VPC connectivity → check security groups và VPC permissions."},
{"id":"q105","q":"A developer is creating an AWS Lambda function that accesses resources in a VPC. The Lambda function polls an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for new messages through a VPC endpoint. Then the function calculates a rolling average of the numeric values that are contained in the messages. After initial tests of the Lambda function, the developer found that the value of the rolling average that the function returned was not accurate. How can the developer ensure that the function calculates an accurate rolling average?","options":["Set the function's reserved concurrency to 1. Calculate the rolling average in the function. Store the calculated rolling average in Amazon ElastiCache.","Modify the function to store the values in Amazon ElastiCache. When the function initializes, use the previous values from the cache to calculate the rolling average.","Set the function's provisioned concurrency to 1. Calculate the rolling average in the function. Store the calculated rolling average in Amazon ElastiCache.","Modify the function to store the values in the function's layers. When the function initializes, use the previously stored values to calculate the rolling average."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Đáp án A là chính xác vì:\n\n1. **Reserved Concurrency = 1**:\n - Ensures single instance processing\n - Prevents race conditions\n - Sequential message processing\n\n2. **External State Storage**:\n - ElastiCache provides shared state\n - Persistent storage between invocations\n - Accurate rolling average calculation\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n```python\nimport redis\n\ndef handler(event, context):\n # Connect to ElastiCache\n r = redis.Redis(host='elasticache-endpoint', port=6379)\n \n # Get current average\n current_avg = r.get('rolling_average')\n \n # Calculate new average\n for record in event['Records']:\n value = float(record['body'])\n # Update average logic\n \n # Store updated average\n r.set('rolling_average', new_avg)\n```\n\n4. **Accuracy Guarantee**:\n - Single processor\n - Consistent state management\n - No duplicate processing\n\nSai:\n- **B:** Multiple instances can still run\n- **C:** Provisioned concurrency doesn't limit max concurrency\n- **D:** Layers not for dynamic data\n\n**Tips:** Để stateful processing → reserved concurrency + external storage."},
{"id":"q106","q":"A developer needs to manage AWS infrastructure as code and must be able to deploy multiple identical copies of the infrastructure, stage changes, and revert to previous versions. Which approach addresses these requirements?","options":["Use cost allocation reports and AWS OpsWorks to deploy and manage the infrastructure.","Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics and alerts along with resource tagging to deploy and manage the infrastructure.","Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk and AWS CodeCommit to deploy and manage the infrastructure.","Use AWS CloudFormation and AWS CodeCommit to deploy and manage the infrastructure."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"CloudFormation provides Infrastructure as Code (IaC) capabilities for deploying identical copies and managing changes. CodeCommit provides version control for the infrastructure code, enabling staging and reverting to previous versions.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: OpsWorks is for configuration management, not full IaC\n- B: CloudWatch is for monitoring, not deployment\n- C: Elastic Beanstalk is for application deployment, not infrastructure management\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q107","q":"A developer is working on an AWS Lambda function that accesses Amazon DynamoDB. The Lambda function must retrieve an item and update some of its attributes, or create the item if it does not exist. The Lambda function has access to the primary key. Which IAM permissions should the developer request for the Lambda function to achieve this functionality?","options":["dynamodb:DeleteItem & dynamodb:GetItem & dynamodb:PutItem","dynamodb:UpdateItem & dynamodb:GetItem & dynamodb:DescribeTable","dynamodb:GetRecords & dynamodb:PutItem & dynamodb:UpdateTable","dynamodb:UpdateItem & dynamodb:GetItem & dynamodb:PutItem"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"The required operations are:\n- GetItem: Retrieve an item\n- UpdateItem: Update attributes of existing item\n- PutItem: Create item if it doesn't exist\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: DeleteItem not required\n- B: DescribeTable not required\n- C: GetRecords and UpdateTable not required\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q108","q":"A developer has built a market application that stores pricing data in Amazon DynamoDB with Amazon ElastiCache in front. The prices of items in the market change frequently. Sellers have begun complaining that, after they update the price of an item, the price does not actually change in the product listing. What could be causing this issue?","options":["The cache is not being invalidated when the price of the item is changed.","The price of the item is being retrieved using a write-through ElastiCache cluster.","The DynamoDB table was provisioned with insufficient read capacity.","The DynamoDB table was provisioned with insufficient write capacity."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"When prices are updated in DynamoDB, the application continues to read stale data from ElastiCache because the cache isn't invalidated. The application needs to either invalidate the cache or implement a write-through caching pattern.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: Write-through would solve the problem, not cause it\n- C, D: Read/Write capacity issues would cause errors, not stale data\n\nTips:\nDAX chỉ tăng tốc ĐỌC DynamoDB. ElastiCache cho cache tầng ứng dụng (Redis: persistence/pub-sub; Memcached: đơn giản, multi-thread)."},
{"id":"q109","q":"A company requires that all applications running on Amazon EC2 use IAM roles to gain access to AWS services. A developer is modifying an application that currently relies on IAM user access keys stored in environment variables to access Amazon DynamoDB tables using boto, the AWS SDK for Python. The developer associated a role with the same permissions as the IAM user to the EC2 instance, then deleted the IAM user. When the application was restarted, the AWS AccessDeniedException messages started appearing in the application logs. The developer was able to use their personal account on the server to run DynamoDB API commands using the AWS CLI. What is the MOST likely cause of the exception?","options":["IAM policies might take a few minutes to propagate to resources.","Disabled environment variable credentials are still being used by the application.","The AWS SDK does not support credentials obtained using an instance role.","The instance's security group does not allow access to http://169.254.169.254."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"The application is still using the old access keys stored in environment variables, which are now invalid since the IAM user was deleted. The AWS SDK credential chain checks environment variables first before falling back to instance metadata.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: IAM policy propagation is nearly instantaneous\n- C: AWS SDK fully supports instance roles\n- D: 169.254.169.254 is for instance metadata, not related to this issue\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q110","q":"A company has an existing application that has hardcoded database credentials. A developer needs to modify the existing application. The application is deployed in two AWS Regions with an active-passive failover configuration to meet company's disaster recovery strategy. The developer needs a solution to store the credentials outside the code. The solution must comply with the company's disaster recovery strategy. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST secure way?","options":["Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager in the primary Region. Enable secret replication to the secondary Region. Update the application to use the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) based on the Region.","Store credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store in the primary Region. Enable parameter replication to the secondary Region. Update the application to use the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) based on the Region.","Store credentials in a config file. Upload the config file to an S3 bucket in the primary Region. Enable Cross-Region Replication (CRR) to an S3 bucket in the secondary region. Update the application to access the config file from the S3 bucket, based on the Region.","Store credentials in a config file. Upload the config file to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Update the application to use the Amazon EFS file system Regional endpoints to access the config file in the primary and secondary Regions."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Secrets Manager provides automatic encryption, rotation, and cross-region replication capabilities. It's the most secure option that directly supports the active-passive DR strategy.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: Parameter Store doesn't support cross-region replication\n- C, D: Storing credentials in config files on S3/EFS is less secure and more complex to manage\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q111","q":"A developer is receiving HTTP 400: ThrottlingException errors intermittently when calling the Amazon CloudWatch API. When a call fails, no data is retrieved. What best practice should first be applied to address this issue?","options":["Contact AWS Support for a limit increase.","Use the AWS CLI to get the metrics.","Analyze the applications and remove the API call.","Retry the call with exponential backoff."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Exponential backoff with jitter is the standard AWS best practice for handling throttling exceptions. It gradually increases wait times between retries while adding randomness to avoid synchronized retries.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: API limits are fixed and cannot be increased\n- B: CLI uses the same API and would experience same throttling\n- C: Removing functionality is not a solution\n\nTips:\nThrottling: kiểm tra (1) concurrency limit với Lambda, (2) hot partition với DynamoDB, (3) capacity mode. Xử lý gốc bằng retry + exponential backoff TRƯỚC khi tăng capacity."},
{"id":"q112","q":"A company used AWS to develop an application for customers. The application includes an Amazon API Gateway API that invokes AWS Lambda functions. The Lambda functions process data and store the data in Amazon DynamoDB tables. The company must monitor the entire application to identify potential bottlenecks in the architecture that can negatively affect customers. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","options":["Instrument the application with AWS X-Ray. Inspect the service map to identify errors and issues.","Configure Lambda exceptions and additional logging to Amazon CloudWatch. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the logs.","Configure API Gateway to log responses to Amazon CloudWatch. Create a metric filter for the TooManyRequestsException error message.","Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics for the DynamoDB tables to identify all the ProvisionedThroughputExceeded Exception error messages."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"X-Ray provides end-to-end tracing across API Gateway, Lambda, and DynamoDB with minimal development effort. The service map visually identifies bottlenecks and latency issues.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: Requires significant custom logging and analysis effort\n- C, D: Only monitor specific components, not the full application flow\n\nTips:\nTrace phân tán → X-Ray; trên on-premises/server ngoài AWS cần chạy X-Ray daemon. Bật tracing ở MỌI service trong đường đi, nếu không trace sẽ đứt."},
{"id":"q113","q":"An application uses AWS X-Ray to generate a large amount of trace data on an hourly basis. A developer wants to use filter expressions to limit the returned results through user-specified custom attributes. How should the developer use filter expressions to filter the results in X-Ray?","options":["Add custom attributes as annotations in the segment document.","Add custom attributes as metadata in the segment document.","Add custom attributes as new segment fields in the segment document.","Create new sampling rules that are based on custom attributes."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Annotations in X-Ray are indexed key-value pairs that can be used in filter expressions. They are designed specifically for filtering and grouping trace data.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: Metadata is not indexed and cannot be used in filters\n- C: Custom segment fields don't exist in X-Ray\n- D: Sampling rules control which requests are traced, not how results are filtered\n\nTips:\nTrace phân tán → X-Ray; trên on-premises/server ngoài AWS cần chạy X-Ray daemon. Bật tracing ở MỌI service trong đường đi, nếu không trace sẽ đứt."},
{"id":"q114","q":"A web application is using Amazon Kinesis Data Streams for clickstream data that may not be consumed for up to 12 hours. How can the developer implement encryption at rest for data within the Kinesis Data Streams?","options":["Enable SSL connections to Kinesis.","Use Amazon Kinesis Consumer Library.","Encrypt the data once it is at rest with a Lambda function.","Enable server-side encryption in Kinesis Data Streams."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Kinesis Data Streams supports server-side encryption at rest using AWS KMS. This can be enabled during stream creation or on existing streams.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: SSL provides encryption in transit, not at rest\n- B: KCL is for consumer applications, not encryption\n- C: Manual encryption with Lambda is unnecessary and complex\n\nTips:\n“Encrypted at rest” luôn cần KMS (SSE-KMS cho S3/EBS, KMS cho DynamoDB). Nếu đề hỏi thêm cross-account → nhớ bucket policy / key policy."},
{"id":"q115","q":"An application is real-time processing millions of events that are received through an API. What service could be used to allow multiple consumers to process the data concurrently and MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Amazon SNS with fanout to an SQS queue for each application","Amazon SNS with fanout to an SQS FIFO (first-in, first-out) queue for each application","Amazon Kinesis Firehose","Amazon Kinesis Data Streams"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Kinesis Data Streams is designed for real-time processing of millions of events with multiple consumers. It provides ordered, replayable streams and supports multiple consumer applications reading the same data concurrently.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A, B: SNS/SQS is for message fanout but not optimized for millions of real-time events\n- C: Kinesis Firehose is for loading data to destinations, not real-time processing\n\nTips:\nDecouple → SQS (queue, 1 consumer) hoặc SNS fan-out (nhiều subscriber). Cần filter nội dung phức tạp → EventBridge."},
{"id":"q116","q":"Given the following AWS CloudFormation template: What is the MOST efficient way to reference the new Amazon S3 bucket from another AWS CloudFormation template?","options":["Add an Export declaration to the Outputs section of the original template and use ImportValue in other templates.","Add Exported: true to the Content.Bucket in the original template and use ImportResource in other templates.","Create a custom AWS CloudFormation resource that gets the bucket name from the ContentBucket resource of the first stack.","Use Fn::Include to include the existing template in other templates and use the ContentBucket resource directly."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"CloudFormation Cross-Stack References using Export/ImportValue is the standard and most efficient way to share resource information between stacks.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: Invalid CloudFormation syntax\n- C: Custom resources add unnecessary complexity\n- D: Fn::Include is not a valid CloudFormation function\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q117","q":"A developer has built an application that inserts data into an Amazon DynamoDB table. The table is configured to use provisioned capacity. The application is deployed on a burstable nano Amazon EC2 instance. The application logs show that the application has been failing because of a ProvisionedThroughputExceededException error. Which actions should the developer take to resolve this issue? (Choose two.)","options":["Move the application to a larger EC2 instance.","Increase the number of write capacity units (WCUs) that are provisioned for the DynamoDB table.","Reduce the frequency of requests to DynamoDB by implementing exponential backoff.","Increase the frequency of requests to DynamoDB by decreasing the retry delay.","Change the capacity mode of the DynamoDB table from provisioned to on-demand."],"correct":[1,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"Two effective solutions:\n- B: Increase WCUs to handle the current workload\n- C: Implement exponential backoff to handle throttling gracefully\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: EC2 instance size doesn't affect DynamoDB throttling\n- D: Increasing frequency would make the problem worse\n- E: While possible, on-demand may increase costs unnecessarily\n\nTips:\nLỗi xử lý lặp lại → DLQ + maxReceiveCount. Lambda async tự retry 2 lần; muốn kiểm soát tốt hơn thì dùng on-failure destination. Luôn thiết kế idempotent."},
{"id":"q118","q":"A company is hosting a workshop for external users and wants to share the reference documents with the external users for 7 days. The company stores the reference documents in an Amazon S3 bucket that the company owns. What is the MOST secure way to share the documents with the external users?","options":["Use S3 presigned URLs to share the documents with the external users. Set an expiration time of 7 days.","Move the documents to an Amazon WorkDocs folder. Share the links of the WorkDocs folder with the external users.","Create temporary IAM users that have read-only access to the S3 bucket. Share the access keys with the external users. Expire the credentials after 7 days.","Create a role that has read-only access to the S3 bucket. Share the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of this role with the external users."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"S3 presigned URLs provide time-limited access to specific objects without requiring AWS credentials from external users. They are secure and easy to manage.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: WorkDocs is for internal collaboration, not external sharing\n- C: Creating IAM users for external users is a security risk\n- D: External users cannot assume roles without AWS accounts\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q119","q":"A developer is planning to use an Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda to provide a REST API. The developer will have three distinct environments to manage: development, test, and production. How should the application be deployed while minimizing the number of resources to manage?","options":["Create a separate API Gateway and separate Lambda function for each environment in the same Region.","Assign a Region for each environment and deploy API Gateway and Lambda to each Region.","Create one API Gateway with multiple stages with one Lambda function with multiple aliases.","Create one API Gateway and one Lambda function, and use a REST parameter to identify the environment."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway stages and Lambda aliases allow managing multiple environments with single API and function resources, reducing management overhead and cost.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A, B: Creating separate resources increases management complexity\n- D: Using REST parameters for environment separation is an anti-pattern\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q120","q":"A developer registered an AWS Lambda function as a target for an Application Load Balancer (ALB) using a CLI command. However, the Lambda function is not being invoked when the client sends requests through the ALB. Why is the Lambda function not being invoked?","options":["A Lambda function cannot be registered as a target for an ALB.","A Lambda function can be registered with an ALB using AWS Management Console only.","The permissions to invoke the Lambda function are missing.","Cross-zone is not enabled on the ALB."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"When registering Lambda with ALB, the ALB needs permission to invoke the Lambda function via a resource-based policy. This is often missed when using CLI commands.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Lambda can be registered as ALB target\n- B: CLI can register Lambda targets\n- D: Cross-zone load balancing doesn't affect Lambda invocation\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q121","q":"A developer is creating an AWS Lambda function that will connect to an Amazon RDS for MySQL instance. The developer wants to store the database credentials. The database credentials need to be encrypted and the database password needs to be automatically rotated. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Store the database credentials as environment variables for the Lambda function. Set the environment variables to rotate automatically.","Store the database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. Set up managed rotation on the database credentials.","Store the database credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as secure string parameters. Set up managed rotation on the parameters.","Store the database credentials in the X-Amz-Security-Token parameter. Set up managed rotation on the parameter."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Secrets Manager provides automatic rotation for RDS credentials, encryption via KMS, and secure retrieval by Lambda functions.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Environment variables cannot rotate automatically\n- C: Parameter Store doesn't support automatic rotation\n- D: X-Amz-Security-Token is for temporary credentials, not database credentials\n\nTips:\nAccess token / API key / password → AWS Secrets Manager (có rotation). Parameter Store chỉ khi đề nói rõ “ít tốn kém” hoặc “free tier”."},
{"id":"q122","q":"A developer wants to reduce risk when deploying a new version of an existing AWS Lambda function. To test the Lambda function, the developer needs to split the traffic between the existing version and the new version of the Lambda function. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure a weighted routing policy in Amazon Route 53. Associate the versions of the Lambda function with the weighted routing policy.","Create a function alias. Configure the alias to split the traffic between the two versions of the Lambda function.","Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that uses the Lambda function as a target. Configure the ALB to split the traffic between the two versions of the Lambda function.","Create the new version of the Lambda function as a Lambda layer on the existing version. Configure the function to split the traffic between the two layers."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Lambda aliases support traffic shifting between versions, allowing canary or linear deployment strategies for safe testing.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Route53 is for DNS-level routing, not Lambda version routing\n- C: ALB doesn't support Lambda version traffic splitting\n- D: Layers are for code sharing, not traffic routing\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q123","q":"A developer has created a large AWS Lambda function. Deployment of the function is failing because of an InvalidParameterValueException error. The error message indicates that the unzipped size of the function exceeds the maximum supported value. Which actions can the developer take to resolve this error? (Choose two.)","options":["Submit a quota increase request to AWS Support to increase the function to the required size.","Use a compression algorithm that is more efficient than ZIP.","Break up the function into multiple smaller functions.","Zip the .zip file twice to compress the file more.","Move common libraries, function dependencies, and custom runtimes into Lambda layers."],"correct":[2,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Two effective solutions:\n- C: Split large function into smaller, focused functions\n- E: Move dependencies to Lambda layers to reduce deployment package size\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Lambda size limits are fixed and cannot be increased\n- B: Lambda only supports ZIP format\n- D: Double zipping doesn't reduce unzipped size and may cause errors\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q124","q":"A developer is troubleshooting an application in an integration environment. In the application, an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue consumes messages and then an AWS Lambda function processes the messages. The Lambda function transforms the messages and makes an API call to a third-party service. There has been an increase in application usage. The third-party API frequently returns an HTTP 429 Too Many Requests error message. The error message prevents a significant number of messages from being processed successfully. How can the developer resolve this issue?","options":["Increase the SQS event source's batch size setting.","Configure provisioned concurrency for the Lambda function based on the third-party API's documented rate limits.","Increase the retry attempts and maximum event age in the Lambda function's asynchronous configuration.","Configure maximum concurrency on the SQS event source based on the third-party service's documented rate limits."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Setting maximum concurrency on the SQS event source limits how many Lambda functions run concurrently, preventing overwhelming the third-party API.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Larger batches would increase load on the API\n- B: Provisioned concurrency helps with cold starts, not rate limiting\n- C: Retries would continue to hit the rate-limited API\n\nTips:\nCold start: tăng memory (CPU tỷ lệ thuận) → rồi Provisioned Concurrency nếu cần latency ổn định, SnapStart nếu là Java. Provisioned tốn phí cả khi idle."},
{"id":"q125","q":"A company has an online web application that includes a product catalog. The catalog is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket that is named DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET. The application must be able to list the objects in the S3 bucket and must be able to download objects through an IAM policy. Which policy allows MINIMUM access to meet these requirements?","options":["Policy with s3:ListBucket and s3:GetObject permissions","Policy with s3:* permissions","Policy with s3:ListBucket, s3:GetObject, and s3:DeleteObject permissions","Policy with s3:ListBucket permission but denies s3:GetObject"],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Minimum required permissions:\n- s3:ListBucket: To list objects in the bucket\n- s3:GetObject: To download objects\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: s3:* provides excessive permissions\n- C: Includes unnecessary DeleteObject permission\n- D: Denies GetObject, preventing downloads\n\nTips:\nIAM: explicit Deny luôn thắng. Policy cần cả Action + Resource. Với Lambda/ECS hãy dùng execution role, không nhúng access key."},
{"id":"q126","q":"A developer is writing an application to encrypt files outside of AWS before uploading the files to an Amazon S3 bucket. The encryption must be symmetric and must be performed inside the application. How can the developer implement the encryption in the application to meet these requirements?","options":["Create a data key in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use the AWS Encryption SDK to encrypt the files.","Create a Hash-Based Message Authentication Code (HMAC) key in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use the AWS Encryption SDK to encrypt the files.","Create a data key pair in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use the AWS CLI to encrypt the files.","Create a data key in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use the AWS CLI to encrypt the files."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"KMS data keys provide symmetric encryption, and the AWS Encryption SDK enables client-side encryption within the application before uploading to S3.\n\nIncorrect:\n- B: HMAC keys are for authentication, not encryption\n- C: Data key pairs are for asymmetric encryption\n- D: CLI cannot perform client-side encryption within the application\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q127","q":"A developer is working on an application that is deployed on an Amazon EC2 instance. The developer needs a solution that will securely transfer files from the application to an Amazon S3 bucket. What should the developer do to meet these requirements in the MOST secure way?","options":["Create an IAM user. Create an access key for the IAM user. Store the access key in the application's environment variables.","Create an IAM role. Create an access key for the IAM role. Store the access key in the application's environment variables.","Create an IAM role. Configure the IAM role to access the specific Amazon S3 API calls the application requires. Associate the IAM role with the EC2 instance.","Configure an S3 bucket policy for the S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow access for the EC2 instance ID."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"IAM roles for EC2 instances provide temporary credentials that are automatically rotated, eliminating the need to store long-term credentials.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A, B: Storing access keys in environment variables is insecure\n- D: S3 bucket policies alone cannot authenticate EC2 instances\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q128","q":"A developer created a web API that receives requests by using an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an HTTPS listener. The developer configures an Amazon Cognito user pool and wants to ensure that every request to the API is authenticated through Amazon Cognito. What should the developer do to meet this requirement?","options":["Add a listener rule to the listener to return a fixed response if the Authorization header is missing. Set the fixed response to 401 Unauthorized.","Create an authentication action for the listener rules of the ALB. Set the rule action type to authenticate-cognito. Set the OnUnauthenticatedRequest field to 'deny.'","Create an Amazon API Gateway API. Configure all API methods to be forwarded to the ALB endpoint. Create an authorizer of the COGNITO_USER_POOLS type. Configure every API method to use that authorizer.","Create a new target group that includes an AWS Lambda function target that validates the Authorization header by using Amazon Cognito. Associate the target group with the listener."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"ALB has built-in Cognito authentication action that can authenticate requests before they reach the backend. Setting OnUnauthenticatedRequest to 'deny' ensures all requests are authenticated.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Only checks for header presence, not valid authentication\n- C: Adds unnecessary complexity with API Gateway\n- D: Custom Lambda authentication is more complex and less efficient\n\nTips:\nUser pool = authentication (đăng nhập). Identity pool = authorization (đổi token thành credential AWS tạm thời). Đừng lẫn hai vai trò này."},
{"id":"q129","q":"A company recently deployed an AWS Lambda function. A developer notices an increase in the function throttle metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. What are the MOST operationally efficient solutions to reduce the function throttling? (Choose two.)","options":["Migrate the function to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS).","Increase the maximum age of events in Lambda.","Increase the function's reserved concurrency.","Add the lambda:GetFunctionConcurrency action to the execution role.","Request a service quota change for increased concurrency."],"correct":[2,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"Two effective solutions:\n- C: Increase reserved concurrency to guarantee capacity for the function\n- E: Request AWS to increase account-level concurrency limits\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Migration to EKS is operationally complex\n- B: Maximum event age doesn't affect throttling\n- D: GetFunctionConcurrency is for reading limits, not changing them\n\nTips:\nThrottling: kiểm tra (1) concurrency limit với Lambda, (2) hot partition với DynamoDB, (3) capacity mode. Xử lý gốc bằng retry + exponential backoff TRƯỚC khi tăng capacity."},
{"id":"q130","q":"A company is creating a REST service using an Amazon API Gateway with AWS Lambda integration. The service must run different versions for testing purposes. What would be the BEST way to accomplish this?","options":["Use an X-Version header to denote which version is being called and pass that header to the Lambda function(s).","Create an API Gateway Lambda authorizer to route API clients to the correct API version.","Create an API Gateway resource policy to isolate versions and provide context to the Lambda function(s).","Deploy the API versions as unique stages with unique endpoints and use stage variables to provide further context."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway stages provide built-in versioning and isolation with unique endpoints. Stage variables can pass environment context to Lambda functions.\n\nIncorrect:\n- A: Custom headers require application logic and aren't built-in\n- B: Authorizers are for authentication, not version routing\n- C: Resource policies control access, not version management\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q131","q":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline to deliver one of its applications. The delivery pipeline is triggered by changes to the main branch of an AWS CodeCommit repository and uses AWS CodeBuild to implement the test and build stages of the process and AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the application. The pipeline has been operating successfully for several months and there have been no modifications. Following a recent change to the application’s source code, AWS CodeDeploy has not deployed the updated application as expected. What are the possible causes? (Choose two.)","options":["The change was not made in the main branch of the AWS CodeCommit repository.","One of the earlier stages in the pipeline failed and the pipeline has terminated.","One of the Amazon EC2 instances in the company’s AWS CodePipeline cluster is inactive.","The AWS CodePipeline is incorrectly configured and is not invoking AWS CodeDeploy.","AWS CodePipeline does not have permissions to access AWS CodeCommit."],"correct":[0,1],"multi":true,"explanation":"A: The pipeline trigger is configured for the main branch. A change in a different branch will not start the pipeline.\nB: If any stage before CodeDeploy (like CodeBuild) fails, the pipeline stops and CodeDeploy is never invoked.\n\nIncorrect:\nC: CodePipeline does not use an 'EC2 cluster'; it's a workflow service.\nD: The pipeline was working previously, so a configuration error is unlikely.\nE: Permissions were already correctly set for the pipeline to work for months.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q132","q":"A developer is building a serverless application by using AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) on multiple AWS Lambda functions. When the application is deployed, the developer wants to shift 10% of the traffic to the new deployment of the application for the first 10 minutes after deployment. If there are no issues, all traffic must switch over to the new version. Which change to the AWS SAM template will meet these requirements?","options":["Set the Deployment Preference Type to Canary10Percent10Minutes. Set the AutoPublishAlias property to the Lambda alias.","Set the Deployment Preference Type to Linear10PercentEvery10Minutes. Set AutoPublishAlias property to the Lambda alias.","Set the Deployment Preference Type to Canary10Percent10Minutes. Set the PreTraffic and PostTraffic properties to the Lambda alias.","Set the Deployment Preference Type to Linear10PercentEvery10Minutes. Set PreTraffic and PostTraffic properties to the Lambda alias."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Canary10Percent10Minutes immediately shifts 10% of traffic to the new version for 10 minutes before shifting the rest, which matches the requirement exactly. The AutoPublishAlias property is required to manage traffic routing between Lambda versions.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Linear10PercentEvery10Minutes gradually shifts traffic in steps, not immediately shifting 10% for the first 10 minutes.\nC, D: PreTraffic and PostTraffic are for specifying hook functions, not for defining the alias used for traffic shifting.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q133","q":"An AWS Lambda function is running in a company’s shared AWS account. The function needs to perform an additional ec2:DescribeInstances action that is directed at the company’s development accounts. A developer must configure the required permissions across the accounts. How should the developer configure the permissions to adhere to the principle of least privilege?","options":["Create an IAM role in the shared account. Add the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role. Establish a trust relationship between the development accounts for this role. Update the Lambda function IAM role in the shared account by adding the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role.","Create an IAM role in the development accounts. Add the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role. Establish a trust relationship with the shared account for this role. Update the Lambda function IAM role in the shared account by adding the iam:AssumeRole permissions.","Create an IAM role in the shared account. Add the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role. Establish a trust relationship between the development accounts for this role. Update the Lambda function IAM role in the shared account by adding the iam:AssumeRole permissions.","Create an IAM role in the development accounts. Add the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role. Establish a trust relationship with the shared account for this role. Update the Lambda function IAM role in the shared account by adding the ec2:DescribeInstances permission to the role."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"This follows the principle of least privilege and cross-account access best practices. The role with the actual EC2 permissions is created in the development accounts (where the resources are), limiting its scope. The Lambda's role in the shared account only gets the permission to assume that cross-account role.\n\nIncorrect:\nA, D: Granting ec2:DescribeInstances directly to the Lambda's role in the shared account gives it overly broad permissions and violates the principle of least privilege.\nC: The role with EC2 permissions should be in the development accounts, not the shared account.\n\nTips:\nGặp LEAST/FEWEST/MINIMUM → loại phương án cần tự vận hành (EC2, tự build, tự rotate). Dịch vụ managed + fewer moving parts thắng."},
{"id":"q134","q":"A company uses an AWS Lambda function to transfer files from an Amazon S3 bucket to the company's SFTP server. The Lambda function connects to the SFTP server by using credentials such as username and password. The company uses Lambda environment variables to store these credentials. A developer needs to implement encrypted username and password credentials. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Remove the user credentials from the Lambda environment. Implement IAM database authentication.","Move the user credentials from Lambda environment variables to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.","Move the user credentials from Lambda environment variables to AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).","Move the user credentials from the Lambda environment to an encrypted .txt file. Store the file in an S3 bucket."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store is designed for secure, scalable storage of configuration data and secrets. It supports encryption using AWS KMS, providing the required encryption at rest.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: IAM database authentication is not applicable for an external SFTP server.\nC: AWS KMS is a key management service, not a secret storage service. You cannot directly 'store' credentials in KMS.\nD: While S3 can encrypt files, managing a text file is less secure and operationally more complex than using a dedicated secrets service.\n\nTips:\nAccess token / API key / password → AWS Secrets Manager (có rotation). Parameter Store chỉ khi đề nói rõ “ít tốn kém” hoặc “free tier”."},
{"id":"q135","q":"An online sales company is developing a serverless application that runs on AWS. The application uses an AWS Lambda function that calculates order success rates and stores the data in an Amazon DynamoDB table. A developer wants an efficient way to invoke the Lambda function every 15 minutes. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","options":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that has a rate expression that will run the rule every 15 minutes. Add the Lambda function as the target of the EventBridge rule.","Create an AWS Systems Manager document that has a script that will invoke the Lambda function on Amazon EC2. Use a Systems Manager Run Command task to run the shell script every 15 minutes.","Create an AWS Step Functions state machine. Configure the state machine to invoke the Lambda function execution role at a specified interval by using a Wait state. Set the interval to 15 minutes.","Provision a small Amazon EC2 instance. Set up a cron job that invokes the Lambda function every 15 minutes."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Amazon EventBridge (formerly CloudWatch Events) is the native, serverless way to schedule Lambda functions. Creating a rule with a rate expression is simple and requires minimal code or infrastructure management.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, D: These solutions introduce unnecessary infrastructure (EC2, Systems Manager) for a simple scheduling task, increasing operational overhead and cost.\nC: Step Functions is overkill for a simple, periodic invocation and is more complex to set up.\n\nTips:\nNhiều bước tuần tự + retry + xử lý lỗi từng bước → Step Functions (không nhồi hết vào 1 Lambda)."},
{"id":"q136","q":"A company deploys a photo-processing application to an Amazon EC2 instance. The application needs to process each photo in less than 5 seconds. If processing takes longer than 5 seconds, the company’s development team must receive a notification. How can a developer implement the required time measurement and notification with the LEAST operational overhead?","options":["Create an Amazon CloudWatch custom metric. Each time a photo is processed, publish the processing time as a metric value. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is based on a static threshold of 5 seconds. Notify the development team by using an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Each time a photo is processed, publish the processing time to the queue. Create an application to consume from the queue and to determine whether any values are more than 5 seconds. Notify the development team by using an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","Create an Amazon CloudWatch custom metric. Each time a photo is processed, publish the processing time as a metric value. Create a CloudWatch alarm that enters ALARM state if the average of values is greater than 5 seconds. Notify the development team by sending an Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) message.","Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Each time a photo is processed, publish the processing time to the data stream. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that enters ALARM state if any values are more than 5 seconds. Notify the development team by using an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"This solution uses native AWS monitoring services. CloudWatch custom metrics can capture the processing time per photo, and a CloudWatch alarm with a static threshold can trigger an SNS notification for any individual photo that exceeds 5 seconds, which meets the requirement.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: This introduces significant operational overhead by requiring a custom application to process the queue and trigger alerts.\nC: Using an average (e.g., 'Average > 5') might not trigger an alarm for a single slow photo, which violates the requirement.\nD: Kinesis is a complex and costly service for a simple logging and alerting task.\n\nTips:\nGặp LEAST/FEWEST/MINIMUM → loại phương án cần tự vận hành (EC2, tự build, tự rotate). Dịch vụ managed + fewer moving parts thắng."},
{"id":"q137","q":"A company is using AWS Elastic Beanstalk to manage web applications that are running on Amazon EC2 instances. A developer needs to make configuration changes. The developer must deploy the changes to new instances only. Which types of deployment can the developer use to meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","options":["All at once","Immutable","Rolling","Blue/green","Rolling with additional batch"],"correct":[1,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"B (Immutable): This deployment type launches a full new set of instances in a separate Auto Scaling group, verifies their health, and then terminates the old instances. Changes are deployed only to new instances.\nD (Blue/green): This is a technique where a new environment (green) is created and deployed alongside the old one (blue). Traffic is routed to the green environment after testing. This also deploys changes only to new instances.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Deploys to all existing instances simultaneously.\nC, E: These perform rolling updates across existing instances, potentially deploying to a mix of old and new instances.\n\nTips:\nCanary = % traffic nhỏ trước (API Gateway canary, Lambda alias weighted). Blue/Green = môi trường mới rồi switch toàn bộ. Rolling = thay dần từng instance."},
{"id":"q138","q":"A developer needs to use Amazon DynamoDB to store customer orders. The developer’s company requires all customer data to be encrypted at rest with a key that the company generates. What should the developer do to meet these requirements?","options":["Create the DynamoDB table with encryption set to None. Code the application to use the key to decrypt the data when the application reads from the table. Code the application to use the key to encrypt the data when the application writes to the table.","Store the key by using AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Choose an AWS KMS customer managed key during creation of the DynamoDB table. Provide the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AWS KMS key.","Store the key by using AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Create the DynamoDB table with default encryption. Include the kms:Encrypt parameter with the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AWS KMS key when using the DynamoDB software development kit (SDK).","Store the key by using AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Choose an AWS KMS AWS managed key during creation of the DynamoDB table. Provide the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AWS KMS key."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"DynamoDB supports encryption at rest using AWS KMS. Choosing a 'customer managed key' allows the company to generate and manage their own key, which meets the requirement. Specifying this key during table creation ensures all data is encrypted with it.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Client-side encryption adds complexity and is error-prone. It's not necessary when DynamoDB provides built-in server-side encryption.\nC: Default encryption uses an AWS-managed key, not a company-generated one. The kms:Encrypt parameter in the SDK is for client-side operations, not for configuring table-level encryption.\nD: An AWS managed key is generated and managed by AWS, not by the company.\n\nTips:\n“Encrypted at rest” luôn cần KMS (SSE-KMS cho S3/EBS, KMS cho DynamoDB). Nếu đề hỏi thêm cross-account → nhớ bucket policy / key policy."},
{"id":"q139","q":"A company uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy an application that uses an Amazon API Gateway REST API with AWS Lambda function integration. The application uses Amazon DynamoDB for data persistence. The application has three stages: development, testing, and production. Each stage uses its own DynamoDB table. The company has encountered unexpected issues when promoting changes to the production stage. The changes were successful in the development and testing stages. A developer needs to route 20% of the traffic to the new production stage API with the next production release. The developer needs to route the remaining 80% of the traffic to the existing production stage. The solution must minimize the number of errors that any single customer experiences. Which approach should the developer take to meet these requirements?","options":["Update 20% of the planned changes to the production stage. Deploy the new production stage. Monitor the results. Repeat this process five times to test all planned changes.","Update the Amazon Route 53 DNS record entry for the production stage API to use a weighted routing policy. Set the weight to a value of 80. Add a second record for the production domain name. Change the second routing policy to a weighted routing policy. Set the weight of the second policy to a value of 20. Change the alias of the second policy to use the testing stage API.","Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the REST API. Change the production API Amazon Route 53 record to point traffic to the ALB. Register the production and testing stages as targets of the ALB with weights of 80% and 20%, respectively.","Configure canary settings for the production stage API. Change the percentage of traffic directed to canary deployment to 20%. Make the planned updates to the production stage. Deploy the changes"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway has built-in canary deployment features. This allows you to safely roll out changes by routing a specified percentage of traffic (e.g., 20%) to a new version of the API stage. If errors occur, they only affect the small percentage of users in the canary, minimizing impact. It's the most direct and native way to achieve this with API Gateway.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Manually deploying changes in parts is risky, error-prone, and does not guarantee that only 20% of users are affected.\nB: This incorrectly routes traffic to the testing stage API, not a new version of the production stage. It also doesn't use the native capabilities of API Gateway.\nC: Introducing an ALB is an unnecessary complexity. API Gateway is already the entry point and has its own traffic splitting capabilities.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q140","q":"A developer has created a data collection application that uses Amazon API Gateway, AWS Lambda, and Amazon S3. The application’s users periodically upload data files and wait for the validation status to be reflected on a processing dashboard. The validation process is complex and time-consuming for large files. Some users are uploading dozens of large files and have to wait and refresh the processing dashboard to see if the files have been validated. The developer must refactor the application to immediately update the validation result on the user’s dashboard without reloading the full dashboard. What is the MOST operationally efficient solution that meets these requirements?","options":["Integrate the client with an API Gateway WebSocket API. Save the user-uploaded files with the WebSocket connection ID. Push the validation status to the connection ID when the processing is complete to initiate an update of the user interface.","Launch an Amazon EC2 micro instance, and set up a WebSocket server. Send the user-uploaded file and user detail to the EC2 instance after the user uploads the file. Use the WebSocket server to send updates to the user interface when the uploaded file is processed.","Save the user’s email address along with the user-uploaded file. When the validation process is complete, send an email notification through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to the user who uploaded the file.","Save the user-uploaded file and user detail to Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon DynamoDB Streams with Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) push notifications to send updates to the browser to update the user interface."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway WebSocket API provides a persistent, full-duplex connection between the client and server. This allows the backend (Lambda) to push real-time updates (like validation status) directly to the specific user's dashboard as soon as processing is complete, without the need for the user to refresh. It's a fully managed service, offering high operational efficiency.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Managing a self-hosted WebSocket server on EC2 introduces significant operational overhead (patching, scaling, monitoring) compared to a managed service like API Gateway.\nC: Email does not provide an immediate update on the dashboard; it requires the user to check their email and then refresh the dashboard.\nD: While DynamoDB Streams can trigger events, pushing notifications to a web browser typically requires a service like WebSockets or IoT Core. This architecture is more complex and less direct than using a WebSocket API.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q141","q":"A developer is creating a new batch application that will run on an Amazon EC2 instance. The application requires read access to an Amazon S3 bucket. The developer needs to follow security best practices to grant S3 read access to the application. Which solution meets these requirements?","options":["Add the permissions to an IAM policy. Attach the policy to a role. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.","Add the permissions inline to an IAM group. Attach the group to the EC2 instance profile.","Add the permissions to an IAM policy. Attach the policy to a user. Attach the user to the EC2 instance profile.","Add the permissions to an IAM policy. Use IAM web identity federation to access the S3 bucket with the policy."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Using an IAM role attached to an EC2 instance profile is the security best practice. It allows the application to get temporary credentials automatically and avoids storing long-term access keys on the instance.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: IAM groups cannot be attached to EC2 instance profiles. Groups are for organizing IAM users.\nC: IAM users should not be used for EC2 applications. This requires storing access keys on the instance, which is a security risk.\nD: Web identity federation is for web/mobile applications, not for applications running on EC2 instances.\n\nTips:\nIAM: explicit Deny luôn thắng. Policy cần cả Action + Resource. Với Lambda/ECS hãy dùng execution role, không nhúng access key."},
{"id":"q142","q":"A company has migrated an application to Amazon EC2 instances. Automatic scaling is working well for the application user interface. However, the process to deliver shipping requests to the company's warehouse staff is encountering issues. Duplicate shipping requests are arriving, and some requests are lost or arrive out of order. The company must avoid duplicate shipping requests and must process the requests in the order that the requests arrive. Requests are never more than 250 KB in size and take 5-10 minutes to process. A developer needs to rearchitect the application to improve the reliability of the delivery and processing of the requests. What should the developer do to meet these requirements?","options":["Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to process the requests. Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Modify the application to write the requests to the Kinesis data stream.","Create an AWS Lambda function to process the requests. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the Lambda function to the SNS topic. Modify the application to write the requests to the SNS topic.","Create an AWS Lambda function to process the requests. Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. Set the SQS queue as an event source for the Lambda function. Modify the application to write the requests to the SQS queue.","Create an AWS Lambda function to process the requests. Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) FIFO queue. Set the SQS queue as an event source for the Lambda function. Modify the application to write the requests to the SQS queue."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"An SQS FIFO queue provides exactly-once processing and first-in-first-out (FIFO) delivery, which prevents duplicates and ensures order. The 5-10 minute processing time is compatible with Lambda's maximum timeout of 15 minutes.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Kinesis is complex for this use case and doesn't guarantee exactly-once processing like SQS FIFO.\nB: SNS does not guarantee order or prevent duplicates, and it doesn't queue messages.\nC: SQS standard queue does not guarantee FIFO order and may deliver duplicates.\n\nTips:\nStreaming: Kinesis Data Streams khi cần tự xử lý/nhiều consumer; Firehose khi chỉ cần đổ dữ liệu vào S3/Redshift/OpenSearch (near real-time, không quản shard)."},
{"id":"q143","q":"A developer is creating a machine learning (ML) pipeline in AWS Step Functions that contains AWS Lambda functions. The developer has configured an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue to deliver ML model parameters to the ML pipeline to train ML models. The developer uploads the trained models are uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. The developer needs a solution that can locally test the ML pipeline without making service integration calls to Amazon SQS and Amazon S3. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Use the Amazon CodeGuru Profiler to analyze the Lambda functions used in the AWS Step Functions pipeline.","Use the AWS Step Functions Local Docker Image to run and locally test the Lambda functions.","Use the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) CLI to run and locally test the Lambda functions.","Use AWS Step Functions Local with mocked service integrations."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS Step Functions Local allows you to run and test state machines locally. It supports mocking AWS service integrations (like SQS and S3), which is exactly what's needed to test without making actual calls to these services.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: CodeGuru Profiler is for performance analysis, not for local testing of workflows.\nB: The Step Functions Local Docker image alone doesn't specify mocking, which is the key requirement.\nC: AWS SAM CLI is great for testing Lambda functions locally but doesn't provide the same workflow testing with mocked integrations as Step Functions Local.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q144","q":"A company runs a batch processing application by using AWS Lambda functions and Amazon API Gateway APIs with deployment stages for development, user acceptance testing, and production. A development team needs to configure the APIs in the deployment stages to connect to third-party service endpoints. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options":["Store the third-party service endpoints in Lambda layers that correspond to the stage.","Store the third-party service endpoints in API Gateway stage variables that correspond to the stage.","Encode the third-party service endpoints as query parameters in the API Gateway request URL.","Store the third-party service endpoint for each environment in AWS AppConfig."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway stage variables are key-value pairs that can be used to pass configuration to the backend. They are perfect for storing environment-specific endpoints and can be accessed in mapping templates or passed to Lambda.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Lambda layers are for sharing code and dependencies, not for environment configuration.\nC: Hardcoding endpoints in query parameters is not secure, manageable, or scalable.\nD: While AppConfig can store configuration, it's not natively integrated with API Gateway stages like stage variables are.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q145","q":"A developer is building a serverless application that runs on AWS. The developer wants to create an accelerated development workflow that deploys incremental changes to AWS for testing. The developer wants to deploy the incremental changes but does not want to fully deploy the entire application to AWS for every code commit. What should the developer do to meet these requirements?","options":["Use the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) to build the application. Use the sam sync command to deploy the incremental changes.","Use the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) to build the application. Use the sam init command to deploy the incremental changes.","Use the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) to build the application. Use the cdk synth command to deploy the incremental changes.","Use the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) to build the application. Use the cdk bootstrap command to deploy the incremental changes."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"The `sam sync` command is specifically designed for accelerated development workflows. It quickly deploys code changes directly to AWS without going through a full CloudFormation deployment, making it ideal for testing incremental changes.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: `sam init` is for initializing a new SAM project, not for deployment.\nC: `cdk synth` only synthesizes a CloudFormation template; it doesn't deploy anything.\nD: `cdk bootstrap` is for preparing an environment for CDK deployment, not for deploying incremental changes.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q146","q":"A developer is building an application that will use an Amazon API Gateway API with an AWS Lambda backend. The team that will develop the frontend requires immediate access to the API endpoints to build the UI. To prepare the backend application for integration, the developer needs to set up endpoints. The endpoints need to return predefined HTTP status codes and JSON responses for the frontend team. The developer creates a method for an API resource. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Set the integration type to AWS_PROXY. Provision Lambda functions to return hardcoded JSON data.","Set the integration type to MOCK. Configure the method's integration request and integration response to associate a JSON responses with specific HTTP status codes.","Set the integration type to HTTP_PROXY. Configure API Gateway to pass all requests to an external placeholder API. which the team will build.","Set the integration type to MOCK. Use a method request to define HTTP status codes. Use an integration request to define JSON responses."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"The MOCK integration type allows API Gateway to return responses without calling any backend. By configuring integration responses, you can map different HTTP status codes to specific JSON response templates, providing the frontend team with immediate, predefined API endpoints.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: AWS_PROXY requires an actual Lambda function, which contradicts the requirement for immediate access without a backend.\nC: HTTP_PROXY requires an existing backend HTTP endpoint.\nD: Method request defines client input, not server responses. Integration request transforms incoming requests, while integration response handles outgoing responses.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q147","q":"A developer is migrating an application to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The developer migrates the application to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) with an EKS cluster. As part of the application migration to a new backend, the developer creates a new AWS account. The developer makes configuration changes to the application to point the application to the new AWS account and to use new backend resources. The developer successfully tests the changes within the application by deploying the pipeline. The Docker image build and the pipeline deployment are successful, but the application is still connecting to the old backend. The developer finds that the application's configuration is still referencing the original EKS cluster and not referencing the new backend resources. Which reason can explain why the application is not connecting to the new resources?","options":["The developer did not successfully create the new AWS account.","The developer added a new tag to the Docker image.","The developer did not update the Docker image tag to a new version.","The developer pushed the changes to a new Docker image tag."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"If the Docker image tag in the Kubernetes deployment manifest wasn't updated, Kubernetes will continue using the previous cached image with the old configuration. The new image with the updated backend configuration won't be pulled and deployed.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: The pipeline deployment was successful, indicating the new account was created properly.\nB: Adding a new tag doesn't help if the deployment isn't updated to use that tag.\nD: Pushing to a new tag is correct, but if the deployment isn't updated to reference that new tag, it won't take effect.\n\nTips:\nContainer image → ECR; chạy container không muốn quản server → Fargate. Nếu đề nhắc Kubernetes API/manifest → EKS."},
{"id":"q148","q":"A developer is creating an application that reads and writes to multiple Amazon S3 buckets. The application will be deployed to an Amazon EC2 instance. The developer wants to make secure API requests from the EC2 instances without the need to manage the security credentials for the application. The developer needs to apply the principle of least privilege. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create an IAM user. Create access keys and secret keys for the user. Associate the user with an IAM policy that allows s3:* permissions.","Associate the EC2 instance with an IAM role that has an IAM policy that allows s3:ListBucket and s3:*Object permissions for specific S3 buckets.","Associate the EC2 instance with an IAM role that has an AmazonS3FullAccess AWS managed policy.","Create a bucket policy on the S3 bucket that allows s3:ListBucket and s3:*Object permissions to the EC2 instance."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Using an IAM role attached to the EC2 instance follows security best practices by providing temporary credentials. The policy grants only the necessary permissions (ListBucket and *Object) for specific buckets, adhering to the principle of least privilege.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Using IAM user credentials on EC2 instances is insecure and violates best practices.\nC: AmazonS3FullAccess provides overly broad permissions, violating the principle of least privilege.\nD: Bucket policies manage access from the resource side, but using IAM roles is the preferred method for EC2 instances.\n\nTips:\nGặp LEAST/FEWEST/MINIMUM → loại phương án cần tự vận hành (EC2, tự build, tự rotate). Dịch vụ managed + fewer moving parts thắng."},
{"id":"q149","q":"A company has an application that receives batches of orders from partners every day. The application uses an AWS Lambda function to process the batches. If a batch contains no orders, the Lambda function must publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as soon as possible. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement with the LEAST implementation effort? (Choose two.)","options":["Update the existing Lambda function's code to send an Amazon CloudWatch custom metric for the number of orders in a batch for each partner.","Create a new Lambda function as an Amazon Kinesis data stream consumer. Configure the new Lambda function to track orders and to publish to the SNS topic when a batch contains no orders.","Set up an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that will send a notification to the SNS topic when the value of the custom metric is 0.","Schedule a new Lambda function to analyze Amazon CloudWatch metrics every 24 hours to identify batches that contain no orders. Configure the Lambda function to publish to the SNS topic.","Modify the existing Lambda function to log orders to an Amazon Kinesis data stream."],"correct":[0,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"This solution requires minimal changes: update the existing Lambda to emit a custom metric (A), then create a CloudWatch alarm that triggers SNS when the metric is 0 (C). This leverages existing services without introducing new complex components.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, E: Introducing Kinesis adds unnecessary complexity for a simple monitoring task.\nD: Checking every 24 hours doesn't meet the 'as soon as possible' requirement.\n\nTips:\nStreaming: Kinesis Data Streams khi cần tự xử lý/nhiều consumer; Firehose khi chỉ cần đổ dữ liệu vào S3/Redshift/OpenSearch (near real-time, không quản shard)."},
{"id":"q150","q":"A company runs an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances open connections to an Amazon RDS for SQL Server database. A developer needs to store and access the credentials and wants to automatically rotate the credentials. The developer does not want to store the credentials for the database in the code. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST secure way?","options":["Create an IAM role that has permissions to access the database. Attach the IAM role to the EC2 instances.","Store the credentials as secrets in AWS Secrets Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function to update the secrets and the database. Retrieve the credentials from Secrets Manager as needed.","Store the credentials in an encrypted text file in an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the EC2 instance launch template to download the credentials from Amazon S3 as the instance launches. Create an AWS Lambda function to update the secrets and the database.","Store the credentials in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch Events rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to periodically update the secrets and database."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS Secrets Manager is specifically designed for secure secret storage with built-in rotation capabilities. It can automatically rotate RDS credentials and update both the secret and the database, providing the most secure and managed solution.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: IAM roles don't work for SQL Server authentication; they're for AWS service authentication.\nC: S3 is not designed for secret storage and doesn't provide built-in rotation.\nD: DynamoDB doesn't provide encryption or rotation features out-of-the-box like Secrets Manager does.\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q151","q":"A developer manages a website that distributes its content by using Amazon CloudFront. The website's static artifacts are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The developer deploys some changes and can see the new artifacts in the S3 bucket. However, the changes do not appear on the webpage that the CloudFront distribution delivers. How should the developer resolve this issue?","options":["Configure S3 Object Lock to update to the latest version of the files every time an S3 object is updated.","Configure the S3 bucket to clear all old objects from the bucket before new artifacts are uploaded.","Set CloudFront to invalidate the cache after the artifacts have been deployed to Amazon S3.","Set CloudFront to modify the distribution origin after the artifacts have been deployed to Amazon S3."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"CloudFront caches content at edge locations. After updating objects in S3, you must invalidate the cache to force CloudFront to fetch the latest version from the origin. This is the standard solution for this scenario.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: S3 Object Lock is for retention policies, not cache management.\nB: Clearing old objects doesn't affect cached content in CloudFront.\nD: Changing the distribution origin is unnecessary and disruptive; the origin is still the same S3 bucket.\n\nTips:\nDAX chỉ tăng tốc ĐỌC DynamoDB. ElastiCache cho cache tầng ứng dụng (Redis: persistence/pub-sub; Memcached: đơn giản, multi-thread)."},
{"id":"q152","q":"A developer manages three AWS accounts. Each account contains an Amazon RDS DB instance in a private subnet. The developer needs to define users in each database in a consistent way. The developer must ensure that the same users are created and updated later in all three accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","options":["Create an AWS CloudFormation template. Declare the users in the template. Attach the users to the database. Deploy the template in each account.","Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains a custom resource to create the users in the database. Deploy the template in each account.","Write a script that creates the users. Deploy an Amazon EC2 instance in each account to run the script on the databases. Run the script in each account.","Implement an AWS Lambda function that creates the users in the database. Provide the function with the details of all three accounts."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"A CloudFormation template with a custom resource allows you to define database users as infrastructure-as-code. The custom resource can execute Lambda functions to run SQL commands. This provides consistency, repeatability, and easy updates across all accounts.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Standard CloudFormation cannot directly create database users; it needs a custom resource.\nC: Using EC2 instances for this creates unnecessary infrastructure and operational overhead.\nD: A single Lambda function accessing multiple accounts is complex and less secure than account-specific deployments.\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q153","q":"A company is building a new application that runs on AWS and uses Amazon API Gateway to expose APIs. Teams of developers are working on separate components of the application in parallel. The company wants to publish an API without an integrated backend so that teams that depend on the application backend can continue the development work before the API backend development is complete. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create API Gateway resources and set the integration type value to MOCK. Configure the method integration request and integration response to associate a response with an HTTP status code. Create an API Gateway stage and deploy the API.","Create an AWS Lambda function that returns mocked responses and various HTTP status codes. Create API Gateway resources and set the integration type value to AWS_PROXY. Deploy the API.","Create an EC2 application that returns mocked HTTP responses. Create API Gateway resources and set the integration type value to AWS. Create an API Gateway stage and deploy the API.","Create API Gateway resources and set the integration type value set to HTTP_PROXY. Add mapping templates and deploy the API. Create an AWS Lambda layer that returns various HTTP status codes. Associate the Lambda layer with the API deployment."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway MOCK integration allows you to create API endpoints that return predefined responses without any backend. This is perfect for frontend development while the backend is still being built.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, C: These require actual backend infrastructure (Lambda or EC2), which defeats the purpose of having no backend.\nD: HTTP_PROXY requires an existing HTTP endpoint, and Lambda layers are for code sharing, not for creating mock responses.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q154","q":"An application that runs on AWS receives messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue and processes the messages in batches. The application sends the data to another SQS queue to be consumed by another legacy application. The legacy system can take up to 5 minutes to process some transaction data. A developer wants to ensure that there are no out-of-order updates in the legacy system. The developer cannot alter the behavior of the legacy system. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Use an SQS FIFO queue. Configure the visibility timeout value.","Use an SQS standard queue with a SendMessageBatchRequestEntry data type. Configure the DelaySeconds values.","Use an SQS standard queue with a SendMessageBatchRequestEntry data type. Configure the visibility timeout value.","Use an SQS FIFO queue. Configure the DelaySeconds value."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"SQS FIFO queues guarantee exactly-once processing and first-in-first-out delivery. Setting the visibility timeout longer than the maximum processing time (5+ minutes) ensures messages aren't reprocessed if the legacy system takes a long time.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, C: Standard queues don't guarantee ordering and may deliver messages out of order.\nD: DelaySeconds delays message delivery but doesn't solve ordering or duplication issues.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q155","q":"A company is building a compute-intensive application that will run on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application uses attached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes for storing data. The Amazon EBS volumes will be created at time of initial deployment. The application will process sensitive information. All of the data must be encrypted. The solution should not impact the application's performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure the fleet of EC2 instances to use encrypted EBS volumes to store data.","Configure the application to write all data to an encrypted Amazon S3 bucket.","Configure a custom encryption algorithm for the application that will encrypt and decrypt all data.","Configure an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) that has an encrypted root volume and store the data to ephemeral disks."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"EBS encryption provides encryption at rest with minimal performance impact. The encryption is handled at the infrastructure level, transparent to the application, making it ideal for compute-intensive workloads.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: S3 is object storage, not suitable for the block storage requirements of a compute-intensive application.\nC: Custom encryption adds complexity and can significantly impact performance.\nD: Ephemeral disks lose data when instances stop, and encrypted root volumes don't protect data volumes.\n\nTips:\nContainer image → ECR; chạy container không muốn quản server → Fargate. Nếu đề nhắc Kubernetes API/manifest → EKS."},
{"id":"q156","q":"A developer is updating the production version of an AWS Lambda function to fix a defect. The developer has tested the updated code in a test environment. The developer wants to slowly roll out the updates to a small subset of production users before rolling out the changes to all users. Only 10% of the users should be initially exposed to the new code in production. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Update the Lambda code and create a new version of the Lambda function. Create a Lambda function trigger. Configure the traffic weights in the trigger between the two Lambda function versions. Send 90% of the traffic to the production version, and send 10% of the traffic to the new version.","Create a new Lambda function that uses the updated code. Create a Lambda alias for the production Lambda function. Configure the Lambda alias to send 90% of the traffic to the production Lambda function, and send 10% of the traffic to the test Lambda function.","Update the Lambda code and create a new version of the Lambda function. Create a Lambda proxy integration. Configure the Lambda proxy to split traffic between the two Lambda function versions. Send 90% of the traffic to the production version, and send 10% of the traffic to the new version.","Update the Lambda code and create a new version of the Lambda function. Create a Lambda function alias. Configure the traffic weights in the Lambda alias between the two Lambda function versions. Send 90% of the traffic to the production version, and send 10% of the traffic to the new version."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Lambda aliases support traffic shifting between versions. You can create an alias that points to multiple versions with specific weights, allowing gradual rollout from 10% to 100%.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Triggers don't control traffic splitting between versions; aliases do.\nB: Creating separate functions is unnecessary; versions within the same function are better for canary deployments.\nC: Lambda proxy integration is for API Gateway, not for version traffic management.\n\nTips:\nCanary = % traffic nhỏ trước (API Gateway canary, Lambda alias weighted). Blue/Green = môi trường mới rồi switch toàn bộ. Rolling = thay dần từng instance."},
{"id":"q157","q":"A developer is creating an AWS Lambda function that consumes messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. The developer notices that the Lambda function processes some messages multiple times. How should developer resolve this issue MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Change the Amazon SQS standard queue to an Amazon SQS FIFO queue by using the Amazon SQS message deduplication ID.","Set up a dead-letter queue.","Set the maximum concurrency limit of the AWS Lambda function to 1.","Change the message processing to use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams instead of Amazon SQS."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"SQS FIFO queues provide exactly-once processing and prevent duplicates using message deduplication IDs. This directly solves the duplicate processing issue in the most straightforward way.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Dead-letter queues handle failed messages, not duplicates.\nC: Setting concurrency to 1 eliminates parallelism and doesn't guarantee no duplicates.\nD: Kinesis is more expensive and complex than SQS for this use case.\n\nTips:\nLỗi xử lý lặp lại → DLQ + maxReceiveCount. Lambda async tự retry 2 lần; muốn kiểm soát tốt hơn thì dùng on-failure destination. Luôn thiết kế idempotent."},
{"id":"q158","q":"A developer is optimizing an AWS Lambda function and wants to test the changes in production on a small percentage of all traffic. The Lambda function serves requests to a REST API in Amazon API Gateway. The developer needs to deploy their changes and perform a test in production without changing the API Gateway URL. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Define a function version for the currently deployed production Lambda function. Update the API Gateway endpoint to reference the new Lambda function version. Upload and publish the optimized Lambda function code. On the production API Gateway stage, define a canary release and set the percentage of traffic to direct to the canary release. Update the API Gateway endpoint to use the $LATEST version of the Lambda function. Publish the API to the canary stage.","Define a function version for the currently deployed production Lambda function. Update the API Gateway endpoint to reference the new Lambda function version. Upload and publish the optimized Lambda function code. Update the API Gateway endpoint to use the $LATEST version of the Lambda function. Deploy a new API Gateway stage.","Define an alias on the $LATEST version of the Lambda function. Update the API Gateway endpoint to reference the new Lambda function alias. Upload and publish the optimized Lambda function code. On the production API Gateway stage, define a canary release and set the percentage of traffic to direct to the canary release. Update the API Gateway endpoint to use the $LATEST version of the Lambda function. Publish to the canary stage.","Define a function version for the currently deployed production Lambda function. Update the API Gateway endpoint to reference the new Lambda function version. Upload and publish the optimized Lambda function code. Update the API Gateway endpoint to use the $LATEST version of the Lambda function. Deploy the API to the production API Gateway stage."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway canary releases allow routing a percentage of traffic to a different deployment while keeping the same URL. This combined with Lambda versioning provides a safe way to test changes on a subset of production traffic.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, D: These don't use canary releases and would affect all traffic.\nC: Using $LATEST directly in production is not recommended; versions provide better stability.\n\nTips:\nCanary = % traffic nhỏ trước (API Gateway canary, Lambda alias weighted). Blue/Green = môi trường mới rồi switch toàn bộ. Rolling = thay dần từng instance."},
{"id":"q159","q":"A company notices that credentials that the company uses to connect to an external software as a service (SaaS) vendor are stored in a configuration file as plaintext. The developer needs to secure the API credentials and enforce automatic credentials rotation on a quarterly basis. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST securely?","options":["Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to encrypt the configuration file. Decrypt the configuration file when users make API calls to the SaaS vendor. Enable rotation.","Retrieve temporary credentials from AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) every 15 minutes. Use the temporary credentials when users make API calls to the SaaS vendor.","Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and enable rotation. Configure the API to have Secrets Manager access.","Store the credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and enable rotation. Retrieve the credentials when users make API calls to the SaaS vendor."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS Secrets Manager is specifically designed for secure secret storage with built-in rotation capabilities. It can automatically rotate credentials and provides fine-grained access control.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: KMS only provides encryption, not secret management or rotation features.\nB: STS provides temporary AWS credentials, not for third-party SaaS credentials.\nD: Parameter Store can store secrets but doesn't have built-in rotation like Secrets Manager.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q160","q":"A company has an application that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances. The application stores objects in an Amazon S3 bucket and allows users to download objects from the S3 bucket. A developer turns on S3 Block Public Access for the S3 bucket. After this change, users report errors when they attempt to download objects. The developer needs to implement a solution so that only users who are signed in to the application can access objects in the S3 bucket. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements in the MOST secure way? (Choose two.)","options":["Create an EC2 instance profile and role with an appropriate policy. Associate the role with the EC2 instances.","Create an IAM user with an appropriate policy. Store the access key ID and secret access key on the EC2 instances.","Modify the application to use the S3 GeneratePresignedUrl API call.","Modify the application to use the S3 GetObject API call and to return the object handle to the user.","Modify the application to delegate requests to the S3 bucket."],"correct":[0,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"A: Using an IAM role with EC2 instance profile is the secure way to grant permissions to the application without storing credentials.\nC: Pre-signed URLs provide temporary, time-limited access to specific S3 objects, ensuring only authenticated users can download files.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Storing IAM user credentials on EC2 instances is insecure and violates best practices.\nD: GetObject API call doesn't provide the granular access control needed.\nE: Delegating requests is vague and doesn't ensure secure access control.\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q161","q":"An Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue serves as an event source for an AWS Lambda function. In the SQS queue, each item corresponds to a video file that the Lambda function must convert to a smaller resolution. The Lambda function is timing out on longer video files, but the Lambda function's timeout is already configured to its maximum value. What should a developer do to avoid the timeouts without additional code changes?","options":["Increase the memory configuration of the Lambda function.","Increase the visibility timeout on the SQS queue.","Increase the instance size of the host that runs the Lambda function.","Use multi-threading for the conversion."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Increasing Lambda memory also proportionally increases CPU power, which can help process videos faster and avoid timeouts. This requires no code changes.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Visibility timeout only affects how long messages are hidden from other consumers, not processing speed.\nC: Lambda doesn't run on user-managed EC2 instances.\nD: Multi-threading requires code changes, which violates the requirement.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q162","q":"A company is building an application on AWS. The application's backend includes an Amazon API Gateway REST API. The company's frontend application developers cannot continue work until the backend API is ready for integration. The company needs a solution that will allow the frontend application developers to continue their work. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","options":["Configure mock integrations for API Gateway API methods.","Integrate a Lambda function with API Gateway and return a mocked response.","Add new API endpoints to the API Gateway stage and returns a mocked response.","Configure a proxy resource for API Gateway API methods."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"API Gateway mock integrations allow creating API endpoints that return predefined responses without any backend implementation. This is the fastest and most operationally efficient way to provide frontend developers with working API endpoints.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, C: These require actual backend components (Lambda or additional endpoints), which defeats the purpose of having no backend ready.\nD: Proxy resources require an actual backend endpoint to proxy to.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q163","q":"A company is preparing to migrate an application to the company's first AWS environment. Before this migration, a developer is creating a proof-of-concept application to validate a model for building and deploying container-based applications on AWS. Which combination of steps should the developer take to deploy the containerized proof-of-concept application with the LEAST operational effort? (Choose two.)","options":["Package the application into a .zip file by using a command line tool. Upload the package to Amazon S3.","Package the application into a container image by using the Docker CLI. Upload the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR).","Deploy the application to an Amazon EC2 instance by using AWS CodeDeploy.","Deploy the application to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) on AWS Fargate.","Deploy the application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate."],"correct":[1,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"B: Packaging into a container image and uploading to ECR is the standard way to prepare containerized applications.\nE: ECS on Fargate provides serverless container deployment with minimal operational overhead, as AWS manages the underlying infrastructure.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: .zip files are for Lambda functions, not containerized applications.\nC: EC2 with CodeDeploy requires managing the underlying infrastructure.\nD: EKS is more complex than ECS and requires more operational effort.\n\nTips:\nGặp LEAST/FEWEST/MINIMUM → loại phương án cần tự vận hành (EC2, tự build, tự rotate). Dịch vụ managed + fewer moving parts thắng."},
{"id":"q164","q":"A developer supports an application that accesses data in an Amazon DynamoDB table. One of the item attributes is expirationDate in the timestamp format. The application uses this attribute to find items, archive them, and remove them from the table based on the timestamp value. The application will be decommissioned soon, and the developer must find another way to implement this functionality. The developer needs a solution that will require the least amount of code to write. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Enable TTL on the expirationDate attribute in the table. Create a DynamoDB stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to process the deleted items. Create a DynamoDB trigger for the Lambda function.","Create two AWS Lambda functions: one to delete the items and one to process the items. Create a DynamoDB stream. Use the DeleteItem API operation to delete the items based on the expirationDate attribute. Use the GetRecords API operation to get the items from the DynamoDB stream and process them.","Create two AWS Lambda functions: one to delete the items and one to process the items. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda functions. Use the DeleteItem API operation to delete the items based on the expirationDate attribute. Use the GetRecords API operation to get the items from the DynamoDB table and process them.","Enable TTL on the expirationDate attribute in the table. Specify an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue as the target to delete the items. Create an AWS Lambda function to process the items."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"DynamoDB TTL automatically deletes expired items based on the timestamp attribute. Combined with DynamoDB Streams and Lambda, this provides a complete solution with minimal code - just enable TTL and create a simple Lambda function to process the archived items.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, C: These require writing custom deletion logic and are more complex.\nD: SQS dead-letter queue is not the correct target for TTL deletions; DynamoDB Streams should be used.\n\nTips:\nLỗi xử lý lặp lại → DLQ + maxReceiveCount. Lambda async tự retry 2 lần; muốn kiểm soát tốt hơn thì dùng on-failure destination. Luôn thiết kế idempotent."},
{"id":"q165","q":"A developer needs to implement a custom machine learning (ML) library in an application. The size of the library is 15 GB. The size of the library is increasing. The application uses AWS Lambda functions. All the Lambda functions must have access to the library. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Save the library in Lambda layers. Attach the layers to all Lambda functions.","Save the library in Amazon S3. Download the library from Amazon S3 inside the Lambda function.","Save the library as a Lambda container image. Redeploy the Lambda functions with the new image.","Save the library in an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Mount the EFS file system in all the Lambda functions."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"EFS can store large libraries (15GB+) and can be mounted to multiple Lambda functions, providing shared access. It supports growing sizes and doesn't have the deployment package size limitations of Lambda layers or container images.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Lambda layers have a 250MB size limit.\nB: Downloading 15GB from S3 on each invocation would be extremely slow and expensive.\nC: Lambda container images have a 10GB size limit.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q166","q":"A developer is designing a serverless application for a game in which users register and log in through a web browser. The application makes requests on behalf of users to a set of AWS Lambda functions that run behind an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API. The developer needs to implement a solution to register and log in users on the application's sign-in page. The solution must minimize operational overhead and must minimize ongoing management of user identities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Create Amazon Cognito user pools for external social identity providers. Configure IAM roles for the identity pools.","Program the sign-in page to create users' IAM groups with the IAM roles attached to the groups.","Create an Amazon RDS for SQL Server DB instance to store the users and manage the permissions to the backend resources in AWS.","Configure the sign-in page to register and store the users and their passwords in an Amazon DynamoDB table with an attached IAM policy."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Amazon Cognito provides managed user identity services with minimal operational overhead. It supports social identity providers and can provide temporary AWS credentials via identity pools.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Creating IAM groups for each user is not scalable and violates IAM best practices.\nC: Managing a database for user identities creates significant operational overhead.\nD: Storing passwords in DynamoDB is insecure and requires custom authentication logic.\n\nTips:\nUser pool = authentication (đăng nhập). Identity pool = authorization (đổi token thành credential AWS tạm thời). Đừng lẫn hai vai trò này."},
{"id":"q167","q":"A company has a web application that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances are configured to stream logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company needs to receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification when the number of application error messages exceeds a defined threshold within a 5-minute period. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Rewrite the application code to stream application logs to Amazon SNS. Configure an SNS topic to send a notification when the number of errors exceeds the defined threshold within a 5-minute period.","Configure a subscription filter on the CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure the filter to send an SNS notification when the number of errors exceeds the defined threshold within a 5-minute period.","Install and configure the Amazon Inspector agent on the EC2 instances to monitor for errors. Configure Amazon Inspector to send an SNS notification when the number of errors exceeds the defined threshold within a 5-minute period.","Create a CloudWatch metric filter to match the application error pattern in the log data. Set up a CloudWatch alarm based on the new custom metric. Configure the alarm to send an SNS notification when the number of errors exceeds the defined threshold within a 5-minute period."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"CloudWatch metric filters can extract specific patterns from log data and create custom metrics. Combined with CloudWatch alarms, this can trigger SNS notifications when thresholds are exceeded over specified time periods.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Rewriting application code is unnecessary when CloudWatch already handles log processing.\nB: Subscription filters don't support counting occurrences over time periods.\nC: Amazon Inspector is for security vulnerability assessment, not application error monitoring.\n\nTips:\nStreaming: Kinesis Data Streams khi cần tự xử lý/nhiều consumer; Firehose khi chỉ cần đổ dữ liệu vào S3/Redshift/OpenSearch (near real-time, không quản shard)."},
{"id":"q168","q":"A company has a development team that uses AWS CodeCommit for version control. The development team has CodeCommit repositories in multiple AWS accounts. The team is expanding to include developers who work in various locations. The company must ensure that the developers have secure access to the repositories. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","options":["Configure IAM roles for each developer and grant access individually.","Configure permission sets in AWS IAM Identity Center to grant access to the accounts.","Share AWS access keys with the development team for direct repository access.","Use public SSH keys for authentication to the CodeCommit repositories."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS IAM Identity Center (formerly AWS SSO) provides centralized access management across multiple AWS accounts. Permission sets can be configured once and applied consistently, making it the most operationally efficient solution for managing developer access across multiple accounts.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Configuring IAM roles individually for each developer across multiple accounts is operationally inefficient.\nC: Sharing access keys is insecure and difficult to manage.\nD: SSH keys don't provide centralized management across multiple accounts.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q169","q":"A company has built an AWS Lambda function to convert large image files into output files that can be used in a third-party viewer application. The company recently added a new module to the function to improve the output of the generated files. However, the new module has increased the bundle size and has increased the time that is needed to deploy changes to the function code. How can a developer increase the speed of the Lambda function deployment?","options":["Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the function code.","Use Lambda layers to package and load dependencies.","Increase the memory size of the function.","Use Amazon S3 to host the function dependencies."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Lambda layers allow separating dependencies from function code. When dependencies don't change, only the smaller function code needs to be deployed, significantly speeding up deployment times.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: CodeDeploy doesn't solve the large bundle size problem.\nC: Memory size affects execution performance, not deployment speed.\nD: S3 hosting doesn't help with Lambda deployment speed.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q170","q":"A developer creates a static website for their department. The developer deploys the static assets for the website to an Amazon S3 bucket and serves the assets with Amazon CloudFront. The developer uses origin access control (OAC) on the CloudFront distribution to access the S3 bucket. The developer notices users can access the root URL and specific pages but cannot access directories without specifying a file name. For example, /products/index.html works, but /products/ returns an error. The developer needs to enable accessing directories without specifying a file name without exposing the S3 bucket publicly. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Update the CloudFront distribution's settings to index.html as the default root object is set.","Update the Amazon S3 bucket settings and enable static website hosting. Specify index.html as the Index document. Update the S3 bucket policy to enable access. Update the CloudFront distribution's origin to use the S3 website endpoint.","Create a CloudFront function that examines the request URL and appends index.html when directories are being accessed. Add the function as a viewer request CloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution's behavior.","Create a custom error response on the CloudFront distribution with the HTTP error code set to the HTTP 404 Not Found response code and the response page path to /index.html. Set the HTTP response code to the HTTP 200 OK response code."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"A CloudFront function can modify requests at the edge to append 'index.html' to directory paths. This solves the problem without exposing the S3 bucket publicly and maintains OAC security.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Default root object only works for the root path, not subdirectories.\nB: Using the S3 website endpoint would bypass OAC and potentially expose the bucket.\nD: Custom error responses for 404 errors don't efficiently handle directory access patterns.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q171","q":"A developer is testing a RESTful application that is deployed by using Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. When the developer tests the user login by using credentials that are not valid, the developer receives an HTTP 405: METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED error. The developer has verified that the test is sending the correct request for the resource. Which HTTP error should the application return in response to the request?","options":["HTTP 401","HTTP 404","HTTP 503","HTTP 505"],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"HTTP 401 (Unauthorized) is the correct status code for authentication failures with invalid credentials, following REST API standards.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: 404 is for resources not found.\nC: 503 is for service unavailable.\nD: 505 is for HTTP version not supported.\n\nTips:\nAPI Gateway: HTTP API rẻ/nhanh cho proxy đơn giản; REST API cần usage plan, API key, request validation. Timeout cứng 29s — việc dài phải async."},
{"id":"q172","q":"A developer must use multi-factor authentication (MFA) to access data in an Amazon S3 bucket that is in another AWS account. Which AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) API operation should the developer use with the MFA information to meet this requirement?","options":["AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity","GetFederationToken","AssumeRoleWithSAML","AssumeRole"],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"AssumeRole is used for cross-account access and supports MFA authentication. It returns temporary credentials to access resources in another account.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity is for web identity federation.\nB: GetFederationToken is for temporary access within the same account.\nC: AssumeRoleWithSAML is for SAML-based federation.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q173","q":"A developer designed an application on an Amazon EC2 instance. The application makes API requests to objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. Which combination of steps will ensure that the application makes the API requests in the MOST secure manner? (Choose two.)","options":["Create an IAM user that has permissions to the S3 bucket. Add the user to an IAM group.","Create an IAM role that has permissions to the S3 bucket.","Add the IAM role to an instance profile. Attach the instance profile to the EC2 instance.","Create an IAM role that has permissions to the S3 bucket. Assign the role to an IAM group.","Store the credentials of the IAM user in the environment variables on the EC2 instance."],"correct":[1,2],"multi":true,"explanation":"B: Creating an IAM role with S3 permissions follows the principle of least privilege.\nC: Using an instance profile allows the EC2 instance to assume the role and get temporary credentials automatically, which is the most secure method.\n\nIncorrect:\nA, E: Using IAM users and storing credentials is insecure and violates AWS best practices.\nD: IAM roles cannot be assigned to IAM groups for EC2 instances.\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q174","q":"An AWS Lambda function requires read access to an Amazon S3 bucket and requires read/write access to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The correct IAM policy already exists. What is the MOST secure way to grant the Lambda function access to the S3 bucket and the DynamoDB table?","options":["Attach the existing IAM policy to the Lambda function.","Create an IAM role for the Lambda function. Attach the existing IAM policy to the role. Attach the role to the Lambda function.","Create an IAM user with programmatic access. Attach the existing IAM policy to the user. Add the user access key ID and secret access key as environment variables in the Lambda function.","Add the AWS account root user access key ID and secret access key as encrypted environment variables in the Lambda function."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"Using an IAM role with Lambda is the most secure method. The function automatically gets temporary credentials, and no long-term access keys are stored.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: IAM policies cannot be directly attached to Lambda functions.\nC: Storing access keys in environment variables is insecure.\nD: Using root user credentials is extremely insecure and violates AWS best practices.\n\nTips:\nGặp MOST/HIGHEST → ưu tiên phương án dùng IAM role + KMS + dịch vụ managed; loại phương án lưu credential trong code/S3/file."},
{"id":"q175","q":"A developer is using AWS Step Functions to automate a workflow. The workflow defines each step as an AWS Lambda function task. The developer notices that runs of the Step Functions state machine fail in the GetResource task with either an IllegalArgumentException error or a TooManyRequestsException error. The developer wants the state machine to stop running when the state machine encounters an IllegalArgumentException error. The state machine needs to retry the GetResource task one additional time after 10 seconds if the state machine encounters a TooManyRequestsException error. If the second attempt fails, the developer wants the state machine to stop running. How can the developer implement the Lambda retry functionality without adding unnecessary complexity to the state machine?","options":["Add a Delay task after the GetResource task. Add a catcher to the GetResource task. Configure the catcher with an error type of TooManyRequestsException. Configure the next step to be the Delay task. Configure the Delay task to wait for an interval of 10 seconds. Configure the next step to be the GetResource task.","Add a catcher to the GetResource task. Configure the catcher with an error type of TooManyRequestsException, an interval of 10 seconds, and a maximum attempts value of 1. Configure the next step to be the GetResource task.","Add a retrier to the GetResource task. Configure the retrier with an error type of TooManyRequestsException, an interval of 10 seconds, and a maximum attempts value of 1.","Duplicate the GetResource task. Rename the new GetResource task to TryAgain. Add a catcher to the original GetResource task. Configure the catcher with an error type of TooManyRequestsException. Configure the next step to be TryAgain."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Step Functions retriers are specifically designed for automatic retry logic. They can be configured with error types, intervals, and maximum attempts, adding minimal complexity.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Using Delay tasks and Catchers creates unnecessary complexity.\nB: Catchers are for error handling after retries fail, not for retry logic.\nD: Duplicating tasks creates maintenance overhead and complexity.\n\nTips:\nLỗi xử lý lặp lại → DLQ + maxReceiveCount. Lambda async tự retry 2 lần; muốn kiểm soát tốt hơn thì dùng on-failure destination. Luôn thiết kế idempotent."},
{"id":"q176","q":"A developer is creating a serverless application that uses an AWS Lambda function. The developer will use AWS CloudFormation to deploy the application. The application will write logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The developer has created a log group in a CloudFormation template for the application to use. The developer needs to modify the CloudFormation template to make the name of the log group available to the application at runtime. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options":["Use the AWS::Include transform in CloudFormation to provide the log group's name to the application.","Pass the log group's name to the application in the user data section of the CloudFormation template.","Use the CloudFormation template's Mappings section to specify the log group's name for the application.","Pass the log group's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) as an environment variable to the Lambda function."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"Environment variables are the standard way to pass configuration to Lambda functions at runtime. The ARN contains the log group name and can be easily accessed by the application.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: AWS::Include transform is for including external template snippets.\nB: User data is for EC2 instances, not Lambda functions.\nC: Mappings are for static values, not dynamic resource references.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q177","q":"A developer is creating an Amazon DynamoDB table by using the AWS CLI. The DynamoDB table must use server-side encryption with an AWS owned encryption key. How should the developer create the DynamoDB table to meet these requirements?","options":["Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. Provide the key's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) in the KMSMasterKeyId parameter during creation of the DynamoDB table.","Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) AWS managed key. Provide the key's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) in the KMSMasterKeyId parameter during creation of the DynamoDB table.","Create an AWS owned key. Provide the key's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) in the KMSMasterKeyId parameter during creation of the DynamoDB table.","Create the DynamoDB table with the default encryption options."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"DynamoDB uses AWS owned keys for server-side encryption by default. No additional parameters are needed.\n\nIncorrect:\nA, B, C: These options require specifying KMS keys, which are not AWS owned keys.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q178","q":"A company has an application that runs across multiple AWS Regions. The application is experiencing performance issues at irregular intervals. A developer must use AWS X-Ray to implement distributed tracing for the application to troubleshoot the root cause of the performance issues. What should the developer do to meet this requirement?","options":["Use the X-Ray console to add annotations for AWS services and user-defined services.","Use Region annotation that X-Ray adds automatically for AWS services. Add Region annotation for user-defined services.","Use the X-Ray daemon to add annotations for AWS services and user-defined services.","Use Region annotation that X-Ray adds automatically for user-defined services. Configure X-Ray to add Region annotation for AWS services."],"correct":[1],"multi":false,"explanation":"X-Ray automatically adds Region annotations for AWS services. For custom services, developers need to manually add Region annotations to track performance across regions.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Annotations are added in code, not in the console.\nC: The X-Ray daemon collects traces but doesn't add annotations.\nD: X-Ray doesn't automatically add Region annotations for user-defined services.\n\nTips:\nTrace phân tán → X-Ray; trên on-premises/server ngoài AWS cần chạy X-Ray daemon. Bật tracing ở MỌI service trong đường đi, nếu không trace sẽ đứt."},
{"id":"q179","q":"A company runs an application on AWS. The application uses an AWS Lambda function that is configured with an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue called high priority queue as the event source. A developer is updating the Lambda function with another SQS queue called low priority queue as the event source. The Lambda function must always read up to 10 simultaneous messages from the high priority queue before processing messages from low priority queue. The Lambda function must be limited to 100 simultaneous invocations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Set the event source mapping batch size to 10 for the high priority queue and to 90 for the low priority queue.","Set the delivery delay to 0 seconds for the high priority queue and to 10 seconds for the low priority queue.","Set the event source mapping maximum concurrency to 10 for the high priority queue and to 90 for the low priority queue.","Set the event source mapping batch window to 10 for the high priority queue and to 90 for the low priority queue."],"correct":[2],"multi":false,"explanation":"Event source mapping maximum concurrency controls how many concurrent invocations each queue can trigger. Setting 10 for high priority and 90 for low priority ensures high priority messages get processed first within the 100 total limit.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Batch size controls messages per invocation, not concurrency.\nB: Delivery delay affects when messages become available, not processing priority.\nD: Batch window controls how long to wait for batching, not concurrency.\n\nTips:\nĐọc kỹ từ khoá quyết định trong đề (LEAST/MOST/FEWEST, “real-time”, “cross-account”, “least operational overhead”) — chúng thường loại ngay 2 phương án. Loại phương án tự vận hành nhiều hơn nếu đề hỏi managed."},
{"id":"q180","q":"A data visualization company wants to strengthen the security of its core applications. The applications are deployed on AWS across its development, staging, pre-production, and production environments. The company needs to encrypt all of its stored sensitive credentials. The sensitive credentials need to be automatically rotated. A version of the sensitive credentials need to be stored for each environment. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","options":["Configure AWS Secrets Manager versions to store different copies of the same credentials across multiple environments.","Create a new parameter version in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store for each environment. Store the environment-specific credentials in the parameter version.","Configure the environment variables in the application code. Use different names for each environment type.","Configure AWS Secrets Manager to create a new secret for each environment type. Store the environment-specific credentials in the secret."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS Secrets Manager provides encryption, automatic rotation, and allows creating separate secrets for each environment. This is the most operationally efficient solution.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: Using versions for different environments is confusing and not the intended use of versions.\nB: Parameter Store doesn't support automatic rotation.\nC: Environment variables are insecure and don't support rotation.\n\nTips:\nAccess token / API key / password → AWS Secrets Manager (có rotation). Parameter Store chỉ khi đề nói rõ “ít tốn kém” hoặc “free tier”."},
{"id":"q181","q":"A developer is investigating an issue in part of a company's application. In the application, messages are sent to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. The AWS Lambda function polls messages from the SQS queue and sends email messages by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES). Users have been receiving duplicate email messages during periods of high traffic. Which reasons could explain the duplicate email messages? (Choose two.)","options":["Standard SQS queues support at-least-once message delivery.","Standard SQS queues support exactly-once processing, so the duplicate email messages are because of user error.","Amazon SES has the DomainKeys Identified Mail (DKIM) authentication incorrectly configured.","The SQS queue's visibility timeout is lower than or the same as the Lambda function's timeout.","The Amazon SES bounce rate metric is too high."],"correct":[0,3],"multi":true,"explanation":"A: Standard SQS queues guarantee at-least-once delivery, which can result in duplicate messages.\nD: If visibility timeout is too short, messages may become visible again before processing completes, causing reprocessing.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Standard SQS doesn't support exactly-once processing (only FIFO queues do).\nC: DKIM configuration affects email authentication, not duplication.\nE: High bounce rate doesn't cause email duplication.\n\nTips:\nMetric để alarm, Logs để điều tra. Muốn alarm theo nội dung log → tạo metric filter trước. Nhớ đặt retention cho log group để tránh phí."},
{"id":"q182","q":"A developer is deploying a company's application to Amazon EC2 instances. The application generates gigabytes of data files each day. The files are rarely accessed, but the files must be available to the application's users within minutes of a request during the first year of storage. The company must retain the files for 7 years. How can the developer implement the application to meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","options":["Store the files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use the S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval storage class. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition the files to the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class after 1 year.","Store the files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use the S3 Standard storage class. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition the files to the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval storage class after 1 year.","Store the files on an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Use Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to create snapshots of the EBS volumes and to store those snapshots in Amazon S3.","Store the files on an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) mount. Configure EFS lifecycle management to transition the files to the EFS Standard- Infrequent Access (Standard-IA) storage class after 1 year."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval provides millisecond access for rarely accessed data at low cost for the first year, then transitioning to Glacier Deep Archive provides the lowest cost for long-term retention (7 years).\n\nIncorrect:\nB: S3 Standard is too expensive for rarely accessed data, and Glacier Flexible Retrieval has slower retrieval times.\nC: EBS snapshots are not cost-effective for this data volume and access pattern.\nD: EFS is more expensive than S3 for this use case and doesn't support 7-year retention as effectively.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q183","q":"A company's developer has deployed an application in AWS by using AWS CloudFormation. The CloudFormation stack includes parameters in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store that the application uses as configuration settings. The application can modify the parameter values. When the developer updated the stack to create additional resources with tags, the developer noted that the parameter values were reset and that the values ignored the latest changes made by the application. The developer needs to change the way the company deploys the CloudFormation stack. The developer also needs to avoid resetting the parameter values outside the stack. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","options":["Modify the CloudFormation stack to set the deletion policy to Retain for the Parameter Store parameters.","Create an Amazon DynamoDB table as a resource in the CloudFormation stack to hold configuration data for the application. Migrate the parameters that the application is modifying from Parameter Store to the DynamoDB table.","Create an Amazon RDS DB instance as a resource in the CloudFormation stack. Create a table in the database for parameter configuration. Migrate the parameters that the application is modifying from Parameter Store to the configuration table.","Modify the CloudFormation stack policy to deny updates on Parameter Store parameters."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Setting deletion policy to Retain prevents CloudFormation from modifying or deleting the parameters during stack updates, preserving application-made changes with minimal effort.\n\nIncorrect:\nB, C: Migrating to DynamoDB or RDS requires significant code changes and development effort.\nD: Stack policies control stack-level operations, not specific resource updates.\n\nTips:\nCloudFormation: Parameters + AllowedValues để giới hạn lựa chọn; rollback tự động khi stack fail; change set để xem trước thay đổi. SAM = CloudFormation cho serverless."},
{"id":"q184","q":"A company has a social media application that receives large amounts of traffic. User posts and interactions are continuously updated in an Amazon RDS database. The data changes frequently, and the data types can be complex. The application must serve read requests with minimal latency. The application's current architecture struggles to deliver these rapid data updates efficiently. The company needs a solution to improve the application's performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Use Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) in front of the RDS database to provide a caching layer for the high volume of rapidly changing data.","Set up Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration on the RDS database to enhance the speed of data transfer from the databases to the application.","Add an Amazon CloudFront distribution in front of the RDS database to provide a caching layer for the high volume of rapidly changing data.","Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster. Update the application code to use a write-through caching strategy and read the data from Redis."],"correct":[3],"multi":false,"explanation":"ElastiCache for Redis provides an in-memory caching layer with write-through strategy, ensuring cached data stays current with RDS while providing fast read access for frequently changing data.\n\nIncorrect:\nA: DAX is for DynamoDB, not RDS.\nB: S3 Transfer Acceleration is for S3, not RDS.\nC: CloudFront is for static content caching, not dynamic database data.\n\nTips:\nDAX chỉ tăng tốc ĐỌC DynamoDB. ElastiCache cho cache tầng ứng dụng (Redis: persistence/pub-sub; Memcached: đơn giản, multi-thread)."},
{"id":"q185","q":"A developer created an AWS Lambda function that performs a series of operations that involve multiple AWS services. The function's duration time is higher than normal. To determine the cause of the issue, the developer must investigate traffic between the services without changing the function code. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Enable AWS X-Ray active tracing in the Lambda function. Review the logs in X-Ray.","Configure AWS CloudTrail. View the trail logs that are associated with the Lambda function.","Review the AWS Config logs in Amazon CloudWatch.","Review the Amazon CloudWatch logs that are associated with the Lambda function."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS X-Ray provides distributed tracing that shows the flow between services and identifies bottlenecks without code changes when active tracing is enabled.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: CloudTrail logs API calls but doesn't provide performance analysis.\nC: AWS Config is for resource configuration compliance, not performance.\nD: CloudWatch logs show function execution but not inter-service traffic details.\n\nTips:\nTrace phân tán → X-Ray; trên on-premises/server ngoài AWS cần chạy X-Ray daemon. Bật tracing ở MỌI service trong đường đi, nếu không trace sẽ đứt."},
{"id":"q186","q":"A company has on-premises data centers that run an image processing service. The service consists of containerized applications that run on Kubernetes clusters. All the applications have access to the same NFS share for files and data storage. The company is running out of NFS capacity in the data centers and needs to migrate to AWS as soon as possible. The Kubernetes clusters must be highly available on AWS. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options":["Transfer the information that is in the NFS share to an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Upload the container images to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR).","Transfer the information that is in the NFS share to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume. Upload the container images to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR).","Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster to run the applications. Configure each node of the cluster to mount the Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume at the required path for the container images.","Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to run the applications. Configure each node of the cluster to mount the Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume at the required path for the container images.","Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to run the applications. Configure each node of the cluster to mount the Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume at the required path for the container images."],"correct":[1,4],"multi":true,"explanation":"B: EFS provides shared file storage similar to NFS that can be accessed by multiple containers.\nE: EKS maintains Kubernetes compatibility and can mount EFS volumes for shared storage across nodes.\n\nIncorrect:\nA, D: EBS volumes cannot be shared across multiple nodes simultaneously.\nC: ECS would require changing from Kubernetes to a different orchestration platform.\n\nTips:\nContainer image → ECR; chạy container không muốn quản server → Fargate. Nếu đề nhắc Kubernetes API/manifest → EKS."},
{"id":"q187","q":"A company has an analytics application that uses an AWS Lambda function to process transaction data asynchronously. A developer notices that asynchronous invocations of the Lambda function sometimes fail. When failed Lambda function invocations occur, the developer wants to invoke a second Lambda function to handle errors and log details. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options":["Configure a Lambda function destination with a failure condition. Specify Lambda function as the destination type. Specify the error-handling Lambda function's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) as the resource.","Enable AWS X-Ray active tracing on the initial Lambda function. Configure X-Ray to capture stack traces of the failed invocations. Invoke the error-handling Lambda function by including the stack traces in the event object.","Configure a Lambda function trigger with a failure condition. Specify Lambda function as the destination type. Specify the error-handling Lambda function's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) as the resource.","Create a status check alarm on the initial Lambda function. Configure the alarm to invoke the error-handling Lambda function when the alarm is initiated. Ensure that the alarm passes the stack trace in the event object."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Lambda destinations can route failed asynchronous invocations to another Lambda function, SQS queue, SNS topic, or EventBridge event bus automatically.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: X-Ray is for tracing, not error handling.\nC: Lambda triggers are for event sources, not error destinations.\nD: CloudWatch alarms are for monitoring, not real-time error handling.\n\nTips:\nDecouple → SQS (queue, 1 consumer) hoặc SNS fan-out (nhiều subscriber). Cần filter nội dung phức tạp → EventBridge."},
{"id":"q188","q":"A company introduced a new feature that should be accessible to only a specific group of premium customers. A developer needs the ability to turn the feature on and off in response to performance and feedback. The developer needs a solution to validate and deploy these configurations quickly without causing any disruptions. What should the developer do to meet these requirements?","options":["Use AWS AppConfig to manage the feature configuration and to validate and deploy changes. Use feature flags to turn the feature on and off.","Use AWS Secrets Manager to securely manage and validate the feature configurations. Enable lifecycle rules to turn the feature on and off.","Use AWS Config to manage the feature configuration and validation. Set up AWS Config rules to turn the feature on and off based on predefined conditions.","Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to store and validate the configuration settings for the feature. Enable lifecycle rules to turn the feature on and off."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"AWS AppConfig is specifically designed for application configuration management with feature flags, validation, and controlled deployments.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Secrets Manager is for secrets, not feature configuration.\nC: AWS Config is for resource configuration compliance.\nD: Parameter Store lacks built-in validation and deployment features.\n\nTips:\nS3: lifecycle để chuyển storage class/xoá; versioning bảo vệ khỏi xoá nhầm; bucket policy cho cross-account; presigned URL cho truy cập tạm."},
{"id":"q189","q":"A developer needs approval from a product owner before the developer can deploy code for an application to production. The developer uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. The developer configures an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send notifications to the product owner. Which solution is the MOST operationally efficient way for the developer to receive approval from the product owner?","options":["Add a new stage to CodePipeline before the production deployment. Add a manual approval action to the new stage. Add a new notification rule in the pipeline settings. Specify manual approval as the event that initiates the notification. Specify the SNS topic's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) to notify the product owner.","Develop an AWS Step Functions state machine that sends a notification to the product owner and accepts an approval. Add a new stage to CodePipeline before the production deployment. Add the state machine as a Step Functions action to the new stage.","Add a manual approval action to the existing production deployment stage in CodePipeline. Specify the SNS topic's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) while configuring the new manual approval action.","Edit the settings in CodePipeline. Create a new notification rule. Specify manual approval as the event that initiates the notification. Create a new notification target. Specify the SNS topic to notify the product owner. Save the notification rule."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"CodePipeline's built-in manual approval action with notification rules provides the most operationally efficient way to implement approval workflows.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Step Functions adds unnecessary complexity.\nC: Adding approval to existing stage may disrupt the deployment flow.\nD: Notification rules alone don't create approval gates.\n\nTips:\nNhiều bước tuần tự + retry + xử lý lỗi từng bước → Step Functions (không nhồi hết vào 1 Lambda)."},
{"id":"q190","q":"A developer is building a serverless application on AWS for a workflow that processes high volumes of data. In the workflow, an AWS Step Functions state machine invokes several AWS Lambda functions. One of the Lambda functions occasionally fails because of timeout errors during periods of high demand. The developer must ensure that the workflow automatically retries the failed function invocation if a timeout error occurs. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options":["Add a Retry field in the Step Functions state machine definition. Configure the state machine with the maximum number of retry attempts and the timeout error type to retry on.","Add a Timeout field in the Step Functions state machine definition. Configure the state machine with the maximum number of retry attempts.","Add a Fail state to the Step Functions state machine definition. Configure the state machine with the maximum number of retry attempts.","Update the Step Functions state machine to pass the invocation request to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe a Lambda function to the SNS topic. Configure the Lambda function with the maximum number of retry attempts for a timeout error type."],"correct":[0],"multi":false,"explanation":"Step Functions Retry field allows configuring automatic retries for specific error types like timeout errors with configurable intervals and maximum attempts.\n\nIncorrect:\nB: Timeout field controls task timeout, not retry behavior.\nC: Fail state handles final failure, not retries.\nD: SNS adds unnecessary complexity for a built-in feature.\n\nTips:\nLỗi xử lý lặp lại → DLQ + maxReceiveCount. Lambda async tự retry 2 lần; muốn kiểm soát tốt hơn thì dùng on-failure destination. Luôn thiết kế idempotent."}];
